\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 We Refuse To Fight Wars That Matter; Trump Wasn't Afraid To Call Out Failed Foreign Adventures; Biden And Co. See Themselves as Citizens Of The World; Rep. \uc2 Mike Johnson\uc2  (R-LA) Interviewed On His Questions Of \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  During House Judiciary Committee Hearing; President Biden Gives Speech At \uc2 NATO\uc2  Meeting; Bud Light And \uc2 Disney\uc2  Recent Brand Damage Examined; Seattle Middle School Offers Gender Affirming Care To Students On School Grounds.\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Laura Ingraham \par \uc2 7,197 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 July 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Tickets are free. Go to Hannity.com. We have a live audience tomorrow. Please set your DVR 9 pm Eastern 6 pm Pacific so you never ever miss an episode of Hannity. But in the meantime let not your heart be troubled. Laura Ingraham, the Ingraham Angle starts right here, right now. Laura, hi.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Are we sad?\par \par \uc2 (AUDIENCE CHEERING AND APPLAUDING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How is everybody in the studio today? How are all of you?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way tomorrow night because we have what's called no toss Friday, tomorrow will be our last handoff.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What? I don't know if I can take this. I honestly, um --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You abandoned me. I just that's what I look at.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm very -- I'm very upset about this. But I'm also excited about my new time slot. But I'm very -- I'm very sad because I feel like there's a distance growing between us that I'm very, I'm not so comfortable with. So I'm just hoping that somehow, we'll be able to bridge that gap that is obviously impending.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Would you like me to find you a therapist?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. No, there are several existing in your audience right now. But, Sean --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: There is a doctor here tonight. You're right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, I understand that. I can't wait to see you in studio soon in New York.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And we love all of you in New York.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Have a great show.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And thank you so much, Sean, awesome show. Hi, I am Laura Ingraham. This is the Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. The war against common sense. That's the focus of tonight's Angle. Now you know that safety announcement that the airlines always make before you take off.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: If cabin pressure changes, oxygen masks will drop from the panel's above your seat, be sure to adjust your own mask before helping others.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, clearly that thinking doesn't apply to Biden's foreign policy crew. We all, you know, watch the White House do nothing as the war against America kills more than, what 100,000 every year, and the DHS knows who's responsible.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TYRONE DURHAM, ACTING DIRECTOR FOR THE NATIONAL STATE THREATS CENTER: China is the source of most of the precursor chemicals required for fentanyl production. A cartel associate brokers the sale and shipment of fentanyl precursor chemicals from China to clandestine labs in Mexico where the fentanyl is manufactured.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But despite this, the administration refuses to do what's necessary to stop the flow of drugs and their mules who are bringing them across at the border. But there are borders that our president is laser focused on enforcing the borders of another country just 5000 miles away.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATE OF AMERICA: We will not waver. We will not waver.\par \par \uc2 (CROWD CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I mean that. Our commitment to Ukraine will not weaken.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, we will not waver. Those are nice words. But the truth is presidents from Lyndon Johnson to \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2  have seen that the public eventually turns against endless ill-defined wars. Eventually, the people's patience runs out and the money dries up. Remember what happened in the 20 -- 2006 midterms, when voters began to develop a deepening and hardening opposition to the war in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 Now this sentiment only grew and two years later, it helped elect anti-war Democrat Barack Obama to the presidency. And then eight years later, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the presidency as the only GOP candidate to call out the decision making behind the Iraq War.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , 44TH U.S. PRESIDENT: Obviously, the war in Iraq was a big fat mistake. We should have never been in Iraq, we have destabilized the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But now years later, we seem to have forgotten what we should have learned long ago. While we don't have American soldiers of course, deployed in Ukraine, the American taxpayers are once again left holding the bag as ordinary people struggle to make ends meet here at home. Now, to date the tab is what about $115 billion and all we have to show for it is a depleted us munitions stockpile and major Ukrainian cities in ruin.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Mr. President, what sort of update did President Zelenskyy give you on how their counter offensive is going?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Well, I'm -- I'm not at liberty to give you the detail of that. But it's -- we talked at length about it with all his military people within there, and they're -- they're still optimistic, but they know it's a hard slog.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wait, a hard slog? Now, a few months ago, we were told the Ukrainian counter-offensive would break Putin's troops but now we're sending cluster bombs to help them break through? Hmm. Well, at this point, we've come to a parting of the ways, haven't we? Most of us, I think want our government to do what's best for America first. It usually ends up with peace through strength. But Biden and his donors view themselves first and foremost, as members of the global community.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: I believe one of our defining missions is to uphold the international rules-based order.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY BLINKEN\uc2 , SECRETARY OF STATE: Basic principles, basic rights and a rules-based international order.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: None of us could ignore the threat to the rules-based international order.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, and Biden is far more worried about offending \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  than he is about offending any of you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Are you to the will not follow -- The one thing Zelenskyy understands now is that whether or not he's in \uc2 NATO\uc2  now, it's not relevant, as long as he has the commitment.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, the administration caters to Zelenskyy and throws crumbs to the rest of us. So the question Republicans now have to confront is, why should we continue to tax hardworking Americans to try to protect freedom in Ukraine, when our own Treasury Department is working with the Chinese to undermine America?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANEL YELLEN, TREASURY SECRETARY: I've met with Premier Li, Vice Premier Hu, finance minister Liu, \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  head, Pan and other senior officials. These conversations were direct, substantive and productive.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Productive for whom? American factory workers? I don't think so. Now, Biden's donors and plenty of GOP senators are adamant though, that will not offend China, despite the fact that they're trying to undermine us in every continent. And yet, we're literally bowing down to them. Now, none of this makes any sense. 78 years after the end of World War II, for Americans to still be carrying the lion's share of the burden to defend Europe.\par \par \uc2 Now consider how many hours every single year our citizens work versus the citizens of other G7 countries work. Now in France, well, think about this, they work 1500 and so hours a year and Germany just 1340 hours per year, but here in America, we work 1810 hours every year. Now, how can these other countries afford to like have guaranteed weeks off every August? No. How do Europeans get away with paying less than 2 percent of their GDP on defense?\par \par \uc2 Well, I'll tell you why. Because we pay for 3 percent out of our G -- GDP for our military. Now, of course the Euro snobs were enraged remember when Trump called them all out for slacking on their military expenditures. But he was 100 percent right. How often is Biden, for instance, called Greg Abbott, the governor of Texas, who's clearly dealing with the worst of the border crisis and spoken at any time like this to him.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We're going to make sure that you get what you need. Thank you for what you're doing. And bad news for you is, we're not going anywhere. You're stuck with us.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, no wonder trust in government is at an all-time low. The great protectors of democracy have destroyed that trust. So how can we rebuild faith in the government that's supposed to be a government of the people by the people and for the people? Well, first, I think it's time for Americans to realize that we have to protect ourselves from the cartels. That means enforce the border. You know, all of this is a complete nightmare.\par \par \uc2 And second, forget de-risking from China, we need to decouple from China. Because a real superpower doesn't help make its top adversary stronger economically, it wants to defeat it. And third, isn't it time for Europe to be more self-reliant? It's time to end the freeloading era. And fourth, let's return the military to its original mission, defending what the American flag stands for, not the alp