But President but the Secretary Blinken had a great trip to China having way -- to go all the way across the southern two third -- Beijing -- from the Atlantic Ocean to the to the Indian Ocean, in Africa.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, they actually prefer that to a Democrat trying to justify the party's fringe race and gender obsession or defending his party's handling of the border. It's really indefensible. It's better to have the mumbling Biden. Certainly voters in places like Virginia or Georgia, they just want an economy that works for the middle class. They don't want lies about how Bidenomics is working.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Makes good sense Bidenomics, right. It kind of flows off the tongue really well. Certainly, it's a vision, right. It's a vision about growing the economy, from the middle out to bottom up.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's a vision with no results. Now, as bad as that was, it's still better than Joe trying to make the case that you're better off than you were when he took office.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Over the past two years, we've gotten an awful lot done together. We got locked on together. So let's keep it going. We got the most vibrant economy in the world right now in the world.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, no one believes this, which is why given the emergency the Democrats have now broken the glass and dragged Barack Obama out. According to Politico, Obama has been meeting with the next generation Democrats like AOC and Maxwell Frost. Obama even showed up for lunch at the White House today. And while it was closed to the press, we can only assume he got a hero's welcome, like last time. And anytime Barack and Joe are in the same room, you know what happens?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE AND CHEERING)\par \par