-- that the law is on our site here. We are confident in our legal authorities, and we've said over and over again. And as you all know, and I think I've said this before, the solicitor general made a compelling argument before the courts.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Carrie?\par \par \uc2 SEVERINO: I don't know if she watched the same argument I did. I think it is clear that this the student loan case, that Biden has no legal leg to stand on, that what he is doing is reaching out for one of the largest expenditures in American history with just unilaterally making this stuff up.\par \par \uc2 The challenge, I think, is going to be whether the court decides these are the right parties to bring the case. But whether it's this term and this case or maybe another case coming up next term or later, there's no question in my mind what he is doing is completely unconstitutional and violates the law.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Carrie, the decision, one of the decisions everyone is waiting for is this racial preferences case focusing on the rationale of diversity as the driving factor in upholding -- previously upholding Affirmative Action.\par \par \uc2 SEVERINO: I think that one is one I'm really looking forward to it, because I think we're going to get a great opportunity for the court to dismantle racial preferences in education and finally put this issue to rest, because the Constitution really requires that. I'm looking forward to hearing that case.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think the court on that likely will -- I shouldn't say. I don't want to --\par \par \uc2 SEVERINO: Don't jinx it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But you are pretty confident that the court is going to overturn the old rationale for keeping racial preferences.\par \par \uc2 SEVERINO: I'm pretty optimistic. It looks like the chief is probably going to write the opinion. And as he said before, the best way to stop discriminating on the basis of race is to stop discriminating on the basis of race. I think we need to do that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Carrie, great to see you, as always.\par \par \uc2 The affirmative vision for the GOP in 2024, my mini-Angle, yes, mini, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: With Biden's basement campaign sure to continue into 2024, Republicans have to do more than just poke fun at his declining ability or cognition and rail on about how bad things are in the country. We all know how bad things are in the country. We see what is happening with our very eyes.\par \par \uc2 Instead, conservatives need an affirmative plan for restoring America. How are we going to get from point a to b to c all the way to p, meaning prosperity again? Today we heard President Trump offer a clear plan for restoring America's exported strength, meaning American jobs.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: If India, China, or any other country hits us with a 100 percent or a 200 percent tax or tariff on American made goods, which they do, we will hit them with that same tariff or tax exactly the same right now.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It's called reciprocal. It is a reciprocal attachment. If they charge us, we will charge them. If they tariff us or tax us, we will tariff them or tax them.\par \par \uc2 We did great trade deals.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Also today, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , he offered his plan for clamping down on the border and illegal immigration. And yes, that plan includes the word that makes so many liberals go nuts -- "deportation."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS, (R) FLORIDA: It's going to be a national emergency on day one. This is going to be mobilizing all available assets on day one. We have a plan for all the different levers of authority that we have to be able to bring this to bear.\par \par \uc2 Florida has surged our maritime assets. We fill in the gaps. People that come on these boats are interdicted, turned over to the Coast Guard, and then they are deported back to Haiti or Cuba or wherever they came from.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That is music to my ears, and of course, this is a very close to Trump's approach.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: I will immediately terminate every open border policy of the Biden administration. We use all necessary state, local, federal, and military resources to carry out the largest domestic deportation operation of criminals.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Just criminals or everybody who crossed the border with fraudulent asylum claims?\par \par \uc2 Now, for years voters have been discouraged, increasingly, believing that Washington is just hopelessly corrupt. Politicians say one thing to win and then they get into office, and they do the opposite or nothing at all. So they say a pox on all their houses. I'm sick of politics. I don't want to talk about it anymore. I don't want to hear it anymore. And a lot of times I just say I can't blame them.\par \par \uc2 But going forward, Republicans have to avoid their own brand of what sometimes I see as a new victimology. So brush off the doomsdayer attitude. Stop with all that, because that doesn't bring anyone along to your side. Trump and DeSantis actually have plans to win, to change the status quo.\par \par \uc2 And of course, official Washington, we know it's corrupt. We know it needs reform desperately. But if it all starts to seem hopeless, you're just going to ensure that voters either stay home or pick maybe a protest candidate who probably can't win the general election. Right now, Trump's 30 points -- no, 38 points ahead of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in one national poll, and Trump is clipping Biden 44 to 41 in the new Morning Consult poll just out. At least at this point, even with some of his legal troubles, voters do not believe that there's anyone else who will fight for Americans as hard as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will.\par \par \uc2 And the good news is conservatives at the same time are getting traction all across the country. They are making headway on important issues. Don't lose sight of that. We are attracting more minority candidates and building out a true multiethnic coalition.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We see that prices are through the roof, and we want to know what people are going to do to help put that burden down.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The Democratic Party has changed a lot. We are for God, country, family, and hard work.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Where are the concerns that you have about immigration?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The fact of the matter is that we don't feel safe anymore.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And just look at how well \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  did among Latino voters in Florida. And the Democrats' grip on the Muslim-American vote seems to be slipping as well as we showed you a few segments ago with Muslim parents protesting the hypersexualized curricula in the D.C. area suburbs. They don't like it.\par \par \uc2 But more importantly, name one group of voters, young, old, black, white, who love these high prices that Biden promised would be transitory, or who love the massive influx of illegals, or who love the violent crime that is increased in parts of the country, or the fentanyl overdoses that plague this country. No one wants this.\par \par \uc2 But impatient and anxious voters, they don't want candidates who simply agree with them. Everyone is upset, right? They want leaders who have an actual plan for turning things around.\par \par \uc2 So it's time to return to the basics -- ending wasteful spending, protecting American jobs, and a return across the board to personal responsibility. The candidate who makes that case effectively and firmly, urgently, who is unafraid to take that message into unfriendly political territory, can and will win.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us tonight. Greg Gutfeld, he's next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020230628ej6r00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Sets Record Low For Vice President Net Favorability; President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Denies Speaking To \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  About China Deal; Left's Grocery Gripes: Shopper Triggered By Superabundance Of Food Items; Dumb Tourist! Italy Looking For Man Who Carved Names Into Colosseum; Unbroken Bonds Of Battle: Joey's New Book Available At Foxnewsbooks.com\b0\par\par\uc2 Dana Perino, Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters, Greg  Gutfeld \par \uc2 8,352 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: The Five\par \uc2 FOXFIV\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 LEE ABBAMONTE, TRAVEL EXPERT: You might want to wear like your jeans or your sweater or something like that to keep warm on the plane.\par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Yes, or go commando, that's an option but that's for another show.\par \par \uc2 ABBAMONTE: Even better, Neil.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Even better. All right, Lee, I better get out of here fast. That was a great job. Thank you for the tips. As always, Lee Abbamonte travel expert.\par \par \uc2 ABBAMONTE: Thanks, buddy.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Extraordinary. Here comes THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Hello, everyone. I'm Dana Perino along with Judge Jeanine Pirro, Jessica Tarlov, Jesse Watters and Greg Gutfeld. It's 5:00 in New York City and this is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 Check this out, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  breaking new barriers as vice president, just not the ones you'd hoped for. Harris just received the worst vice presidential ratings in NBC News polling history, just 32 percent of respondents held a positive view of the vice president. 49 percent said they held a negative opinion of her and that gives Kamala a net favorability rating of minus 17, I could do my own math.\par \par \uc2 If you stack that number up against previous VPs. The picture is not that pretty. \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  and \uc2 Al Gore\uc2  all seen as more favorable.\par \par \uc2 But Harris does have one public cheerleader, who's that?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I want to thank Kamala, who's there for every single important thing we do. And I'm not sure how we do it without her.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Rehabbing Kamala's image is a top priority for the White House and it better be. Biden's Chief of Staff praising her work and saying, "I think the enthusiasm and energy is palpable. We just need to make sure that we do a good job of exposing her to the American public".\par \par \uc2 But exposure may not be the problem.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANDY COHEN, BRAVO HOST: I'm going to tell you the banger of the summer, OK? That you need to play for your people, and they're going to love it. Everybody's going to go crazy.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I like it.\par \par \uc2 COHEN: Yes. This is the song of the summer, OK? You need to tell the DJ to have that going, OK?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: OK.\par \par \uc2 COHEN: All right. You ready to see Stonewall?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, you know, I don't know if more exposure is a good idea. Think about Biden.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Did you see? They're wearing the same suit.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: What was that about?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I don't know. And she was biting her lower lip, like a white guy dancing at a wedding. That is so uncomfortable and awkward to watch.\par \par \uc2 I mean, it's almost as awkward as when John Mayer was dating Taylor Swift.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: It's actually more awkward even now.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: But she is historical figures. She is, you know, obviously the first female vice president, first woman of color, and now the worst V.P. in history. And that's because of the first two -- the first two got her in but that didn't promise any competence or excellence.\par \par \uc2 All she had to do was tick those boxes. And unfortunately, she didn't deliver the rest, which is like 10 percent, just show up. Show up, do one thing a year, that's all you got to do. But she couldn't even do that.\par \par \uc2 So, that's what -- that's where they're at right now. They don't -- you know, she is kind of the current state of the Democratic Party. She is the hood ornament, you know, identity Trump's competence, and it never reflects it, you know, and they continually act like it's the 1850s or the 1950s.\par \par \uc2 I'm sorry, if you're -- if you're a black woman, and you got an education, you have the golden key that unlocks every door. And when you get inside, and you can achieve anything, that's on you.\par \par \uc2 By the way, did you see the other survey, Dana?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: What was that survey?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: This is amazing. Reuters found out that every single U.S. president including Barack Obama was the descendant of slave owners, except for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So, that means Obama has to pay reparations, but Trump doesn't.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: And there you have it. You know what, that's a good survey.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It is a good survey.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Very interesting.\par \par \uc2 Judge, one of the things that we get about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is about once a week, there's a story. Maybe it's every other week. But it is a lot that they are -- have a new plan and a new makeover and a new plan to rehab her reputation. And this is -- now we're 2-1/2 years into the administration and so far, not working.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: The amazing part of this is that never in history has a position of vice president but more important than it is now.\par \par \uc2 Should Biden be elected? He'll be 82 at the time he's sworn in. She is literally a heartbeat away from the presidency. And with this negative, what is it, 17 points, 39 percent had very negative feelings about her, like hated her. It's not just negative with the 49 -- 39, very negative.\par \par \uc2 She has an office with a toxic work environment. People are fighting with each other to get to the exit door. This is a woman who was in a position to make it easy for other women behind her to come forward and do the job where Americans can say, you know, a woman is capable of doing this.\par \par \uc2 If anything she has established that precedent that a woman is incapable of being vice president, and just look at her with respect to what she's done.\par \par \uc2 I mean, the root causes at the border and this nonsense that Joe's trying to sell us that I couldn't do it without Kamala.\par \par \uc2 I mean, who was he kidding? So, I guess the real question for them is, who do we let out, Joe? We don't know if he's going to fall or if he's going to stumble on his words, or Kamala who just laugh her way through the whole thing?\par \par \uc2 I don't know what she's giggling about. But I have a philosophy in life. And my philosophy is, if somebody's out there always giggling, they're a miserable person when you get to work for them.\par \par \uc2 And finally, let me just say about setting records. She -- do you remember when they came out, and she said, Joe, we did it, we did it when they won. It was so inauthentic, there was something about it that you just couldn't buy.\par \par \uc2 So, if they really want to show Kamala more, the problem is she's got nothing to tout. Maybe she'll talk about abortion, but they wanted to talk about infrastructure. I don't know if that's going to go so well.\par \par \uc2 But for a woman who had it handed to her on a silver platter, because she checked off all the boxes, for her to literally fail in this job is really a sad commentary on her abilities.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Abortion is certainly an issue that she is going to push forward on. But Jessica, will that be enough?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: It really depends who's running in 2024. This is all candidate based. And if it's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  versus \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I think it's going to be fine for the Democrats. We're an incredibly polarized country. I don't think anyone is ever going to have a landslide.\par \par \uc2 But when you look at all of the data, it suggests that Trump, if he's in the race, he makes it about Trump and people have very clear views about that. His diehard supporters you see him gaining, gaining, gaining in the primaries and falling, falling, falling in the general election and Biden picking up more independence, more suburban voters, people who could be swayed back by a more moderate Republican candidate potentially.\par \par \uc2 But this is -- and if you look at the NBC approval ratings, it's like a race to the bottom. So, Kamala's approval rating is higher than Nikki Haley's, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 's, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 's, Tim Scott's. All people who want to be the Republican candidate.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's net negative rating makes Kamala look like the most successful woman in history. It's negative 56, right?\par \par \uc2 So, this is the guy who seems to be sweeping the primary season with, you know, each new bit of information about another indictment coming in.\par \par \uc2 And last night, we all heard audio of him showing people a classified document, he lied to Bret Baier, right? He said there was no document. We heard shuffling of papers, and he sounds like a teenager.\par \par \uc2 Hey, guys, isn't this cool? Look what I got. Talking about the nation's secrets, not a personal thing.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: What about her though? Like, --\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: It's obvious, she doesn't resonate with the American public, that it's not -- whatever is happening right now is not working. I don't know if showing her off more makes a difference. But it all comes down to what are the names going to be on the top of the ballot?\par \par \uc2 And if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the name under the R, I don't know if talking about the net negatives that Kamala has makes any difference.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: (INAUDIBLE) is that the thing, Jessica?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Obviously his family was slow to a good business deal or something, right?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Well, I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  might be more popular if the Department of Justice wasn't leaking evidence in the middle of a criminal investigation.\par \par \uc2 Just think about all of the terrible things though, that the media can make popular. Disco, Don Lemon, margarine.\par \par \uc2 You remember they had people out there that used to chant save the whales, save the whales, but now the windmills are murdering all the whales and they're like, oh, you know what? They had it coming.\par \par \uc2 You don't understand what's going on, the media can market anything except \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and they have tried and tried and tried.\par \par \uc2 Jessica, cigarettes kill people. And cigarettes are more popular than \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . They tried to melon scoop this woman out of the ticket a couple of months ago, and they couldn't pull it off.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Who would try to melon scoop her out?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: They covered it on the show, Jessica.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That was the greatest verb, melon scoop.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Well, it had to be delicate. And why did why did Biden run? He said he was going to be a bridge to the new generation. Well, that bridge is blown to smithereens because the woman fails under pressure. And now he's stuck with someone is about as popular as toxic waste.\par \par \uc2 Would you fly an airplane if the pilot was old and rickety, and the copilot couldn't land it? You'd not fly the plane, you drive.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley hit that right on the head the other day when she said that we're not running against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , we're running against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And that sent the White House into a panic mode.\par \par \uc2 And so, what they're trying to do is now every answer out of this woman's mouth is abortion. They'll ask her about infrastructure, it's abortion, abortion, abortion. That's all you're going to hear.\par \par \uc2 But I'm waiting for one thing. I'm waiting for reporters to ask \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  about her boss extorting foreign nations for cash bribes.\par \par \uc2 What she says there will tell you everything about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And that's what I'm waiting for.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: You might have to wait a long time because I don't think one of those interviews is going to happen. But the Andy Cohen interview, that will happen. Next time, you could wear something different.\par \par \uc2 All right, coming up who is telling the truth? President Biden denying that he ever talked business with Hunter despite a whistleblower saying otherwise.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: The big guy is giving a big denial despite an \uc2 IRS\uc2  whistleblower providing a text message that points to dad being in the room while Hunter was shaking down a Chinese businessman. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is still denying that it ever happened.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Mr. President, did you lie about never speaking with Hunter about his business deals? Did you lie about never speaking with Hunter about his business deals, sir?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: No.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Have you spoken with Hunter -- have you ever spoken with Hunter?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: And "The View" thinks we're all just misinterpreting the Hunter scandal.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANA NAVARRO, ABC "THE VIEW" HOST: The Hunter Biden story, the scandal, the this, the that, it's also the story of a father's love. And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has never and will never give up on his son Hunter, and will never treat him lesser than, and so he is a father first, take it or leave it.\par \par \uc2 SUNNY HOSTIN, ABC "THE VIEW" HOST: He's an addict. He's had this addiction for many years and to various things. And I wonder where our compassion is.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That's very touching, Dana. Usually, "The View" only cries when the greenroom runs out of krill.\par \par \uc2 So, do they have a point? Are they doing that thing where they're using the addiction as like a protection against any criticism?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, if you've noticed in the last 48 hours is when this line about Hunter's addiction has come back into fashion. What happens? You know how there's that Democratic bat signal that goes out. It's like, OK, now that he's pled guilty to these two misdemeanors, and everybody deploy the addiction defense.\par \par \uc2 When was the last time you heard that? We talked about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  all the time, I get asked about it often. And it is true, yes, he was an addict. It also is true that it is just impossible to believe and maybe not believable, that a father of a son who he loves so much, a son who was addicted would not ask his son, how are you doing? What are you doing today? What's your purpose in life today? What are you getting up to do? How the hell are you making all this money and stop using my name to get it?\par \par \uc2 Like, some sort of -- what kind of a father doesn't ask, where's the tough love? I have some friends who have been through this with their children. And it is a heart wrenching thing. Sometimes the tough love is just got to be the hardest part of it, the worry, all of that.\par \par \uc2 But there are also consequences. I would think that everyone should take a look, there's many things written about this. But Byron York at the Washington Examiner has done a really good, interesting piece about whistleblower number two, because it is curious, if this goes all the way back to 2014 and 2015 and he wasn't paying taxes then.\par \par \uc2 But he only has to deal with the tax misdemeanors from 2018 and 2019. No one in America would get that deal, except for somebody like \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . So, there does seem to be something there.\par \par \uc2 And I know the White House would love to say case closed. This is over. And a father loves his son, but it is just not going to cut it.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No. And you know, Judge, what gets me about that excuse is that, you know, it could be a real excuse. But we know it's not because clearly Hunter is incredibly competent at raising money.\par \par \uc2 You can't be 