uation when you look at Social Security and Medicare. But if you even raise this idea of maybe means testing, you know, if someone's very wealthy, maybe they don't need the Social Security test. Or maybe they should raise the age a little bit.\par \par \uc2 Let me ask both Amanda and Jeffrey. Are you open to the idea of making adjustments to these benefits so that they last longer for the rest of the country?\par \par \uc2 AMANDA HAMBRICK ASHCRAFT, NEW YORK DEMOCRAT: I have a question for Mr. Christie as a fellow parent of four.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: OK.\par \par \uc2 HAMBRICK ASHCRAFT: I like you and your campaign, you know, hope to tell my children the truth about all things --\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HAMBRICK ASHCRAFT: -- that they -- but more importantly, all children can survive and thrive. To that end, I'm so interested in knowing what legislation you would hope to pass that could curb the rising gun violence in this country, climate catastrophe and poverty. And that would protect the teaching of racial education in public schools, our LGBTQ+ siblings, and access to abortion care. You can choose any of those that you wanted. As a fellow parent, those are the issues that are really close to my heart.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Amanda is a registered Democrat, and then we have two, we have undecided Republican and sort of undecided Republican.\par \par \uc2 ALBANO: Strong Republican.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: OK. Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE: All right. So let's deal with a few of those issues as quickly as we can even though --\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: We'll keep talking.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE: They're really complicated and really emotional, right? Look, when you talk about new gun laws, you look at this Hunter Biden case today.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE: That's a gun law that was on the books. That if you are a drug user or drug abuser, you're not allowed to apply for a gun permit. Now that law seems to make 