rritories. God help us.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, God help us is right.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary is reveling in her status, her historic status.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: This is a historic administration. I am a history figure and I certainly walk in history every day. But this is also a historic making administration because of this president.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes. It's historic the way the Hindenburg and the Titanic were historic, Judge. Anything is historic if you frame is properly. We are historic. It's the first time we are together at 10:40 on Juneteenth. But the Biden historical society never ends. KJP is not the only historic figure there.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The second gentleman tells bad jokes, and we're going to do it in here.\par \par \uc2 Why did the political report go to the gym so often? For the daily spin class.\par \par \uc2 I got laughs.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: That's clever.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: He sounds like his wife.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: These two better stick to being historical, because hysterical they ain't, I can tell you.\par \par \uc2 Before we go, Judge, I have to update you on your favorite royals, Harry and Meghan. I know you follow their every exploit. They lost that $20 million \uc2 Spotify\uc2  deal. Bill Simmons, who is a \uc2 Spotify\uc2  executive, put it this way.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL SIMMONS, "THE BILL SIMMONS PODCAST": I wish I had been involved in the Meghan and Harry Spotify negotiation. They are grifters. That's the podcast we should have launched with them.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Judge, Meghan didn't even do her own podcasts. Her staff would reportedly interview the people she invited on and she would overdub the questions later. We need to sign up for that gig. That would be like you get your assistant to do the interview and then you just fake the questions later. There are a couple of words for that. "Fraudulence" is one. The other could be called the "Sussex Solution."\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know what's crazy about it, now they say that she -- there are reports that she may be the model for Dior. I don't know where they get this. That though Dior shot down those rumors tonight. Listen, I don't know if Dior listen to me, but I buy Dior sometimes. I think it's very important they know that is not making sense to me.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Dior was trying to do a deal with both Harry and Meghan. And look, this is a bit of a pity. I'm sorry they're not doing it, Judge, because who better than \uc2 Meghan Markle\uc2  to front a perfume like poison? Come one.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's good.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: And maybe the two of them could have launched their own new fragrance, lazy and entitled. It smells like old cash with a hint of Oprah. Might be appealing to some.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: That's very good. I'll tell you the two of them. I don't think they figured out what it is they need to do, other than hate the royals. And every time I look at Kate, she looks so perfect. Everything about her is perfect. And I think this one is just dying that she is not over there. But they could have stayed and they made a choice not to.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You can't gripe about the relatives and that be your whole brand. People get tired of it. And after that, they say, OK, what are you going to do now? The answer for these two, not much.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You've got to give them credit. How do you make $20 million, they call them grifters, on a podcast that you only do 12 on? I don't even want to divide that up.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's unbelievable. My gosh, you do more shows than that in two weeks, Judge. Give me a break.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's unbelievable.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Raymond, we love you. Take care.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Love you, too, Judge. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, a jarring attack on pro-life advocates caught on tape. The video in moments. Plus, another medical association prioritizing race over health. My friend Dr. Marc Siegel responds next. Stay right there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Disturbing new video was just released of the brutal attack on two elderly pro-life advocates outside of a Baltimore Planned Parenthood. FOX News senior national correspondent Kevin Corke joins me from our D.C. Newsroom with all the details. Kevin?\par \par \uc2 KEVIN CORKE, FOX NEWS WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Evening, Judge. Weeks on the victims are still recovering tonight. Meanwhile the search for their attacker is also ongoing. Two pro-life activists standing outside of a Planned Parenthood in Baltimore nearly three weeks ago brutally attacked by a man who apparently opposed their stance on abortion. Tonight Baltimore police are asking for the public's help to find the attacker. The victims targeted outside the facility on North Howard Street and have been identified as Dick Schaefer and Mark Crosby, 80 and 73 years olds respectively.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I am still blind in this one eye. This eyeball is bleeding. The orbital shelf area is all cracked and fractured. I need surgery there.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CORKE: Just vicious. Meantime, Jay Walton, president of the Baltimore County Right to Life chapter wrote on a \uc2 GoFundMe\uc2  page, "For years Mark has prayer in front of the Planned Parenthood in Baltimore city to let the scared, young abortion minded women know that they're loved, that their baby is loved."\par \par \uc2 As for the suspect, according to police, he was last seen on security cameras several blocks away wearing a gray t-shirt, blue jeans, brown shoes, and a full beard. Somehow he has still managed to evade justice, at least so far. Tonight, there is a $2,000 reward being offered for information leading to his arrest, and anyone with information is asked to call Baltimore police, 410-396-2411, or your local metro crime stoppers in that particular circumstance in Baltimore. It is 866-7-lockup. Judge?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Kevin, that's horrific. Thank you so much for reporting on that important story.\par \par \uc2 CORKE: You bet.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And you know what my fear is, if they do get them that they might be let out right away with this cashless bail nonsense.\par \par \uc2 CORKE: Yes. Let's get him first.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Absolutely. I'm with you. Thank you, Kevin.\par \par \uc2 And now it's time for -\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: When everything is racist.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I guess "When everything is racist." The \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  is now telling doctors to stop using the body mass index as a primary measurement for bodyweight because, shock, of course, it's racist. They say it has a history of harm and racial exclusion, and that BMI cutoffs are based primarily on data collected from previous generations of non-Hispanic white populations and does not consider a person's gender or ethnicity.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is my good friend and doctor, Dr. Marc Siegel, clinical professor of medicine at NYU Langone, FOX News Medical News contributor. What is your reaction to the roots of BMI being racist?\par \par \uc2 DR. MARC SIEGEL, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: That's hooey. Listen, I didn't believe that the AMA was going to get involved in cancel culture, but now they are cancelling the body mass index which is the thing I look at to at least start me off in the direction of obesity. And by the way, even obesity is under attack.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: So what are they saying --\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: Everyone is saying body positivity, you've got to accept yourself the way you are. Except for one thing, Judge. These things lead to bad health outcomes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, but wait a minute, so they're saying, what is it, like 20 percent of fat is good or bad, or 80 percent? What is the danger zone?\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: They are not saying that. They are saying that different ethnicities distribute their fat differently and that what you have really got to worry about is visceral fat, fat in the abdomen. OK, that's correct. And that's what I do in the office. But the first thing I need is a basic guideline to let me know that somebody is in a category that I need to look further. It's not racist. It's called good medicine.\par \par \uc2 And the AMA has a history, lately, of getting involved in politics. This is politics. This is not medicine. Again, this is fueled by the body positivity group that says accept yourself as you are. But I as an internist want people to lose weight. OK, I can get a microscope going and figure out where its distributed. I can use a magnifying glass and say, wait a minute, it's in an OK region where it's brown fat. But that's not how I do it. I want an overall indication. If you're in a group I've got to worry about, I'm worried about diabetes, I'm worried about heart disease, I'm worried about cancer, I worry about high blood pressure. I want you to lose weight.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But the truth is that --\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: Not you.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No, but the truth is you can't lose weight in a certain area. When you lose weight, you lose it in your whole body. So they are saying fat in some areas in some people is good? But it's got to be the overall index that makes sense.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: Exactly. I'll tell you the one tiny area they are right about, and we do this automatically. It's going to seem so foolish. I once compared myself to a boxer. I said that Boxer is the same BMI as me. I must be in great shape. But then I realized the boxer was all muscle. So muscle is heavier than fat. And I can size a person up in five seconds and say, wow, you are working out. You've got big pecs. I don't have to worry as much about your overall weight. I do that. I don't need a guideline. I don't need somebody taking a tool out of my toolbox. That's what they're doing here.\par \par \uc2 By the way, we don't have enough attention paid to obesity, period. We are moving in the wrong director here.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Let me ask you this.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: We've got to get insurance to pay for treatments for obesity. Instead with the AMA talking like this, we're not going to even have that. We don't have enough prevention as it is, and they're moving away from prevention.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, so you give everybody Ozempic and call it a day?\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: I give everybody a treadmill and call it a day.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: Everyone get off their duff now with the pandemic over. Everyone improve their diet. Every eat olives. Everyone, Mediterranean diet.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Are olives good for you?\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: You of all people asking.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I'm on a Mediterranean diet, but I just don't know if it's good for me.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: Of course. Berries, fruit, fish, olives, all really, really good for you.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. No Ozempic, huh? I hear it stops you from smoking now, and that if you drink a lot, it will stop you from drinking.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: It has uses. I'm not against it. I'm for it for certain people. If it gets their weight down and gets their blood pressure down and their healthier, yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But then I hear you have Ozempic face where your face falls.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: You're not getting that.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I'm not getting it. I don't want it.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: But look the overall thing is the AMA here is being political. Let's stop our medical organizations from being so political.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Why should they be any different? The government is political. Everything is political. Of course. Look at magazines now.\par \par \uc2 We have to go now. Dr. Siegel, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 SIEGEL: Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: The most awkward moment on TV today, shockingly, did not come from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The Last Bite sprains.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Don't consider taking off work on Juneteenth because it won't go unnoticed.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Happy Juneteenth to you. Is it lost on anybody that the only white guy at the table is off today to celebrate Juneteenth, and we are still here. Glad to be here.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We are glad to be here.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I hope Tony is enjoying his Juneteenth holiday.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Oh, boy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right, Gayle, because that's the only reason why anyone is allowed to be off today.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us tonight. I'm Judge Jeanine Pirro in for Laura Ingraham. Make sure to watch every weekday at 5:00 p.m. You can catch me co-hosting "THE FIVE."\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020230620ej6j00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Iowa Town Hall with \uc2 Donald Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity \par \uc2 9,435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity."\par \par \uc2 And, tonight, we are in beautiful Clive, Iowa, right outside of Des Moines. We have a massive, incredible, enthusiastic audience tonight.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, in a few short moments, well, the very first 2024 presidential caucus will take place right here in Iowa, unlike the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 But in just a moment, the leading presidential candidate for the Republicans, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , will be with us for the full hour.\par \par \uc2 By the way, unlike fake news CNN, it's not my job to sit here and debate the candidate. We're going to ask him about the issues of the day that actually matter to the people that came out here tonight in the rain and thunder and lightning, the voters, and they will also have their questions as well. Nothing is off the table.\par \par \uc2 And, as of now, Trump is not only beating his Republican rivals, but he's also beating President Biden.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: RealClearPolitics average, Trump is up in a head-to-head matchup there. And the most recent Harvard/Harris poll has him up by seven points over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of Americans, including Democrats, they're not happy with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . I don't think many Americans are happy with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , to say the least. And based on recent polls, voters believe that Biden is corrupt, incompetent, creepy, both mentally, physically, cognitively unfit to serve.\par \par \uc2 By the way, today was no exception. At the \uc2 Air Force Academy\uc2 , Biden could not remember the word pilot or fighter pilot. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: By the way, I met with the -- who are those guys that fly over shortly? You've heard of them, haven't you? Three of them are women.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: So don't screw around, guys.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, it got much worse from there.\par \par \uc2 And, by the way, viewer warning: This is kind of hard to watch. But following those remarks, well, Biden fell flat on his face and took another tumble and fall. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Wing, ten-hut. Mr. President, thank you for joining us today.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, we all hope the president is OK, but there needs to be a serious discussion in this country about his physical fitness, his mental acumen, his ability to serve.\par \par \uc2 The presidency is the toughest job on Earth. It requires, well, a tough, capable leader. And you might recall, 2024 -- and we talked about this in past election years -- the American people, they will now have a critical opportunity to right the ship. That begins right here in the great state of Iowa.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's give a warm Iowa welcome.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Joining us now for the hour, the 45th president of the United States, current GOP presidential candidate, front-runner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Hi.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: Trump! Trump! Trump! Trump!\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's a nice group. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: Trump! Trump! Trump! Trump!\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: USA!\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Oh.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: USA! USA! USA! USA! USA!\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Oh.\par \par \uc2 AUDIENCE: USA! USA!\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Whoa.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, they all came out. It was raining cats and dogs today.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 It was a little nasty out, but it's Iowa. It's a beautiful place. When it rains, it's beautiful.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We love you!\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We have been -- we have really been loved in Iowa. And I love Iowa. We won both times by a lot.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So, we're very happy.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We're very happy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're up in the polls here.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I want to start with the current president. Did you see the video of when he fell?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And did you see the video? He actually said, by the way, I met with -- who are those guys that are going to fly over shortly?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes. That's your president right now.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It was not too good.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It's sad. It's sad.\par \par \uc2 It's not -- it's -- they're representing -- we are all representing the country. You become president, and you're sort of not allowed to do that. But it's happened. It's happened, and it's happened pretty badly.\par \par \uc2 We won't go into it, but we all know the ones. And they count those acts. You know, they never forget. But that was a bad fall.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I remember they made -- remember the media made so much. You -- I think you were at West Point at the time.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And you were coming down a ramp.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It didn't have a rail. You had dress shoes on, like you have now...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... which have very slippery soles.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's correct. They look a little better, but you better not walk in rain. That's true.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes, especially downhill on a ramp.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : You know, it was very interesting.\par \par \uc2 I think I made my best speech. That was my best speech, and I was so proud of it.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It was pouring. It was pouring.\par \par \uc2 And I said, this speech was so good. And then I said: "How do I get down?"\par \par \uc2 "Sir, you have to go down the ramp."\par \par \uc2 I said: "The same when I came up?" It was a long -- like an ice skating rink. And they said: "Yes, sir."\par \par \uc2 And I had the general next to me, the commandant of cadets, nice guy, big guy, strong guy. I said: "General" -- and he's wearing combat boots. They don't slip too much.\par \par \uc2 I said: "General, get ready, because I may have to grab you here." But I said: "I'm not falling. There's no way."\par \par \uc2 So I'd go tippy-toe down the thing.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That was a mistake, because it didn't look so good. I even agree it was -- but I got killed. And they never covered that speech. I said, it was my best.\par \par \uc2 Someday, they will -- in 100 years, they're going to put that speech on. I really -- but you can't fall. You just can't fall, no matter what. Just can't allow it to happen. And I better not allow -- especially after saying this, I better not allow it to happen with me.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But things like that do happen.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, in past interviews that we have had together -- and we have had many over the years.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have asked you repeatedly about what you think about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's cognitive state. I have asked you about, is he up to the job physically, mentally?\par \par \uc2 You have been very reluctant to go there. I'm not reluctant. To me...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Does everyone agree with me that this guy is cognitively not there?\par \par \uc2 I doubt he knows what day of the week it is today. That's how -- that's how bad I think it's gotten for him. Why are you reluctant to call that out?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, I don't know if I'm supposed to say this. I actually called Sean and I asked Sean not to joke about it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I was joking about it.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Because he used to joke about it.\par \par \uc2 And I said: "Honestly, I don't think it looks good for you or for anybody for you to joke about it, because it's a serious problem."\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I was talking about sippy cup and warm milky at night and bedtime stories.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So I said: "I just don't think it's good for anybody, and it's not appropriate. You can speak about it if you want, but you -- I don't think you should joke about it."\par \par \uc2 And you really didn't after that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, now I realize how serious it is, I mean, especially -- and we will get into foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 And with China, Russia, and Iran forming, I'm calling it a new axis of evil.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I am very, very concerned that he's abdicated our role on the world stage.\par \par \uc2 Let me start...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I do say this. I think it's the most serious time and the most dangerous time right now in the history of our country. We have nuclear weapons on lots of different areas.\par \par \uc2 We have Russia. We have North Korea. We have -- Iran is going to soon have one. That should have never happened. I had that set up. We would have made that deal within a week after the election, and they would have never had a nuclear weapon. But nobody picked it up, because I terminated the Iran nuclear deal.\par \par \uc2 But this is the most dangerous time in the history of our country because of the power of the weaponry. And we have somebody that doesn't understand what's happening. And it's a very dangerous thing. It's a very bad thing, I mean, some really bad things.\par \par \uc2 If you would see -- and I got to see it -- if you would see the power of what we're talking about, this isn't army tanks going back and forth shooting at each other. This is something that's a whole different place. This is annihilation of the world, literally. The power is so, so horrible.\par \par \uc2 And I was actually working on something with Putin where we start getting rid of nuclear weapons. It's just too powerful. And all of a sudden, people are talking about nuclear weapons all the time. I wouldn't let people talk about it. I had somebody come down from MIT. I was talking about that.\par \par \uc2 My uncle was a great professor for many years at MIT. And I had somebody come down, and I say: "What would you say, like, during the debate about nuclear weapons?"\par \par \uc2 He looked at me, said: "Sir, don't talk about them."\par \par \uc2 I said: "Why?"\par \par \uc2 He said: "There's nothing you can say. It's so powerful. It's so extraordinary. The best thing you can do is not talk about them."\par \par \uc2 Now they're talking about them all the time. That's all they talk about. In fact, I guess Putin announced the other day he's moving nuclear weapons to Belarus. So, this is a very dangerous time for our country, but it's a very dangerous time for the whole world.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You end your rally speeches now with music in the background, and you start with: "We are a nation in decline."\par \par \uc2 And this -- this is a very different America than what it was when you left it as president 2.5 years ago.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I can point to the border. I can look at laws all over the country, defund, dismantle, no-bail laws.\par \par \uc2 We have given up energy independence. We're importing oil from Venezuela and OPEC and the...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Who would have believed that?\par \par \uc2 And we now see two-thirds of our country are living paycheck to paycheck. You see some people now cashing in their retirement just so they can make ends meet. Others are putting bare necessities on credit cards. I will mention this in Iowa, because I have a radio show at 720 stations.\par \par \uc2 Farmers call me. The cost of fertilizer is three times what it used to be. The cost of seed is twice what it used to be. And if you can get the parts to repair your equipment, it's four times what it used to be. I -- how -- I have never seen it this bad or this -- decline this precipitously.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So we were energy-independent, think of it, three years ago.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And...\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And what people -- what people don't know is that we have, I call it liquid gold, because it's gold. It's better than gold.\par \par \uc2 We have liquid gold under our feet, more than any other nation, more than Saudi Arabia, more than Russia. We were energy-independent. Within six months, we would have been energy-dominant. And we were going to sell energy to Europe and lots of other places. And we were going to make so much money doing it, because it's such a big world.\par \par \uc2 It's such a big business. It's all-encompassing. And that's what started the inflation, I mean, the energy. We stopped drilling, and, all of a sudden, gasoline is going up to $5, $6 a gallon in a car, for a car. And just horrible things were happening.\par \par \uc2 And it happened.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But we were going to pay off debt. We were going to reduce taxes further. We gave you the biggest tax cut in the history of our country, bigger than the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  tax cut and the biggest...\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And, you know, I think, more importantly, Sean, we gave you the biggest regulation cuts. That's why we had more jobs than we ever had before.\par \par \uc2 We have never had anything close. And we did all of that. And then to end that, but we were going to pay off debt. We were going to get the debt, because the money is so big, it's so massive. You look at Saudi Arabia, the money they have, no nation has ever had anything like it, and we have more than they have. We were going to pay off debt.\par \par \uc2 We were going to get the energy prices down. We were going to get interest rates down. It was like we had something going that -- and, within six months, we would have been dominant, because we would have taken over Europe. We would have literally been supplying the energy to Europe. And we would have made a fortune. We would have paid down the debt.\par \par \uc2 We would have cut the taxes. It was going to be so beautiful.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me focus on the issues that I think, bread-and-butter issues, that impact everybody.\par \par \uc2 I want to know, if you get elected president, how fast are you going to be able to fix our borders, bring us back to energy independence, how quickly you might be able to work to change the school system, bring back law and order and safety and security to this country in every town and every city, because I think people need that if they want to pursue happiness.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How quickly can you -- can you shift gears and move this country?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right. I think very quickly.\par \par \uc2 And let me -- let me just say, so I heard DeSanctis saying: Oh, well, I get eight years. I get eight years. He gets four.\par \par \uc2 You don't need four, and you don't need eight. You need six months. Within six months, I said...\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Within six months, this can be done.\par \par \uc2 Other than -- other than -- you don't need eight years. And, frankly, I wouldn't vote for him because he said, you need eight years. You need six months.\par \par \uc2 We're going to drill. We're going to get our energy down.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : When the energy comes down, other things come down. And we're going to take care of things.\par \par \uc2 We're going to immediately close up the border. We had the greatest border. We had the safest border in the history of our country. Now we have the worst border in the history of the world. There's no -- and I say this during rallies. We love our rallies.\par \par \uc2 But I say that there's never been a Third World country that allowed people to pour into it. They'd stand there with sticks and stones if they had to. What's happening to our country -- but in terms of doing it, you don't need eight years, and you don't need four years.\par \par \uc2 We can have a lot of it done, because these guys are amazing. The oil guys, they will be -- in fact, I had it so low that we had to raise it, or they would have all been out of business. We had so much oil, we didn't know what to do with it. We bought a lot of it for very little for the Strategic National Reserve...\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... that he then took to keep the prices down before an election.\par \par \uc2 We had the Strategic National Reserves almost full, and then Biden came along and took it to keep prices down. It's called artificially down. And the thing is almost empty now, and that's meant for times of war. It's not meant to keep a price down for an automobile. It's meant for war, for real problems.\par \par \uc2 And we had it 75 -- think of it -- 75 million barrels. And I bought it for peanuts. And Congress, I had to fight Congress, and the pricing was so crazy and so good. And we needed a place because we had so much.\par \par \uc2 So, we started filling it up. This guy comes along and he takes it, for automobiles -- for people, so they -- before the election, so the price could come down.\par \par \uc2 Now it's totally empty. It's the emptiest I think it's been in 50 years.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Down 48 percent.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And it's so sad. And, by the way, the price is still very high.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I don't think gas went over $3 a gallon, if I'm not mistaken, when you were -- when you were president, as an average.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We had it down to $1.87.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We actually had a little period of time where it was...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We had it -- we had it lower than that.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But the energy companies -- the oil companies weren't going to last. We had to say -- I had said, "Wait a minute, I love it in one way, but in another way they're all going to go bust; we've got to get it up a little bit." But we had it down to $1.87. But we had a period of time where it was much lower than that. It was too low, actually.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So we have...\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's a good problem, by the way. That's a much better problem than it's at $6 and $7 and $8 and $9.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So we have this new -- I call it a new axis of evil...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You have China aligned with Russia aligned with Iran. Let's start with China.\par \par \uc2 Here you have a Chinese spy balloon; there are no consequences. Here you have, just this week, a Chinese simulator that takes out all of our warships in the Pacific, in the China Sea.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Very sophisticated.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You have a confrontation with a fighter jet of China with our fighter jet. They come, what, within 400 feet, or whatever it was. Our -- \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's defense secretary wants to meet with their defense secretary, and they basically gave \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  the middle finger and say no.\par \par \uc2 And you see that there's a growing Cold War with China, who's aligned with two other hostile regimes. And I've got to believe that's not a good situation for America right now. Because, you know, Putin seems to have no qualms about taking down a drone out of the sky, no consequences for him, no consequences for China. What would you -- what would you do?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So we had a great thing with China, until COVID came in, then I didn't even want to deal with them. But I had a great relationship with President Xi. But I was charging them tariffs. And if I didn't do it -- because they were dumping steel like nobody's ever seen anything like it before, destroying our steel mills and our steel plants. And I put a 50 percent tariff, and all of a sudden our steel industry was doing good. I did it for washing machines; I did it for dryers. I did it for a lot of things, because they were destroying a lot of our businesses.\par \par \uc2 But we were taking in hundreds of billions of dollars, And we're in Iowa. I gave the farmers $28 billion. You know that, $28 billion. And...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... in one of my moments I said, "There's no way I lose Iowa. I gave the farmers $28 billion from China. I took $28 billion. I asked \uc2 Sonny Perdue\uc2 , who was the secretary of agriculture, and a very good guy -- I said, "Sonny, how badly have our farmers been hurt by what China was doing?" They were killing our farmers, right, just killing them.\par \par \uc2 He said, "About $28 billion." I said, "That's OK." And I had $28 billion worth of checks written out to all of the farmers of our country. And I said, "There's no way I'm going to lose this state, and there's no way I'm losing Nebraska and some other ones."\par \par \uc2 But I've had more people thanking me for that. But think of it, I took $28 billion from China and gave it to our farmers. Nobody else would do that -- nobody else.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  -- you have said repeatedly in interviews that, if you were president, he never would have went into Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : He would have never.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How do you say that? And then you also have said that, if you're president, you can end this very quickly.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I'd say...\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: If I'm president -- and, by the way, this is a much worse position than before it started. Before it started, it was easy. He wasn't going to do it, and I had conversation. And it was always the apple of his eye. I mean, I could see that. But I said, "You're not going do it. And if you do it, we're going to have problems like you've never had before."\par \par \uc2 He understood. I said things -- he said, "You don't mean that." I said, "I mean it a 100 percent." And he didn't totally believe me, but he believed me 10 percent, and that's all he had to do. He...\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... he knew that there was going to be a problem.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Can I just say...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: And President Xi, the same way.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... you're -- you're implying something here. You basically said, "I'd obliterate you." Is that what you said to him?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I said things that were very bad, very nasty.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Kind of like what...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And, you know, honestly, I got -- I got -- and he said, "You don't mean that -- had to do with Moscow."\par \par \uc2 I said -- he said, "You don't mean that." I said "I do. I'll never talk about it again, but I do."\par \par \uc2 He said, "You don't mean it; you don't mean it." And we then went on to other subjects. But I don't think he believed me, but he believed me 10 percent. That's all he had to believe me. Five percent would be good enough.\par \par \uc2 But I had the same conversation with President Xi about Taiwan, President Xi of China. I said, "President, don't do it with Taiwan. Don't even think about doing it with Taiwan."\par \par \uc2 He was never going to do it. And now he's circling, circling. Ships are circling. Planes are flying over the top; 28 bombers last week went right over the middle of it, a lot of stuff going on.\par \par \uc2 And a lot of this has to do also with the fact that we were so incompetent in the way we left Afghanistan. It was so...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I think it was the most -- it was the most embarrassing and most incompetent moment in the history of our country. And I think both of them looked at that and they said, "Wow, this is not the same country that we know."\par \par \uc2 We rebuilt our military. I rebuilt the military, with new jets, new everything. We had everything. And...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... they gave away $85 billion worth of the best equipment in the world. Nobody can even believe it. The biggest -- I mean, the biggest seller of equipment; they're the biggest -- right after us -- Afghanistan. Can you imagine? Afghanistan is one of the biggest arms merchants in the world. because they don't need 700,000 guns and rifles, 70,000 armor-plated trucks, and trucks, and different things -- but millions of dollars for some of them, 700,000 arms -- think of it -- rifles, 70,000 trucks.\par \par \uc2 There's not a used car lot in all of Iowa or in all of the country, probably, that has more than 500. These people had 70,000. And some of these are, you know, big, heavy, armor-plated stuff for the roadside bombs. Soleimani -- you know, Soleimani was not good. That situation was taken care of. And al-Baghdadi was not good, and that situation was taken care of.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But we did a lot. You know, our military is great, a lot of things going on with our military, with the woke and all this nonsense. They're not learning to fight and protect us from some very bad people. They want to go woke. They want to go woke. That's all they talk about now. I see letters that are being sent. It's horrible. I mean, it's really a serious problem. That would end immediately.\par \par \uc2 But when you look at what we did...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We rebuilt...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 We rebuilt our military. We added Space Force. Everyone said, "Oh, Space Force, what is that all about?"\par \par \uc2 When they came in, Biden wanted to end it. He said, "What is this, a game?" It's going to turn out to be one of the most important -- hasn't happened since Air Force, 78 years ago, and it's unbelievable now. China and Russia were taking over space, and now we're leading in space because of Space Force.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So it's very important.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We've got to take a break. More with former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We'll ask him about the growing GOP field, the weaponization of our justice system and so much more. We are in beautiful Clive, Iowa, outside of Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you for being with us. Our town hall, and questions from the audience, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (FOX NEWS ALERT)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, we are back with \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 . We're outside of beautiful Des Moines, Iowa, for the hour. We will be taking questions from the audience.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And tonight, as the '24 race heats up...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... President Trump and other Republican candidates are now criss- crossing the state. And of course the former president has a commanding lead in both Iowa and nationally. The GOP field, though...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... is growing.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Last week Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  threw his hat in the ring, and soon we expect that former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  will be in. Anti- Trump zealot \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  will join in...\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... and but...\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... can anyone close the gap?\par \par \uc2 Let's talk about -- what, I guess we're up to nine people after next week.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : That's a good thing, isn't it? I think, pretty good.\par \par \uc2 But I don't think it matters. I don't know why people are doing it. They're at 1 percent. Some are at zero. I hear \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 's coming in. He's at...\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: He was at -- he was at 6 percent in New Jersey, which is -- I love New Jersey -- but 6 percent approval rating in New Jersey. What's the purpose? And he's -- he's polling at zero.\par \par \uc2 And others are -- I call him Ada Hutchinson. I don't call him Asa. I call him Ada Hutchinson. I gave him a little name for some reason -- for certain reasons.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But this guy, nobody knows who the hell he is -- never, never good.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And some -- you know, it's fine, but I don't understand what they're doing. Now, maybe there's something wrong, but when you're at 1 percent or less -- you know, 1 percent -- it says 1 percent with an arrow pointing left. There's one guy who's at zero with an arrow pointing left. That means he's at less than zero.\par \par \uc2 So it is what it is. You know, I really go after the one who's second. And I think the one who's second is going down so much and so rapidly that I don't think he's going to be second that much longer. I think he's going to be third or fourth. He had a very bad day today. He got very angry at the press. You're not allowed to get angry at the press.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me -- let me...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: At the fake news, he got angry.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So you probably became, in history, the most investigated president of all time.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Times 10.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. So...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But if my poll numbers went down, it would all end. You know, every time my poll goes up, I say, uh-oh, this is a problem.\par \par \uc2 But we had a poll today that showed I was 44 points above number two, and beating Biden -- and beating Biden by 11 points, being Biden by 11 points, and beating Biden by 15 and 16 points in some of them. And he's not doing well against Biden.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And let me ask you, because you are --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But we can't take a chance in this election.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think a lot of people agree with that. I don't -- I don't think things have been as bad -- turned so badly so quickly.\par \par \uc2 The third issue is there's a special counsel that's appointed and news broke yesterday that there might be a tape recording, quote, where you acknowledged that you understood --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- that these were classified documents.\par \par \uc2 First of all, do you know who this call may be with? Do you know anything about it?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, I don't know anything about it. All I know is this -- everything I did was right. We have the Presidential Records Act which I abided by a hundred percent.\par \par \uc2 Biden has 1,850 boxes with a lot of classified stuff that he's not supposed to have in his case. I have the right to declassify as president.\par \par \uc2 He's got 1,850 boxes that he doesn't want anyone to see. He had seven or eight boxes in Chinatown in Washington, D.C., where nobody even speaks English in Chinatown. Chinatown is very -- it's in favor of China and he has boxes in Chinatown.\par \par \uc2 They took those boxes and they sent them to Boston to his lawyer so his lawyer can look through `em and probably do things that you're not supposed to do.\par \par \uc2 No, this is about election interference. And, in fact, I have to tell you, Dershowitz and a couple very good guys wrote an article today, the tobacco king, you know who the tobacco king? He did great job on the tobacco companies.\par \par \uc2 They wrote an article today that this is a disgrace that they're even looking at this stuff. There was nothing done wrong, nothing whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 Now, look at the boxes with Biden where they're in his garage. They're all over the floor. They're sitting under his Corvette with the grease and everything else, on a garage door that you could cut with a scissor and no Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 I have Secret Service all over the place. Mar-a-Lago is a fort. It's literally -- you know, she built that as a southern White House.\par \par \uc2 But when you look at it, and it's another -- it's a continuation of the greatest witch hunt of all time. It's a hoax.\par \par \uc2 And it has to do --\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : -- it has to do, more than anything else, with trying to interfere with the election.\par \par \uc2 And, let me tell you, DOJ actually took -- you talk about Bragg, the D.A. of New York, never thought I'd be dealing with a guy like this. You talk about Bragg -- the DOJ in Washington put his top guy into the D.A.'s office which is local, which is city state, but they put the top guy in the Justice Department into that office to make sure Trump gets in trouble. Can you believe it? It's never, ever happened before.\par \par \uc2 And then \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 's lawyer, from I guess it's Paul, Weiss, left Paul, Weiss to work in the prosecutor's office because he hates Trump and he wants to get Trump. And then nobody wanted to do anything because they say, you know, Trump didn't do anything wrong, including Bragg originally. He said Trump didn't do anything wrong, and then he persecutes me for what he said was not wrong.\par \par \uc2 But they took this guy --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let me --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : -- they took this guy and they put him in there and he left the firm and he went in -- it's a big -- you know, Pomerantz, Mark Pomerantz -- and he left to become a prosecutor. He was a Democrat lawyer, and now, he's trying to prosecute me. And then what happened is they wouldn't do what he wanted to do because it was too bad even for them.\par \par \uc2 So this guy left and he writes a book during the process. They tell me what he did is criminal. They tell me. Now let's see what happens. But he's in a lot of trouble.\par \par \uc2 So here's a prosecutor left and he wrote a book during a prosecution. But I've been going through this for seven years. Russia, Russia, Russia, all of it, the Mueller report, which was no collusion after 2-1/2 years, there was no collusion with Russia.\par \par \uc2 I was the worst thing -- Putin would say, you know, they say, you like me. He said, you are the worst guy that we've ever had to deal with.\par \par \uc2 I'm the one that stopped the pipeline, the big pipeline going up to Germany. I stopped it.\par \par \uc2 When Biden came in -- it's called \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2 . When \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2 , nobody ever heard of it until I came along. I said, you're allowing Russia to build a pipeline through Europe? I stopped it, it was stopped dead.\par \par \uc2 And then the election came about and Biden came in, one of the first things he did was allow Russia to complete the pipeline. I had it stopped.\par \par \uc2 And then they say, I'll tell you what? They're a party of disinformation. They'll say Trump is soft on Russia.\par \par \uc2 I'm the hardest on Russia that there's ever been. The sanctions we did, everything else. And I got along with Putin, and I got along with Putin.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me -- let me follow up.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And by the way, the hardest on China by a factor. I took in hundreds of billions of dollars from China and as I said, no other president ever took in 10 cents.\par \par \uc2 And you know what? China respected us and President Xi respected your president and he didn't want to have any more tariffs and he didn't want to have any more sanctions but he respected us, and now he doesn't respect -- they don't even return phone calls.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, abortion now is back as a real campaign issue.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And then issues I didn't think when I started my radio career in 1987 I'd be talking a lot about, but education, kids, gender identity classes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: CRT. I never thought we would really have this deep debate about whether or not biological men could be laying in women's sports. When you - -\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So crazy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: On all of these issues, you know, what is the best way that you see this settled (ph)?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Well, I did something that nobody thought was possible. I got rid of Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And by doing that, by doing that, it put pro-lifers in a very strong negotiating position. Now they're negotiating different things.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, I happen to be of the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  school in terms of exemptions where you have the life of the mother, rape.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Right. Rape, incest, mother's life.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So you have that. And I think, you know, for me that works very well, and probably 80, 85 percent, because don't forget, we do have to win elections.\par \par \uc2 But I did something that nobody could do and I also made them the radicals because they are able and willing to kill babies in the ninth month, they're willing to kill babies. That's radical.\par \par \uc2 Pro-life isn't radical. They made pro-life radical, the other side. Pro- life is not radical.\par \par \uc2 What's radical is killing a baby in the 8th month, the 7th month, the 9th month, or even the baby's -- after the baby is born.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And -- and, you know, unfortunately a lot of politicians and you saw in the midterms, I think it was a big factor, that didn't really know how to talk about what we did with Roe v. Wade and what we did on pro-life. They didn't know how to talk about it and it energized the Democrats and they used that -- I mean, they used that as a commercial. You wouldn't believe it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, what should the Republican position be?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But especially when you didn't have the exceptions. When you didn't have the exceptions, they went after the people like viciously, the ads -- and those people did not -- generally speaking, they didn't do very well in terms of election.\par \par \uc2 But when you have the exceptions and you go through the whole -- the whole gamut, it's something that's an incredible thing. But one thing it really did, though, Sean, is it gave people that are pro-life a great power to negotiate. We had no power to negotiate because you had Ray -- Roe v. Wade sitting in there where you could do anything, where the other side could do anything. They can't do that right now.\par \par \uc2 So we're in a great position to negotiate something really, really good. And most people, I think, really respect what we did.\par \par \uc2 Now, I will say, every once in a while, I watch somebody say, I did more for abortion, on abortion, and abortion rights, and pro-life, I did more than Trump -- well, only stupid people would say that because everyone said there was no way that Roe v. Wade was going to disappear, but because -- because it was very unfair.\par \par \uc2 The other thing is people wanted to bring it back to the states. I consider that less important but nevertheless, a lot of people wanted to bring it back. This brings it back to the states.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: More with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and we'll hear from our Iowa audience as we continue from the great state of Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Please stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Welcome back to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 Hello, Iowa. Thank you for being here.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, according to a recent Harvard-Harris poll, the majority of Americans now believe, quote, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was involved with his son in what is an illegal influence peddling scheme, and yet, as far as we know, despite a mountain of evidence -- now, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  had Hunter's laptop since December of 2019, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and DOJ, they refuse to investigate, quote, the big guy, who Hunter complained he had to give half his income to.\par \par \uc2 And, on the other hand, there's no shortage of witch hunts against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  which we were talking about a little bit in the last segment.\par \par \uc2 Now, the 45th president of the United States is back with us for reaction to all of that.\par \par \uc2 This goes to the heart of Jim Jordan's investigation. Is the \uc2 FBI\uc2  politicized? Is the DOJ weaponized?\par \par \uc2 James Comer's committee looking into whether or not the Biden family, in fact -- we know that Joe lied when he said in a debate with you, and said it to other press people, when he said, there's -- I've never talked to my son about his foreign business dealings.\par \par \uc2 We got photographic evidence. We have dates and times of meetings. We now have, according to James Comer, routing plans to different LLCs and monies going to nine separate Biden family members.\par \par \uc2 And they're looking for one particular document where $5 million was exchanged for an act that they claim that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  may have committed in exchange for this deal.\par \par \uc2 Yet, how come --\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But they're being protected. Look at the time that Biden said about the billion dollars to get rid of the prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 Now, if -- can you imagine if I said that? A billion dollars to get rid of the prosecutor. You talk about tape. That's on tape. That's so illegal, what he said. It's America's money. We're not going to give you a billion dollars unless you get rid of the prosecutor that was prosecuting his son and his son's company, even though his son didn't know anything about energy or anything else.\par \par \uc2 And he's on the board of an energy company, getting paid a fortune, by the way. No, the whole thing is crazy, what's going on. And it's so bad, because it makes them look so bad. We talk about borders, we talk about elections, but you can add the -- our justice system.\par \par \uc2 If it's corrupt, if the people think -- if there's any perception of being corrupt -- and when you look at all of this criminality, like, the laptop has so much stuff on it, it's so bad, it's so evil, and yet they don't want to do anything.\par \par \uc2 It even affected the impeachment, because impeachment hoax number one and two, if they read the laptop, and they had the laptop, should not have proceeded, because I was right. And it should not have proceeded. A lot of people said that.\par \par \uc2 But it is a dual system of government. There's a dual system of -- you talk about law and order. You can't have law and order in a country where you have such corruption. And the corruption is -- and they fight so hard not to give the papers.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : With me, they make up papers.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : They fight so hard not to give a document. Now, how bad can this document be?\par \par \uc2 And it's very dangerous. I think it's a third point. But it's very dangerous for our country.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, Comer said to me on radio today he has the document. He said on TV last night.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And, by the way, he's doing a great job, and Jim Jordan are doing -- they're doing a fantastic job.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let me ask you one question.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have asked you this question before, and it comes up a lot.\par \par \uc2 People know that I have interviewed you all these years. I have known you almost 30 years. And people ask me and say to them, why does he have to fight so hard? Why doesn't he pick his fights a little more? Why does he have to call people names?\par \par \uc2 And the only reason I think this is an important question is because these -- I think everyone here tonight is likely voting for you, right? So...\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: However...\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I hope so.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: ... it's going to come down to those people that maybe you're in the middle a little more.\par \par \uc2 And the argument that they make to me is, if he would just tone it down a hair, stop a little of the name-calling...\par \par \uc2 (BOOING)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Hang on. I said it's their question. Leave me alone. All right.\par \par \uc2 That it might help you with swing voters and -- that are needed for you to get over the finish line. It's already hard enough, electoral vote-wise, for a Republican to win. What do you say to them?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: OK, you ready?\par \par \uc2 And I say this to everybody. I won an election. It was unprecedented. We beat somebody that supposedly had it made, and they probably did things in that election too. They were shocked. But I came into office. And from the day I got in, I was under siege by people that have been in Washington for many years, put in there by many different presidents, in most cases, people that were against me.\par \par \uc2 Like, they spied on my campaign. They did all sorts of things. I was under investigation and under siege, and so were my people. And if I wasn't tough, I wouldn't be here right now. I guarantee you that.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : If I didn't fight back, I wouldn't be here.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : What they did is so bad, and they have been caught.\par \par \uc2 Now, so far, nothing's happened to them of consequence. We had an attorney general, Bill Barr, who didn't have the courage to fight. He just didn't have the courage. He was a nice man, but he didn't have the courage. He lost his courage when they wanted to impeach him. They said, we're going to impeach Bill Barr.\par \par \uc2 They didn't even know why. There was no reason to impeach him. He didn't do anything wrong. But he didn't have the courage. We need courage in this country, or we're going to lose our country.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, I will tell you what.\par \par \uc2 You could stand up if you want or sit down, whatever you prefer.\par \par \uc2 Hi, sir. What's your name?\par \par \uc2 MIKE ETHERIDGE, VOTER: Mike Etheridge (ph).\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, Mike, is it?\par \par \uc2 ETHERIDGE: Mike.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Hi, Mike.\par \par \uc2 You have a question for President Trump?\par \par \uc2 ETHERIDGE: I do.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I like that, by the way. I -- I think I'm going to like this question. Look at that.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Look at that shirt.\par \par \uc2 ETHERIDGE: I'm going to say yes.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He's making money off your name, just so you know.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I'm -- OK. I'm going to -- we're going to not sue him.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, somebody is.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I'm not going to sue him.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ETHERIDGE: My question is, from the time that you left office until now -- and, in fact, in my case, it happened very quickly.\par \par \uc2 I am a veteran. I use the VA. I was getting in to see a doctor two, three weeks.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes.\par \par \uc2 ETHERIDGE: From the time you left, and this is within a month, the next time was eight months.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Yes, I know. They let the system break. Are you talking about the VA?\par \par \uc2 ETHERIDGE: I am.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So, we had a 92 percent approval rating. Nobody's ever come close. I think the highest was 51, and it was many years ago.\par \par \uc2 We had a 92 percent with the VA. And I did two things that were really -- we had great people at the top. We had a lot of great people. You know, we talk about the bad ones, but we had a lot of great people, and they did a fantastic job. When you get a 92 percent rating -- and I really appreciate that you say it. What happened with the V.A. is they had a lot of very bad people in the V.A., sadists, very sick people, that were really -- they were beating up and hurting our people. And you couldn't do anything about it. And I got through Congress an act where we can fire those people. We got rid of 7,000 really bad people. But the other thing...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 ... of equal importance, maybe more important, if you had to wait -- like you said, you had to wait, under my system, if you had to wait more than a day, as you know, you would go to a private hospital, or you would go to a private doctor, and they would take care of you. And people weren't dying.\par \par \uc2 You know, people were dying waiting on line. They were waiting for six months. They became terminally ill for something where a simple procedure or a simple prescription could have taken care of it. And if they had to wait for more than 24 hours, I gave them the right to go to a private doctor. We paid the bill. We negotiated with them. We had certain set prices, because otherwise, you know, it wouldn't be good. And we had the highest rating. That's why the veterans love Trump. We did a great job.\par \par \uc2 It's so nice that...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... you said it. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you, Mike. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right. I understand -- sir, what's your name?\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: My name's Tony, retired USAF lieutenant colonel, volunteer for a number of senior organizations, to include AARP, full -- full disclosure.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Great.\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: High inflation; we have a Medicare system that is severely lacking funding, running out of funding.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Right.\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: We have a trust fund in Social Security that's going broke. Across Iowa, serious concerns for seniors. What's your envision? What can you do? How can we solve these problems and get 'em done?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : So inflation is a killer of countries. If you look back 200 years, you could look back to empires where inflation came; the empires all dissolved. They were all gone. Inflation is -- it's a cancer to a country.\par \par \uc2 We are going to stop inflation. We still have way high inflation, the highest in 52 years. And they're saying, "Oh, we're doing better because it's down to 5 percent." Five percent is a lot. But we were heading up, and we could head up right now, with what's going on, we could end up very, very much higher.\par \par \uc2 But we're going to drill. We're going to bring energy way down. When energy comes down, other things come down. That's what caused the inflation in the first place. We're going to bring energy down. We're going to then bring interest rates down, because interest rates, people can't buy homes; they can't borrow money. They can't do anything now.\par \par \uc2 I mean, our -- right now, our economy is a total mess. And we'll stop it. And when we stop inflation...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... and when we get interest rates down, and when we do all of the things that we have to do, including -- again, I rebuilt our military, but we have to rebuild it again. You know, our military has no ammunition. We have no ammunition. We've given much of it, almost all of it, but we've given much of it to Ukraine. And we want to help people, but I want to stop the war. I don't want that war to continue. And I'll stop that war, mark my words\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I'll stop that war in 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : But we're in a position...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mr. President, let me ask, serious question, how do you stop that war in 24 hours?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: I know both, and frankly, Zelenskyy was very good, because, you know, he was part of the phone call, and he said he didn't say anything wrong to me. The -- he could have gone and grandstanded and said, "Well, I felt threatened; I felt threatened." He didn't. I get along with him. I get along with Putin. It's -- it would have been much easier to stop it before it started. Putin would have never done this. It would have been much easier. Right now, it's a mess. Now they're hitting Kyiv and hitting all sorts of things that weren't supposed to be hit. The country is being decimated.\par \par \uc2 By the way, the deaths are far more than they're -- you know, when they say nine apartment houses got knocked down and two people got hurt, no, no, hundreds of people died. The -- the numbers are much different than what you're being told.\par \par \uc2 I will get them into a room, and they will -- and I know an exact way. Number one, you tell one, "You're not going to get anything unless you make a deal." You tell the other one, "They're going to get a lot unless you make a deal."\par \par \uc2 And you just sit 'em...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... and you put 'em in -- and you have to make a determination.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : And within -- I'm telling you, within 24 hours, that whole thing will be settled. It will be settled. And I have -- and you need the power of the Oval Office. You do. You can't just walk in and say, "Oh, I'm going to settle the deal." You need the power of the presidency.\par \par \uc2 It was a war that should have never, ever started. It's a horrible war. It's a vicious, vicious -- I saw today where missiles are going into cities, in this case Kyiv. And you see the schoolchildren going to school, and missiles are following them. The whole thing is horrible. I will have that settled in 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : People say, "Oh, you can't." It's just like...\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: ... when I hear DeSanctis -- when I hear DeSanctimonious come and say, "We need eight years." Again, if he needs eight years, don't vote for him.\par \par \uc2 I'll have that -- this country will be hopping in six months and a lot of it is going to do with energy and energy cost (ph).\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : It will be hopping --\par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: All right.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: -- in six months, and less than six months, but it will be -- it will be back.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Thank you, Iowa, for -- Iowa, for being here.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, Iowa, and all of you all over the country, that's all the time we have left this evening. Thank you all for joining us. Thank you. We hope you all had a good time.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, from the great state of Iowa. Now, tomorrow night, we're taping more of the president taking questions from this great crowd.\par \par \uc2 Have a great night. Thank you for joining us. More coming up tomorrow night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020230602ej6100001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Two Assaulted Pro-Life Activists Speak Out; Moments Away: Senate Debt Deal Vote; Trump Denounces Biden's Leadership In Townhall; Rep. \uc2 Andrew Clyde\uc2  (R-GA) Interviewed on Federal Judge Temporarily Blocking ATF Rule Concerning Gun Braces; Two Pro-Life Demonstrators Violently Attacked Outside Baltimore Planned Parenthood\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Campos-Duffy, Chad Pergram, Will Cain \par \uc2 7,748 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Anyway, from the great State of Iowa, now, tomorrow night, we're taping more of the President taking questions from this great crowd. Have a great night. Thank you for joining us. More coming up tomorrow night.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL CAMPOS-DUFFY, FOX NEWS HOST: I'm Rachel Campos-Duffy, and this is a special edition of "The Ingraham Angle" from New York City.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we speak exclusively to two pro-life activists who were brutally beaten while praying outside of a Planned Parenthood. And at any moment, the Senate will vote on the debt ceiling bill. We will bring you all the details as it is happening live from Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 But first, as the 2024 campaign kicks into high gear on the GOP side, there is a burning question that remains. What exactly is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  running on? The economy is in danger of recession. His foreign policy blunders have created an America with less power and influence, while unholy alliances led by China keep growing, and oh yes, the massive corruption engulfing his presidency shows no sign of abating. Watch this remarkable moment from the White House briefing yesterday.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: There is one Committee trying to get an \uc2 FBI\uc2  file alleging that President Biden took bribes. There is another \uc2 IRS\uc2  whistleblower who is alleging there is a cover-up in the investigation. Amid all of this, there was a Harvard/Harris poll this month that found that 53 percent of the public, including a fourth of Democrats, believe "\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was involved with his son in an illegal influence peddling scheme". There is, of course, evidence the President interacted with his relative's associates from China, Mexico, Kazakhstan, Russia, and Ukraine. So, what do you say to the majority of Americans who believe that the President is himself corrupt?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Can I take that question?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY, SPOKESPERSON, U.S. NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL: The President spoken to this, and there is nothing to these claims.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: I don't know if you could hear it, but off camera, as Kirby was trying to figure out how to answer that devastating question, a stunned KJP reportedly took the Lord's name in vain. But, beyond the incompetence and the corruption, there is another question. Where is Joe? He is running for re-election, but he hasn't even held a campaign event yet. We did finally find him today taking a quick trip in Colorado.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Remember how the media reacted when all Trump did was walk gingerly down a pretty steep ramp at West Point.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: President Trump is facing some new questions about his health, after an unsteady walk down a ramp.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: New questions about President Trump's health after his visit to West Point.\par \par \uc2 MIKA BRZEZINSKI\uc2 , MSNBC HOST, "MORNING JOE": The event sparked some concerns about the President's own health.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It took him 10 minutes to walk down a ramp in the shuffle that alarmed a lot of people around the country who says, what's wrong with the President the United States?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: What's wrong with the President? He didn't want to slip on a ramp, Steve. Are you going to ask the same thing about Joe now that he has fallen and can't get up? By the way, Joe also criticized Trump for walking down a ramp.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Look at how he steps and look at how I step. Watch how I run up ramps and he stumble down ramps. OK? Come on.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Look how Trump walks up the stairs, and now look how you walk up the stairs. I could do this all day long. Biden stumbling on the stage is actually the perfect metaphor for his stumbles in the debt ceiling debate. His bumbling negotiating tactics months ago, now has America at the brink of default. The man who was sold to us as a master negotiator because of his many decades in the Senate, has been largely a wall. But, in spite of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the deal is actually still getting closer to his desk. Any moment now, the Senate will vote on the Biden-McCarthy debt ceiling deal.\par \par \uc2 For all the details, we go live to Capitol Hill where Fox News Senior Congressional Correspondent Chad Pergram is standing by. Chad.\par \par \uc2 CHAD PERGRAM, FOX NEWS SENIOR CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Rachel, good evening. The nation is closer to avoiding a crisis over the debt ceiling. The Senate will vote within the hour to suspend the debt ceiling through 2025. The Senate is now working through a series of amendments before final passage. Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is assuming the role of track coach, rushing the Senate through votes.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): We were indulgent in the first vote. That's over. We're doing 10-minute votes. Please stay in your seats so we can finish this bill in a reasonable hour.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: Now, Schumer is encouraging Senators to get through each vote in 10 minutes or less.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SCHUMER: Madam President --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The majority leader is recognized.\par \par \uc2 SCHUMER: -- 10 minutes 40 seconds. We got 40 seconds to go when we can get it all at 10.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: The Senate vote comes on the heels of the House posting a robust 317 "yeas" on the same bill last night. The bill needs 60 votes for passage. Once the Senate approves the bill, it goes to the President's desk for signature. The Senate was largely cut out of the deal. This was a negotiation between President Biden and House Speaker Kevin McCarthy. Rachel.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Thank you, Chad.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Missouri Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , one of the planned "no" votes on this debt ceiling. Senator, why are you voting "no" on this?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOSH HAWLEY\uc2  (R-MO): Really simple. For me, the most important deficit we face is our trade deficit with China. Every dollar of that deficit represents jobs lost to China, 60,000 in my home State of Missouri alone. It represents industry lost to China. It represents manufacturing withering away. And this deal doesn't do anything to address those needs to bring back blue-collar jobs to this country and actually start making things here again. So, I'm going to vote "no". And I tell you what? \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's policy of making China rich and America poor has got to be reversed.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: So, Senator, tonight, Senator Majority Leader Schumer said that the debt bill does not prevent Congress from pursuing more aid to Ukraine. What's your reaction on that?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Oh, I mean, isn't it striking that what the Senate is most concerned about, as we look at what all of the challenges the United States is facing, our runaway deficits or runaway trade deficit is aid to Ukraine, more billions of dollars in aid to Ukraine without any accountability? Here is what's going to happen. The Congress is absolutely going to blow right through these supposed caps. Already tonight, Schumer was talking about how they're going to pass more money for defense, more money pretty soon for domestic spending, more money for all kinds of giveaways. Mark my words, pretty soon, they will be right back to the pork barrel spending. Nothing is going to change here.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Senator, you want more spending cuts. But, let's be honest. I mean, the Senate majority is in the Democrat hands, so is the White House. So, how do you get a deal done when they actually want to spend more money?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Yes. Well, the way that you get a deal is you've got to insist on what's most important. And for me right now, ending our trade deficit with China is priority number one, bringing back those jobs, blue-collar jobs to this country, making things in America again. When we're going to start producing stuff in this country? To me, that's how you put our economy on a sound footing into the future. That we should be laser focused on and reversing Biden's policies of making China rich and America poor.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Well, speaking of China, I wonder what they think about that fall that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took. I mean, I hate to keep talking about it. But it sends a message, doesn't it, to our enemies?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Well, I think what they see is what the whole world can see, which is that this President just isn't up to the job. And it's not about one incident one day. It's about what goes on every single day. He won't take questions. He won't engage. He is gone half of the time. And when he is engaged, it's on all the wrong issues for all -- in all the wrong ways. So, listen, we need to change at 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue. There is no doubt about it. And I'm looking forward to the American people getting away and really soon.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: I know you'd like to talk about policy, Senator, but I'm going to have to ask you about politics.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Sure.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: What does that fall, what kind of implications will that have for the Democrat ticket? I mean, you see RFK Jr making a lot of moves here, getting stronger, and you see President Biden falling, as the Democrats are trying to rally everyone around him and kick everyone else out of the race. They won't even debate.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: I think it definitely signals weakness. I think it doesn't communicate any signal of strength, any projection or image of strength at all. And I think what it says is, to the rest of the world, is we have an American President who frankly isn't up to the job. And listen, people know this. The Democrats know it. They say it all the time behind closed doors. They talk about his age. They wish he wouldn't run again. But, he is bound and determined to. And so, pretty soon, the American people are going to get to weigh in.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Who is to blame for this? I mean, I saw that video. I was sad for our country, for him. I was kind -- as a political -- former political spouse, I was upset at his wife, and the people closest to him for putting him in this position.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Well, I think the choice is ultimately his. I mean, it's his choice to run or not to run. He thinks he wants to run again. And the truth is, at a certain point, you have to ask yourself, can you really do the job? But, here is my bigger issue with him, is that even if he could do the job, everything he wants to do is terrible. You look at what he is doing, making us dependent on Chinese solar powers, making us dependent on Chinese batteries, turning off our energy supply in this country. I mean, even when he is 100 percent lucid and with it, his policies are a disaster. So, all the way around, it's bad, which is why we've got to have a change.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes. All of those policies sound like someone who is compromised, perhaps. They just make no sense if you care and love America. If you care about America, love it. All right. Senator, great talking to you.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: It's the most serious time and the most dangerous time right now in the history of our country. We have nuclear weapons on lots of different areas. We have Russia. We have North Korea. We have Iran who is going to soon have what that should have never happened. This is the most dangerous time in the history of our country because of the power of the weaponry, and we have somebody that doesn't understand what's happening, and it's a very dangerous thing. It's a very bad thing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: I couldn't agree more, and that was President Trump during an exclusive townhall with our own \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joining me now to break it down is \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , former Senior Advisor to President Trump and Founder of America First Legal, as well as Will Cain, my friend and co-host on "Fox & Friends Weekend", and host of the "Will Cain Podcast."\par \par \uc2 Stephen, I'm going to start with you. What's your reaction to President Trump's performance tonight on that townhall with \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FMR SENIOR ADVISOR TO PRES TRUMP, & FOUNDER, AMERICA FIRST LEGAL: Well, obviously, that's President Trump in his element. I worked with him. I was at his side for six years. He is incredible when he is with real Americans out there in the country, interacting with them, taking their questions. Remember, he spent his entire life, for decades, before politics, working on construction sites with blue-collar workers, everyday citizens. So, that's where he feels most comfortable. And you really saw him shine in that venue.\par \par \uc2 But, on a substantive and a policy analysis, I think what he said about Ukraine, as his priority, is so important to bring peace back to Europe. We have the greatest threat of nuclear war in our country since the height in the world, since the height of the Cold War. And this primary is going to be about anything, and this general election is going to be about anything. What could possibly be more important than restoring peace to Europe, in the world, a piece that we hadn't knew, but just a little bit more than two years ago?\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Will, Stephen brings up a great point. Ukraine isn't talked enough about. It is a place where perhaps there is a little bit of a difference between DeSantis and Trump. Is there enough of a difference, or should they be on the same page? If you're DeSantis, is that the better position to be on?\par \par \uc2 WILL CAIN, FOX NEWS HOST, "FOX & FRIENDS WEEKEND": Before I dive into DeSantis versus Trump, Rachel, if I may --\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Sure.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: -- I think the style and the substance of what we just witnessed with \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is one and the same, the style and the substance. Put this into the context of the conversation that we just heard \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have, that you and Stephen are having, about this moment in history, the danger --\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: -- the fact that the world is nuclear armed up and we're sitting on this precipice. And then, as I listened to you earlier tonight, Rachel, talk about something that I think is of consequential importance, the incapability of the current President of the United States to walk a few feet. Now, I'm not here to kick a man while he is literally down. But, this is the free world we're talking about. This is the leader of the free world. And we cannot have someone who is simply incapable. It is a national security risk. And you look at that and you take that moment and you pause it against the fluency, the competency, the comfort, that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had in an hour of ad lib, not pre-scripted, not screened questions, not even a monologue, simply responding in real time to a question that cannot be anticipated.\par \par \uc2 We need, whether or not it's Trump, whether or not it is DeSantis, we need a leader who literally can lead with competency and with strength. And I think those two moments, Biden falling, Trump standing, sitting there with Hannity, those are all the style and also all of the substance of this election.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes. I couldn't agree with you more. I think you're absolutely right on point. In addition to foreign policy, as you know, Stephen, we are facing a culture war here at home. This week, a video went viral of a moustache man greeting little girls outside of the Bibbidi Bobbidi Boo (ph) salon in \uc2 Disney\uc2 . And it was just another example of little girls being robbed of spaces and experiences from their girlhood for the sake of this ideology. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is fighting \uc2 Disney\uc2  on this, and a lot of conservative moms have told me they are happy that he is doing that, and yet \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is fighting him on this, or at least criticizing him on this. Would you say if you were advising Trump that that was a smart thing to do?\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Well, just not how I see the situation at all. President Trump has put out a plan to fight the transgender lobby. That is the most cutting edge plan I've seen from anybody. He is going to -- he is proposing to decertify medical institutions so they cannot get Medicaid or Medicare that perform these procedures. He is saying he will instruct the DoJ to pursue civil rights charges and criminal charges against people who hurt our children. And he is proposing a 50 state ban on child genital mutilation. This is all hard hitting aggressive culture warrior stuff. His criticism on this issue has been all about the effect. Has it worked? Is \uc2 Disney\uc2  protecting children? Is \uc2 Disney\uc2  safeguarding the interests of our families?\par \par \uc2 When it comes to being a culture warrior, I can tell you, when