aw at \uc2 Disney\uc2  is an affront to truth and beauty, and we are in the midst of a cultural revolution, and we need a strong leader. Stephen, Will, great having you on.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, our exclusive interview with two pro-life activists who were brutally beaten while praying outside of Planned Parenthood. But, first, Joe wasn't the only Biden to tumble today. Was today is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's worst day ever? Well, let's see. We're going to lay out all of Hunter's terrible developments coming up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: There have been so many Hunter Biden developments this week. I hope I can actually get through all of them tonight. First, in the House Oversight investigation into the Biden family's corrupt business dealings, Republicans were sent to interview an informant when he suddenly went missing.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MARIA BARTIROMO\uc2 , FOX BUSINESS NETWORK ANCHOR: Where is that informant today? Where are these whistleblowers?\par \par \uc2 REP. JAMES COMER (R-KY): Well, unfortunately, we can't track down the informant. We're hopeful that the informant is still there. We have people that want to come forward, but honestly, Maria, they fear for their lives. Not only are the Biden lawyers and the Biden White House intimidating them, the media is trying to intimidate and discredit them.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Well, that missing informant has actually turned up again. Gal Luft telling the New York Post he is alive and living as a fugitive in an undisclosed location after skipping bail in Cyprus while awaiting extradition to the U.S. over arms trafficking charges. He says he is innocent and that he was forced to skip bail because he is the victim of a political persecution by the U.S. to protect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his son Hunter and his brother Jim.\par \par \uc2 Next up, as his dad pushes for stricter gun laws, POLITICO reports that if Hunter is charged with a gun crime for purchasing one while lying about his drug use, his lawyers are ready to challenge the law under the Second Amendment. And just hours ago, we learned that John Paul Mac Isaac, the computer repair shop owner who had Hunter's laptop, was deposed by Hunter's attorneys today. It's all part of a countersuit, saying Isaac illegally distributed Hunter's personal data from the laptop. Finally, speaking of Hunter's laptop, more pictures. A new website is launched today featuring nearly 10,000 photos spanning over 11 years. I don't know if I want to see them.\par \par \uc2 But, joining me now is Garrett Ziegler. He is the former White House aide, and the man behind Bidenlaptopmedia.com, along with Chris Swecker, former \uc2 FBI\uc2  Assistant Director.\par \par \uc2 Garrett, let's start with you. What's up with these new photos? What are they? What story do they tell? And also, what's up with the website, because it seems to have been down all day?\par \par \uc2 GARRETT ZIEGLER, CREATOR OF BIDENLATOPMEDIA.COM, & FORMER TRUMP WHITE HOUSE AIDE: Well, thank you for having me on. Yes. This site, Bidenlaptopmedia.com, is our group's third project. We put together a 644- page dossier on the contents of the device. It's called "Report on the Biden laptop". That was released in October of 2022. The second project was Bidenlaptopemails.com, 120,000 emails that anybody with an internet connection can go to and download all of them. And so, this was the third installment of our nonprofit research group putting out these photos in a responsible way, all the genitalia is redacted and there is considerable genitalia, and all of the Social Security numbers and credit card information is redacted.\par \par \uc2 And so, this is our mission to bring truth and transparency. If the American people want to know what their First Family is like, they're going to get it. And we don't leave anything out. We just redacted -- redact the less than savory --\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ZIEGLER: -- parts of the --\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 ZIEGLER: -- photos.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 ZIEGLER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: All right. I'm going to go to you, Chris.\par \par \uc2 ZIEGLER: And --\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Oh, go ahead.\par \par \uc2 ZIEGLER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Really quick.\par \par \uc2 ZIEGLER: Well, I was just going to say that we've had worldwide DDoS attacks. We've been on the phone with \uc2 Cloudflare\uc2 . We are going to get it up and running just like the email site launch. There is some kinks. But, next week, we think it'll be perfectly running smooth like a well-oiled machine.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: All right. Kinks, no pun intended. All right. Chris, let's go to you. We know that \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  has been interfering with the investigation being done by the House, by Representative Comer. He had a subpoena. He still hasn't turned over the documents. What would be the justification for \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  not turning over the documents that Representative Comer has asked for?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS SWECKER, FORMER \uc2 FBI\uc2  ASSISTANT DIRECTOR: Well, he is going to say -- I think he is citing the attorney general guidelines that basically say that all confidential informants were -- we were taught very early on to protect their identities. That's appropriate. But, there are exceptions to that rule. And the lawyers in the \uc2 FBI\uc2  that are advising him know that. And that's why they caved in and said, Hey, come on up to the Hill or we'll come to you, you Congress, and you can review this information in a skiff.\par \par \uc2 But, I contend there is a lot more information than just that 1023, which is about a five or six-page report of the information that came from this confidential source back in June of 2020, supposedly. There is got to be follow-up investigation and other documents that need to be reviewed as well. And I hope they're asking for the right documents, because that's just the beginning, the 1023. That should trigger a whole lot of vetting and just proactive follow-up investigation to prove or disprove the information the source brought forward.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes. I mean, what else do you think they should be asking for? And by the way, it must be really a smoking gun. It must not just be protecting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  for not further investigating this, because he was willing to risk being -- having contempt of charges -- contempt of Congress procedures against him.\par \par \uc2 SWECKER: Yes. I mean, this case has been riddled with special accommodations for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  from the very start. I mean, to answer your question, there is a whole lot of FD-302s that ought to be accompany the 1023. But, to go back to the other thought, this state case started in 2018. That's five years. Nothing takes five years. They apparently delayed it for 18 months because they didn't want to do any real investigation in the lead up to the election because they thought it might impact the election. His lawyer just got a very special audience and got to make his case that they shouldn't indict him for the gun charge and the tax charge.\par \par \uc2 Heck, there is a fair violation in there. There is money laundering violations. There is fraud. There is tax violations, and then the gun charge. But, they want to put us to --\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SWECKER: -- sleep with the gun charge and the tax violations.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Well, Garrett, that might be why this shocking poll came out recently, 59 percent of Democrats still think that the laptop is a Russian disinformation. What's your reaction to that, and also to the fact that most Americans, a lot of Americans, also believe that the Hunter Biden laptop story is real, and that's what you're exposing through 