 to spend, how both candidates, Trump and DeSantis. They have to convince people. They're going to be a lot richer three years from now than they are right now.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: Well, we already saw what it was like in the Trump era, how we had wages growing, how the economic situation had become more stable so that corporations could actually have a regulatory environment that made sense that would allow them to grow, and these things will be important for whoever gets the nomination.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Mollie and Stephen, great to have your analysis. Thanks so much, and we have an update on that nutbag. Now prone to violence professor who cursed out pro-life students that we brought you yesterday? Well, it involves a sharp object. Well, see the shocking video for yourself. But first, what's really going on with this debt ceiling fight? Jonathan Turley is going to react to Biden secret plan to blame the Republicans and try to become constitutionalist.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The White House thought it was playing smart poker on the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: On the merits based on what I've offered, I would be blameless and there's a lot of others -- for example, the idea that we're in terms of taxes that they refuse to, for example, we -- I was able to balance the budget and pass everything from the global warming bill anyway.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. But they made a big mistake. McCarthy outmaneuver them by getting Republicans to stick together and pass an increase in the debt ceiling that was tied to popular cuts and spending and a fairly modest work requirement for welfare recipients.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. KEVIN MCCARTHY (R-CA): On February 1, when I sat down with the President, I said, let's work together. These are areas that I will not do, we will not raise taxes, we'll be bringing in more money than any time 