erica has proved resilient obviously, thrived in some ways, struggling in what other ways today, and she's just unbelievable. I can't believe that they still invite her to give talks like that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Oh, she's probably getting paid, Dana.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Do you think you got paid for --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I don't know. I don't go anywhere without getting paid. Judge Jeanine --\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT-AT-LARGE: I've got a dollar on me.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: She could have obviously said, you know, he's done a great job and I hope he gets reelected. And that's it.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL LEGAL ANALYST: Right. Oh, but that's not who she is. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  is the epitome, she is the essence of a woman who will step on anyone, right over anyone, do what she's got to do to get the front of line and I'm going to limit it to that. OK.\par \par \uc2 But what I will tell you is that one week after the Durham report, one week, where they come out and they tell us, this whole Russia collusion hoax was Hillary's idea. And she told \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and she told Barack Obama that she was going to do it, because the e-mail scandal was too hot, and she had to get the prosecutors off her back. One week later, she's running for president. OK.\par \par \uc2 You know, age is an issue, baloney, she's 75, he's 80. It's not age Hillary, its competence. And the truth is that, you know, 63 percent of Americans can't agree on anything today. But what they can agree on, is the fact that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not mentally sharp enough to be the president.\par \par \uc2 And yet, these Democrats, they come out and say, I just hope he stays focused, which is translation, that guy is so unfocused, his wife has to hold his hand, they have to remind him who's standing there with them.\par \par \uc2 Look, how many times as a woman have to lose running for president that stops her from running again? S