g sleeves all the time.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I love that.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You can't come to my club now. Geraldo?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Just over a year ago, my beautiful niece, Elizabeth Hurst Blair, loving mother of two, passed away -- awful, awful -- after a two-year battle with ovarian cancer. Initially misdiagnosed, she was determined to bring awareness to the symptoms of ovarian cancer. She established, a foundation called Elizabeth's Wish. This weekend, family and friends gathered fundraising near Philly, raised $50,000 for the cause, featured a live performance by 80s Rocker Rick Springfield. Elizabeth would be very proud of the turnout. For information, you can go to elizabethswish.org, elizabethswish.org.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I heard he does a pretty good, Jesse's Girl.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Jesse's Girl?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: I bet he does. OK, so a Missouri woman who's in the early stages of Alzheimer's and also has Parkinson's is in hospice care and she's a big Dolly Parton fan. And by the way, in case you've noticed, I've been playing Dolly Parton songs all week -- but her medical team posted her love for Parton on social media and posters filling her bedroom. Parton saw it and got in touch with the hospital, came to Missouri to visit the hospice patient, showering with gifts, giving her an invitation to her theme park, Dollywood. And that's who Dolly Parton is. She's really a good person.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Lovely. Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: She sure is. Tonight, "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME" at 7:00, we go inside the DeSantis Musk event. Take a look at that. What about you, Kennedy?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY: I certainly will. Well, Jesse, I'm glad you asked. Lester the steer had been missing for weeks. And finally, you can see this highway dash cam in Michigan. And it took -- no, don't worry. He survived. I'm not going to show a steer getting killed on live T.V. He was roped. He was lassoed.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Only zebras. We only do zebra.\