Have a great show.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I am Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. Where is Al? That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Now, there is only one thing worse than \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  claiming to care about black people. It's \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  and one of his proteges pretending to care about black people. Well, each of them celebrate one another.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REV. AL SHARPTON, PRESIDENT, NATIONAL ACTION NETWORK, & MSNBC HOST, "POLITICSNATION": We've got convictions. It was the first time we had convictions of a Police officer like that in all the years that I've been involved --\par \par \uc2 KEITH ELLISON, ATTORNEY GENERAL, MINNESOTA: Sure.\par \par \uc2 SHAPRTON: -- and this was monumental. You've set the template on how to do these kinds of cases.\par \par \uc2 ELLISON: All of us remember how you talked about get off our neck. You'll remember that that was such an important moment. And you were a voice for the people because of the precedent you laid down and many others laid down.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 , did you say a voice for the people? Please. But, just remember, they always care more than anyone else, always, especially if it is Police involved like, of course, the tragic case of George Floyd.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: You cared about the family, the human price that people pay to lose a loved one.\par \par \uc2 ELLISON: Well, you know, people who lose their loved ones to Police brutality are crime victims. They are crime victims. And any prosecutor worth his or herself is going to make those victims center. And so, this is something that I felt compelled to do.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Neither Keith Ellison, the AG of Minnesota, nor \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  are anything but racial opportunists. So, if a crime involving a black person can offer a PR or a political benefit, or in the case of something like Sharpton or Attorney \uc2 Benjamin Crump\uc2 , a financial pay day, they might get prominently involved. Otherwise, don't hold your breath. And on the nuts and bolts issues that actually plague the black community, especially in urban areas, the racial industrial complex is either nowhere to be found or actively working against the black community. How much time has \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 , for instance, devoted to the persistent problem of black gang violence in Minneapolis?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: My child can't play in the yard. I hear four gunshots a night.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: There is so much drug trafficking. There is so much gang violence.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I've never seen it this bad. I think not anybody has seen it this bad.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Gang violence in Minneapolis is so bad that the feds got involved. DoJ issued a major indictment of 45 gang members a few weeks ago, didn't get much coverage, alleging members of the gangs called the Highs and the Bloods engaged in a brutal and unrelenting trail of violence over the course of years, including revenge killings and alleged trafficking in fentanyl and methamphetamine. Now, our own Mike Tobin talked to an active member of the Gangster Disciples recently about violence in the city.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: These gangs are reckless, real reckless. It's not organized no more. It used to be structured in there. No women, no kids. Now, it's just a freefall.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Who knows how many black residents of Minneapolis gangs they've killed over the years by either drugs or murder? But, where is Rev. Al now? Why isn't he or one of his acolytes there mentoring youth to keep them out of the gangs? Because there is no fame in it, and there is certainly no money in it. And not a peep from Sharpton about this savage attack, six teens on bicycles, savagely beat what appeared to be a white man in LA. And this was just a few days ago. The video was disturbing.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Where are the parents? Where are the fathers who raised these kids? And where is \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 ? Or because the victim looks like was white, does this not count as injustice in the good Rev.'s eyes? And the reason, by the way, the brave Social Justice Warriors don't care to address the recurrent black on Asian attacks in our cities. Well, in Long Beach, California, last week, a 53-year-old victim said her attacker yelled racial slurs at her before punching her face. I thought I was going to die, she told the local reporter, too scared to even share her name. The attackers are still on the loose. Again, this is violence for no reason, broken families, a criminal justice system that's overloaded and that too often treats criminals like victims and victims like criminals.\par \par \uc2 So, does \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  and his pals believe that racism is the reason that teens as young as 13 in Maryland are stealing cars? And I looked and I looked and I found no sign of \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  speaking out last week after this shocking story out of Oxon Hill, Maryland, came out, where a 14-year-old girl orchestrated an attempted murder on a school bus. Now, these stories speak to deeper challenges in the communities that Sharpton and Crump claimed to care so much about, broken homes, deadbeat dads, and marijuana use at a young age. If \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  spent as much time advocating for fathers, as he does against so-called systemic bias in policing, he would really have made a huge impact.\par \par \uc2 Now, ditto for views on the issues that hurt minority families most, open borders. It's a nightmare for inner city America. It sucks up social services, crowded schools, but \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 , he wants to let in more illegals