or of your skin is, no matter what particular group you belong to, if you start to attack and stereotype and use violence against a collective other group, then you're a racist. And certain people who attack people because of the color of their skin are racists. It doesn't matter if they're brown or black or white. But, we haven't said that. We've said particular groups because of a long history of oppression cannot be racist. But yet, when we have these violent, racially motivated crimes, if they're attacking people on the basis of their race, or if they're demagoguing people --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Period.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: -- on the basis of their race, or they are stereotyping people and collect them on the basis of the race, and let's admit it, they are racists.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Pastor Brooks, Victor, thank you very much tonight.\par \par \uc2 And ahead of addressing the actual problems -- instead of addressing the actual problems facing the black community, the race grifters want to punish the states that are actually offering the best opportunities for businesses and families. So, you all heard about the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  issuing this travel advisory for the State of Florida, claiming it opens -- Oh, it's openly hostile to African Americans.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DERRICK JOHNSON\uc2 , PRESIDENT, NAACP: We should not use race or other as a tool to weaponize against people, and it unfortunately for a large percentage of Floridians, that's what he has done. Therefore, we are advising African Americans and others that if you travel to Florida, beware that your life is not valued, that we have a political landscape that could cause harm.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Join me now, Florida Congressman Byron Donalds. Congressman, first, how are you doing with all this hostility? It's a very difficult place for you to represent if it's so hostile to African Americans.\par \par \uc2 REP. BYRO