r \par \uc2 WHOOPI GOLDBERG, HOST, THE VIEW: He has got \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  syndrome.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  syndrome. Oh Whoopi. Really? That's it. That's it. We're still dining out on that line. I mean, it's actually I feel bad for them because now they're just out of material.\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: Look, Whoopi has made it, and she had made it with her last name Goldberg. And I think that's her actual birth last name. Sunny Hostin has made it. She is doing good. There are black people in our country who are making it and doing quite well. Black families are actually forming at the highest rate than they've been in 40 years, black moms and black dads raising their kids. That's a good thing. But, they're haters, because they're liberals, first and foremost. And they cannot tolerate black people in this country saying, you know what? I'm done with Democrat policy, because it doesn't work when you actually look at it, because the Democrats understand that without black voters being loyal to them, then they lose. Period.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How did Barack and Michelle make it? I mean, this country is so awful. Like, how was he a two-term President elected with majority white vote?\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: He gave a good speech to argument.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. I mean, you don't have -- I'm just saying, like, if it's all rigged, like, how do you make it?\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: Look, the truth of the matter is --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You are lucky.\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: -- the Democrats, this is the only game that they have, because if you look at their policy, whether you want to talk about currency, economy, border, foreign affairs, crime, education, you look at the actual points, they are losing the country, but they weaponize race, unfortunately, against our -- against the American people to continue to divide our politics.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Byron Donalds, always great to see you. Thanks so much for coming in tonight.\par \par \uc2 All right. The debt ceiling fight is really a battle of wills between whomever is running the White House and Kevin McCarthy. We're going to examine next. Plus Raymond Rose on the road in Orlando. What is he doing? I want to give you a hint. 2024. That's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: We're pretty well divided in the House, almost down the middle, and it's not any different in the Senate. So, we got to get something we can sell to both sides. And we need to cut spending.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They will come up right there. But, it's important to remember that the House has already passed a bill that would raise the debt ceiling. In fact, it did so back in April 26. That was almost a month ago now. Now, if it's the debt ceiling that represents a true threat to the US. Economy, I'd think that the business community would be pressuring the Senate and the White House to pass the House bill even if that means agreeing to some spending cuts. I understand those aren't always popular. But, haven't we been told that the debt ceiling is an existential threat to the whole economy?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WOLF BLITZER, CNN HOST: I'm not sure Americans are going to suffer if President Biden and Congress can't reach a deal.\par \par \uc2 REP. JEFF JACKSON (D-NC): There is just no overstating this. I think people have heard this from a lot of people. But, it is just plain truth. This would be a generational, economic, self-inflicted wound. We cannot allow a default.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Joining me now, Ben Domenech, Editor-at-Large for The Spectator, and a Fox News Contributor. Ben, McCarthy said tonight that they are getting closer to a deal. It was productive. What's your take?\par \par \uc2 BEN DOMENECH, EDITOR-AT-LARG