mocrat to call on California Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  to step down.\par \par \uc2 Michigan Congresswoman \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  responded to Democrat colleague \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 , after the Congressman repeated his call for Feinstein to step down gracefully.\par \par \uc2 Tlaib attack Feinstein for her absences from the Senate floor. Saying, they have allowed Republicans to pass legislation through the Chamber.\par \par \uc2 While the House has voted in favor of striking down President Biden's action last year, allowing Chinese solar panel manufacturers to avoid Obama-era tariffs.\par \par \uc2 12 Democrats joined Republicans in approving the resolution. It argues that tariffs were necessary to protect the fledgling U.S. solar industry, which is dwarfed by Chinese manufacturing. The Senate is expected to vote next week on similar legislation.\par \par \uc2 Navy Secretary \uc2 Carlos Del Toro\uc2  is defending his recent remark that climate change is a top priority for the service. He told lawmakers today he believes the issue is just as important for the Navy as ensuring a steady stream of sailor recruits.\par \par \uc2 Republicans say Del Toro, the Pentagon, and the Biden administration are losing sight of the main focus of the military in order to pursue extraneous goals like climate equity and eliminating extremism in the ranks.\par \par \uc2 Two U.S. helicopters returning from a training flight collided in Alaska yesterday, leaving three soldiers dead, and the fourth injured.\par \par \uc2 Each helicopter involved was carrying two people. The crash happened near Healy, Alaska. The choppers were headed for Fort Wainwright near Fairbanks. The cause is under investigation.\par \par \uc2 Montana's Republican governor has signed a bill to ban gender affirming medical care for young transgender people. The action by \uc2 Greg Gianforte\uc2  comes after the floor battle in the statehouse ended with the removal of a transgender lawmaker.\par \par \uc2 The state branch of \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  says it will file a challenge in courts.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, a pair of teachers in California is suing education administrators over policies they say require them to deceive parents about their children's gender identity.\par \par \uc2 The national correspondent William La Jeunesse has more from Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAM LA JEUNESSE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: In 2014, California lawmakers passed a landmark bill.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This law is just about making sure that transgender students can go to school.\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE: A battle over that law and others like it are challenging school districts across the country.\par \par \uc2 Does a student's right to privacy outweigh a parent's right to know?\par \par \uc2 Two San Diego middle school teachers say no. They claim the Escondido School District forces them to use, "any pronouns or gender specific name requested by the student during school, while reverting to their legal name when speaking with parents in order to actively hide information about their child's gender identity.\par \par \uc2 CORY BREWER, ATTORNEY, WISCONSIN INSTITUTE FOR LAW AND LIBERTY: They should have policies in place that are, you know, transparent, respect parents, and allow them to know what these policies are when it impacts their children.\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE: Legal experts say most states give parents the right to handle their children's health and welfare, in this case, 10 to 14-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 But in California, school officials must keep students' transgender status private. Disclosing that without a student's permission may violate the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 However, parents and some students believe, the law is being abused.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And everything was on the hush hush. They didn't want to talk to us about it.\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE: This