is is not like it was when Rick Perry was running and waiting for his legislative session to end.\par \par \uc2 I was a state representative in the Rick Perry-led governorship, and I watched him struggle with waiting for our session to end. But what he didn't have was a former president, which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  now is, and an operation already in place. It was a free-for-all, so to speak, and he didn't have an organized Trump team fighting against him that Governor DeSantis does today.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, now, you have mentioned the present governor of Texas, Greg Abbott. He could, we're told, throw his hat in the ring as a presidential contender. Does it matter? You still prefer \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 GOODEN: I don't believe he will do that. I believe he will support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 I believe all prominent Texans are seeing the light. They are realizing that the Trump train has not just left the station and it has not returned to the station, and it is moving along forcefully.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GOODEN: We want to retake this nation. We believe in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We believe he's a fighter.\par \par \uc2 And I believe the American people know he's a fighter. And I believe Democrats are terrified of him being back in the White House, and I hope they are. And I'm looking forward to that day, and I believe it will be a great day.\par \par \uc2 But, until then, we have got to get him nominated. We have got to get him across the finish line. And I believe the American people are all going to rally around him, and I'm really excited to be a part of his team.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Some of your Republican colleagues, not all of them, agree with that. They're impressed with what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did when he was president.\par \par \uc2 But there's been a lot of baggage since, a lot of controversy since. Now, as an indicted former president, whatever you want to say about 