e venues. You take, for instance, in Chicago, where crime is out of control. The mayor there, the new mayor, is protecting the crooks, talking about, well, it happens, but these young people are dealing with poverty.\par \par \uc2 The hell with them dealing with poverty. Tell them to go out and get a damn job. The problem we have is, we are supporting criminals and we are harming citizens as a result, Neil.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: And the fact is, if we look at some of the more major and substantial crimes, and they point to those that go down a little bit, still at levels that are extremely high, and that is something that is not proving on the national level.\par \par \uc2 Always good catching up with you on this stuff. I regret that it always has to be on this stuff, Ted, but thank you just the same.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: My pleasure, my friend.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, be well.\par \par \uc2 All right, in the meantime, Homeless Security Secretary Mayorkas, he has had a rough week before committees, but it got really nasty today. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. MICHAEL MCCAUL (R-TX): This drug trafficking that's killing 100,000 Americans, for God's sakes, and you, sir, I believe are complicit with this by your inaction at the border.\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, U.S. SECRETARY OF HOMELAND SECURITY: To say that we are doing nothing is an absolute falsehood. We are taking it to the cartels.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, hurry up and wait a little longer.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court ruling temporarily extending a hold on a lower court ruling that would have imposed restrictions on an access to a key abortion drug. More time for the justices to consider what to do on Friday.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. DONALD PAYNE (D-NJ): You want the narrative of the Southern border as the problem. Everything wrong with this country is the Southern border.\par \par \uc2 REP. DAN BISHOP (R-NC): Do you admit that your policies have led the country farther away from operational control of the border, as defined by the Congress?\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: Congressman, no, I do not.\par \par \uc2 BISHOP: I'm not surprised.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 SHEILA JACKSON LEE\uc2  (D-TX): This is what Republicans' idea of operational control. Mr. Secretary, would you please remind me who was president in 2019, when this photo was taken?\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: Congresswoman, that was President Trump.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON LEE\uc2 : That's right.\par \par \uc2 REP. MICHAEL GUEST (R-MS): Are all nine sectors of the Southwest border secure? And I'm just asking for a yes-or-no answer.\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: Congressman, I know you are asking for a yes-or-no answer. And the fact of the matter is that the challenges at the border are very complex and dynamic.\par \par \uc2 GUEST: Well, I'm going to take from that, if you can't answer yes, then the answer is no.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: OK, that went well.\par \par \uc2 But any hearing these days involving Alejandro Mayorkas have not really been going well, as he tries to justify or state that there's improvement going on at the border.\par \par \uc2 Bill Melugin has seen anything but.\par \par \uc2 But, again, this continues the theme in Washington where they're getting exasperated with what's happening because there's a lot worse that could be happening -- Bill.\par \par \uc2 BILL MELUGIN, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Yes, Neil this was a fiery hearing.\par \par \uc2 Republicans really went after Secretary Mayorkas over his handling of the Southern border. And there was one remarkable moment in particular where the secretary testified he disagrees with his own chief of U.S. Border Patrol. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do you disagree with the head Border Patrol agent when