hese three suspects as adults. In the meantime, the sheriff remains confident this third suspect will be caught and brought to justice. Back to you.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Jonathan Serrie live in Miami. Jonathan, thanks a lot.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in Fox News Chief Political Analyst Brit Hume. Brit, good evening.\par \par \uc2 BRIT HUME, FOX NEWS SENIOR POLITICAL ANALYST: Hi, Mike.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: On these last two stories, Tennessee and South Florida both have ties to guns. I want to play a clip from the sheriff in South Florida and I'll get you to react to it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WOODS: But one thing that has no ability or the capacity to commit the crime itself and that's the gun. All the gun laws we got in place didn't prevent it, did it? Neither will any new ones.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Brit, it seems to me when they are terrible crime stories these days. The left knee jerk reaction is go after the guns but in many of these cases, there's a mental health component. And there are also cases where the breakdown of the American family is evident.\par \par \uc2 In South Florida, you're talking about 12, 16 and 17 year old suspects. Where are you on these subjects tonight?\par \par \uc2 HUME: Well, I would just say, Mike, that what the sheriff said kind of goes to the heart of what the debate is always has long been about, gun control, which is this, that the gun itself cannot do anything. It is the person wielding the gun that is the danger and in the nation of Washington guns where the Constitution protects the right to own and keep a gun, and you know, millions and millions of guns out there. No gun control than anybody could ever imagine reconciling with the Constitution would be able to prevent these crimes. What you have to try to do is prevent the emergence of criminals.\par \par \uc2 And of course, in this case, one of the criminals we're talking about, the alleged criminals we're talking 