that criminals back on the street. It's an issue with their forensic processing, that the processor of forensic evidence, I guess it's not up to snuff in DC. I thought I was dreaming or having a nightmare when I heard that. That takes the cake.\par \par \uc2 REP. JAMES COMER (R-KY): Yes, talk about passing the buck. I mean, this is one example of many prosecutors in all these blue cities that just aren't doing their job. They are soft on crime. They're passionate about criminal justice reform. They want to give criminals more rights than then law- abiding citizens. And as a result, there's a direct correlation with soft on crime, prosecutors and increased crime. And Washington, DC is a perfect example that we have a terrible group of prosecutors in this city, and that's why we have skyrocketing crime.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, they're saying well just help us become a state and all will be well. I say, well, how about Maryland that's run by Democrats. How's Baltimore doing? Illinois run by billionaire JB Pritzker? How's Chicago doing? So, - they think statehood is going to - they can't even run this city, let alone have it be a state.\par \par \uc2 COMER: No, there's no way they could be self-sustainable as a state. They want to be a state for one reason to be able to have two more Democrat U.S. senators. That's the whole thing. It's all about politics. It has nothing to do with public safety. It has nothing to do with sustainability. It's all about politics and trying to tip the scale of power in the House of Representatives and in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And I believe that the leaders in Washington, DC have really done a great injustice to the people. They think that all the problems in Washington, DC are as a result of not having representation in Washington, DC, when they have representation--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They just want two more. They just want two reliable Democrat Senator.\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2 : That's it.\par \par \uc2 INGR