ussion with my administrators, but they refused to do so.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Mr. Kitchen, my apologies, by the way on what's happened to your, I think, great country. What's your recourse legally in Canada?\par \par \uc2 JAMES KITCHEN, ATTORNEY: Well, it's limited, of course, because our Constitution is much weaker and because there seems to be culturally and legally much less respect for individual rights and freedoms and much more interest in, you know, government having the kind of power to do what it wants.\par \par \uc2 But there is recourse to the Ontario Human Rights Commission in this case. We think there's been religious discrimination on the basis of Josh's Christian religious beliefs. So we're going to file a complaint to the Ontario Human Rights Commission.\par \par \uc2 And there is recourse through the Board itself, as far as appealing these disciplinary decisions and we hope to explore that as well.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I mean, \uc2 Fidel Castro\uc2  's son takes over your country, and all of a sudden it becomes Cuba. Like it's just shocking.\par \par \uc2 Josh, quickly to you. The police officers who arrested you, a high school student for quoting the Bible in a Christian school, must have been ashamed of themselves, I would hope. Did they seem embarrassed?\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER: I wouldn't say so. I've had a lot of experience with police over the last couple of years, just through the Freedom Convoy and other events like that and the police state is quite embarrassing in our country. So no, there was no different response from them.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Are you going to continue High School?\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER: I am certainly going to try to. I would hope that my personal beliefs wouldn't exclude me from an education, but it would appear that's the way it's going to be.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It's an unbelievable story. I hope you'll both come back.\par \par \uc2 Thank you, Josh Alexander and James Kitchen, his attorney. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You may recall the best story of the year, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  's transgendered nuclear waste disposal official, Sam Brinton exposed as an airport kleptomaniac. We are going to talk to one of his victims, an African designer next week.\par \par \uc2 Have the best weekend with the ones you love.\par \par \uc2 See you Monday.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TCARL00020230311ej3a00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 White House Celebrates International Women's Day By Honoring Biological Male; QAnon Shaman's Mother And Lawyer React To New Surveillance Footage; Interview With Rep. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (R-FL); Resolution To Withdraw US Troops From Syria Fails In House Vote; New Intelligence Suggests A Pro- Ukrainian Group Sabotaged Nord Stream Pipeline; Sheep Saved Their Own Lives By Escaping The Slaughterhouse; Members Of Congress Spar Over The \uc2 Twitter\uc2  Files; \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  Shares Plunge On Stock-Sale Plan To Stem Cash Burn; Simon Ateba: The WHCA Lied In Their Letter To Me And Did Not Follow Their Own Membership Guidelines\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Tulsi Gabbard, Charlie Gasparino \par \uc2 7,629 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 March 2023\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: I didn't think about it that way. Maybe those types of people shouldn't be reproducing.\par \par \uc2 That's all for tonight. DVR the show.\par \par \uc2 Tucker is up next and always remember, I'm Watters and this is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2  , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 The battle of the sexes has finally ended after several million years of jockeying and strife. Men won conclusively. We know this because yesterday was International Women's Day. That's the day we, as a global community celebrate women. But if you looked closely at the women we were celebrating, you may have noticed a lot of them weren't actually women. They were lumpy-looking dudes, and that was not accidental.\par \par \uc2 In fact, it was a brilliant piece of sexual jiu-jitsu. Sun Tzu could have written that strategy.\par \par \uc2 Here you had men who are clearly craftier than they look somehow convincing a whole lot of otherwise self-aware and highly educated women to praise them as living paragons of womanhood. Think about how hard it would be to sell that proposition. "I'm going to steal your identity and then mock and degrade the immutable characteristics that define you as a person, and then as I do this, you are going to smile brightly and applaud and then give a speech about how liberated you feel." How about that?\par \par \uc2 The whole thing is amazing. It's like watching a practical joke devised by the drunkest, most cynical fraternity brothers at the University of Alabama during a hungover breakfast at \uc2 Denny's\uc2  . You can picture them all there in baseball hats, dipping Copenhagen