2 So the men are taking all the prizes set aside for women, but that's not all they're stealing. They're also taking what progressive called "lived experiences." So anyone could throw on a halter top, but the real dividing line is biology. Only actual women can have menstrual cycles. Well, not anymore. Anything a woman can do, a man can do better. That's the slogan of the trans movement, and that includes getting cramps. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TRANSGENDER GIRL: Wow. I was just thinking, "Oh, I swear to God, if anyone says, welcome to womanhood, I'm going to lose my [bleep].\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Talk about mansplaining. That's the ultimate mansplainer. Some guy, ladies at a certain time each month, your tummy may hurt a little, let me tell you about it and what to do when that happens. It's too funny.\par \par \uc2 "Of course, if men can get their periods, by definition, they can also get pregnant, and that's why we need legal abortion. So, men won't be forced into back-alleys." Watch Law Professor Khiara Bridges explain.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOSH HAWLEY\uc2  (R-MO): You've referred to people with a capacity for pregnancy. Would that be women?\par \par \uc2 KHIARA BRIDGES, LAW PROFESSOR: Many women, cis women, have the capacity for pregnancy. Many cis women do not have the capacity for pregnancy. There are also trans men who are capable of pregnancy as well as non-binary people who are capable of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: So, this isn't really a women's rights issue?\par \par \uc2 BRIDGES: We can recognize that this impacts women while also recognizing that it impacts other groups. Those things are not mutually exclusive, Sen. Hawley.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: So, your view is, is that the core of this right then is about what?\par \par \uc2 BRIDGES: So, I want to recognize that your line of questioning is transphobic and it opens up trans people to violence. Denying that trans people exist and pretending not to know that they exist.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: I'm denying that trans people exist by asking you if you are talking about women having pregnancies?\par \par \uc2 BRIDGES: Are you? Are you? Are you? Do you believe that men can get pregnant?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: No, I don't think men can get pregnant.\par \par \uc2 BRIDGES: So, you are denying that trans people exist.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: How long did that woman spend in the North Korean brainwashing camp? How long would she hesitate before killing you? Not long.\par \par \uc2 So, here she is telling Sen. Hawley, "Stop defending the matriarchy, Senator. Abortion is between a man and his doctor. Hands off men's bodies. Abortion is for the men." Well, the media agree, by the way.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ZINHLE ESSAMUAH, MSNBC REPORTER: So, we've all been talking about what the Dobbs decision means for women, but it also matters for non-binary and trans-birthing people.\par \par \uc2 So, I went to Atlanta, Georgia, to hear from one trans man about his experience with abortion.\par \par \uc2 REP. DAN BISHOP (R-NC): Do you believe that men can become pregnant and have abortions?\par \par \uc2 AIMEE ARRAMBIDE, ABORTION ACTIVIST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 REP. CORI BUSH (D-MO): Trans men and non-binary people do become pregnant.\par \par \uc2 COLLEEN MCNICHOLAS, PLANNED PARENTHOOD: So long as you have a uterus, you have the capability of getting pregnant, and if you think that accessing abortion care is stigmatizing when you present as a woman, imagine what it is when you're presenting as your authentic male self.\par \par \uc2 REP. RO KHANNA (D-CA): I appreciate your mentioning that there are transgender men and non-binary individuals who rely on reproductive health services and abortion services.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Somewhere at the University of Alabama, those fraternity brothers are throwing in another dip and howling. "We got them to make abortion all about men's bodies. We got them to watch TikTok videos where some dude lectures them about menstrual cramps. We got them to give all the ladies' awards to men and feel virtuous as they were doing it." It is the funniest practical joke ever.\par \par \uc2 Of course, it eliminated an entire category of humanity: Women. So where are the defenders of women? You remember Gloria Steinem famously said, "If men could get pregnant, abortion would be a sacrament." Now she's going to House hearings saying men can get pregnant.\par \par \uc2 So Kara Dansky probably doesn't vote for the same people we vote for, but she is one of the only people we know who has persistently defended the rights of women to exist and we are grateful for that. She is President of the US Chapter of Women's Declaration International, author of the book, "The Abolition of Sex." She joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Kara Dansky, thanks for coming on. And I'm sorry to make fun of it, because it is, of course going to destroy civilization itself. But it is kind of amazing that all of these self-aware, well-educated people are saying this stuff that actually is a huge middle finger in the face of women, everywhere.\par \par \uc2 KARA DANSKY, WOMEN'S DECLARATION INTERNATIONAL: It is. It's horrible. Thanks so much for having me.\par \par \uc2 Giving Women of Courage Award to a man on International Women's Day is of course appalling and disgusting to feminists, including myself, who fight for the right to privacy and safety of women and girls. And also, it's not more horrible than anything else that's gone on in terms of the erasure of women and girls throughout society.\par \par \uc2 We are all expected to accept men who claim to be women either simply by saying that they are or by undergoing hormonal and/or surgical treatment to make themselves appear maybe slightly more like women, and we're all just supposed to accept it and go along.\par \par \uc2 I do want to take quick issue with your assertion that feminism is dead. I am here to assure viewers feminism is not dead. But where I will agree with you is that mainstream feminist organizations, organizations that claim to be feminist, including organizations like Planned Parenthood, and the \uc2 National Organization for Women\uc2  , and the National Center for Lesbian Rights have completely caved to what is in effect, an industry fueled men's rights movement. So I'll agree with you on that.\par \par \uc2 But there are those of us on the political left who call ourselves radical feminists and we will not stop fighting for women and girls.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Do you think the -- I mean, the average person on any issue has no voice at all in this country. And that's, I think, becoming more true with the day. But do you think the average woman sees this as insulting?\par \par \uc2 As a man I can as -- who actually likes women -- this seems like the most insulting possible thing I can imagine. Do you think it's perceived that way?\par \par \uc2 DANSKY: I do and you know the other day I came across a really interesting polling that suggested that people who consider themselves to be either very liberal or liberal, around 70 to 75 percent know that sex is real, know that sex doesn't change.\par \par \uc2 So when you're referring to liberals going along with this, of course, you're absolutely right that the Democratic Party is pushing this, and the sort of Democratic liberal elite is pushing this, but ordinary Americans across the political spectrum are not going along and yes, I absolutely think that ordinary average American women see this as insulting.\par \par \uc2 What they may not realize, though, is that it's no more insulting than the so-called trans movement has been to women and girls for years now.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That's right. That's right. And I appreciate you're saying so. I know it's probably not a natural move to come on the show, but we're grateful that you do.\par \par \uc2 Kara Dansky, thank you.\par \par \uc2 DANSKY: Thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So last night we talked to a lawyer who represented January 6th defendant, Jacob Chansley, the so-called QAnon Shaman. The lawyer told us that the government, the prosecutors in this case, in violation of the Constitution, hid exculpatory evidence from him and the defense in order to send Jacob Chansley to prison for four years where he is tonight.\par \par \uc2 Now, we showed you that evidence this week. It is surveillance footage that shows Federal officers leading Jacob Chansley around the Capitol like tour guides. At one point, they even opened the door of the hollowed Senate Chamber for him and usher him in.\par \par \uc2 So the tape proves conclusively that Jacob Chansley, whose every action inside the building was videotaped, committed no felony. And the government hid that fact, and because they did, the media were allowed to paint Jacob Chansley as a dangerous terrorist who deserve to be killed.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 STEVE SCHMIDT, THE LINCOLN PROJECT: I think the most amazing thing about the whole thing is watching the video, and on the Senate floor, there's a cop who's armed and a guy bursts in, the QAnon Shaman, dressed like a Viking and he basically talks to him.\par \par \uc2 I'm watching, "Shoot him. Shoot him," like if you burst into the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  , if he was dressed like Bin Laden, would he have shot him?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Imagine if they said that about someone you loved.\par \par \uc2 Well, now we know that the Biden administration created that perception that this man should be killed and then broke the law specifically to destroy the life of American citizen and naval veteran, Jacob Chansley, who again remains in prison tonight.\par \par \uc2 The question is what happens next?\par \par \uc2 Martha Chansley is Jacob Chansley's mother; William 