 House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , he's not at fault. It's not his problem. We didn't have this problem when the last administration.\par \par \uc2 Biden ended almost all of Trump's border protections and halted construction of the border wall ended to stay in Mexico policy and told illegal immigrants, come one, come mall. There's no vetting, not even vetting during a pandemic as far as health issues.\par \par \uc2 Now, according to DHS Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, his boss \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , he is just not responsible. No. You'll never guess what really is responsible -- climate change. He thinks -- no, he thinks there are climate refugees all over the world and there is just nothing that the president can do about it. It's the climate's fault.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, DHS SECRETARY: When we speak about the border, we have to put it in context, that this is not a challenge and it is indeed a challenge. Not a challenge exclusive to the United States.\par \par \uc2 You know, Chile just deployed its military to its border. Colombia has 2.5 million Venezuelans within its borders. Costa Rica's population is increasingly Nicaraguan. We are seeing a movement of people throughout the hemisphere and quite frankly throughout the world that is historic.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wait a second, aren't these the same people that tell us again and again and again that your border is secure? That's what I recall. Do you recall that?\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INTERVIEWER: It sounds to most folks like a crisis.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Well, look, it's way down now. We've now gotten control.\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: Precisely that the border is closed.\par \par \uc2 Nor could I have been clearer and continue to be so which is the border is closed.\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: The United States will continue to enforce our laws and secure our border.\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS: The border, we are working to make the border more secure.\par \par \uc2 INTERVIEWER: You're confident this border is secure?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: We have a secure border in that that is a priority for any nation, including ours and our administration.\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: We agree that the border is secure.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, okay. Now, of course, it's not just who crosses the borders unlawfully. By the way, think of all the drugs that cross that border, lethal drugs pouring into our country and this leads us to yet another Biden record and that is the number of fentanyl deaths. More Americans sadly are now dying from fentanyl than ever before.\par \par \uc2 Now keep in mind, most of that fentanyl that is made in China, it is shipped to Mexico, smuggled across the wide open southern border, a record 100,000 plus Americans died from drug overdoses in just the last year. This current federal government is now controlled by a group of woke idiots and now, what, there are really only with a few things certain in Biden's America?\par \par \uc2 Let's see. We get record inflation. Debt -- that's guaranteed in anybody's America. Higher taxes for every American.\par \par \uc2 Now, as we speak, excess deaths are at a record high, even though the pandemic is in the rear view mirror. And Americans are now paying more taxes than they've ever paid before. This includes the new taxes that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just implemented, $225 billion corporate tax hike on corporations that will get passed on to you the consumer. I make the case all the time, corporations don't pay taxes. Okay, they charge more for their goods and services. It's that simple, we pay it.\par \par \uc2 Now, Joe's $71 billion tax on your retirement funds, okay, you save for retirement. Now, we're going to tax that. And Joe's multi-billion dollar tax on those who end up powering their homes with natural gas, Joe's $12 billion tax on crude oil, Joe's billion dollar tax on coal.\par \par \uc2 Guess what? All the people in this country are impacted by this and Joe promised he'd never raise taxes on any American that made under four hundred thousand dollars a year. Now the war on American energy doesn't stop there. Biden is reportedly now set to reject what is a massive new oil and gas project in Alaska. Now at the same time, Biden opened up oil imports from the hostile regime socialist nation of Venezuela where we now buy three million barrels of crude oil every single month.\par \par \uc2 Now, Joe is impoverishing you and your families and making countries what like Venezuela and China and Russia rich again? Does that make sense? We have high paying career jobs. It's good for our national security. And guess what? It is the lifeblood of the world's economy.\par \par \uc2 And don't forget, importing oil comes with a cost. That cost is passed on to you, the American people. In other words, a hidden tax on every single gallon of gas that you buy. It also raises the cost of heating and cooling your home.\par \par \uc2 And now, yet another tax hike after blasting Republicans over that secret plan to upend Medicare. Remember during the State of the Union Address, Biden now wants to increase taxes on Medicare.\par \par \uc2 So it turns out \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was right. There were people in Washington with a secret plan. It was him. He has a secret plan to increase the cost of Medicare.\par \par \uc2 At the very same time, Joe wants to give government workers what it will be the largest pay increase in 43 years. By the way, if you work for the government, you already make more money on average than people in the private sector.\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, Biden already gifted $36 billion of your dollars to the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  to bail out their badly managed pension fund. It was the largest private pension bailout in the history of the country. But what is a few billion dollars among friends, right?\par \par \uc2 Keep in mind, the teamsters union, they extort blue collar workers. They then donate that money to elect Democrats like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But today on Capitol Hill, well, the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  president accused Republican Senator \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  of being greedy. Why? Because Mullin owned a family business.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARKWAYNE MULLIN (R-OK): What job have you created, one job, other than sucking a paycheck out of somebody -- somebody else that you want to say that you're trying to provide because you're forcing them to pay dues?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No, we don't force them. You're out of line, man.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: Don't tell me I'm out of line.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You're out of line.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: Don't tell me --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: Shut your mouth.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You're telling me to shut my mouth?\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: Yes, I did.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Hold it, hold it.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: You haven't created a job.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We haven't?\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: You haven't been there. You haven't.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sure, we have.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: You haven't.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sure, we have.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: Tell me one job that you created.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIIFED MALE: What are you talking about -- be specific.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: You're an employer? Do you employ people?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No, I'm not an employer, no, it's funny, we created opportunity.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: That's not creating jobs.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We created opportunity because we hold greedy CEOs like yourself accountable.\par \par \uc2 MULLIN: That's -- you call