sidency has been a train wreck and that's why even Democrats, they are very hesitant to support \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for a second term. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Would you support President Biden running for re- election in '24?\par \par \uc2 SEN. MAZIE HIRONO (D-HI): If he runs for a re-election, sure.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: In that same vein --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Are you going to endorse \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  if he runs for reelection?\par \par \uc2 SEN. JOE MANCHIN (D-WV): Oh, there's plenty of time for the election. This is the problem with America right now. We start an election every time there's a cycle.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: He's the leader of your party.\par \par \uc2 MANCHIN: I -- no, the bottom line is let's see who's involved. Let's wait until we see who all the players are. Let's just wait until it all comes out.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Doesn't sound very confident to me.\par \par \uc2 All right. Whoever gets nominated in the Democratic Party will be bolstered by a system of legal ballot harvesting. Now, Biden is now accused of weaponizing voter turnout unlawfully on the federal level with an executive order that enables the \uc2 USCIS\uc2  to register new citizens at naturalization services, as well as the Department of Education to push voter registration to any student taking out a college loan. And that's not all.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department is now getting voter information to federal prisoners. That's what they get. They get to vote from jail, put it in a drop box, God knows where it's going to end up. Anyway, according to the former President Trump, the best way now to counter these efforts, and Republicans, you better pay attention, you better adapt, and you better adjust, you better get over your reluctance and resistance to voting by mail and voting early and you better meet and probably defeat the Democratic efforts at legal ballot harvesting based on state law.\par \par \uc2 These efforts by the way is the only way you'll get in a game or otherwise you'll you start out Election Day down, you know, 500,000 votes. That's hard to make up on Election Day. Anyway, take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT: Many states have banned ballot harvesting to keep our elections honest and fair, but in the states where ballot harvesting is still legal, we have no choice but to beat the Democrats at their own game. It's very simple. Either we start ballot harvesting or you can say goodbye to our country. You can just wave goodbye, because Democrats would win every single election. We have to get smart.\par \par \uc2 With your help, we will master the Democrats game of ballot harvesting and we will win back the White House from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the people that are destroying our country. They're absolutely destroying America. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Here with reaction, the author of the big new book "Serenity in the Storm: Living Through Chaos by Leaning on Christ", \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2  is with us. Also FOX News contributor Tammy Bruce, the host -- the co-host of the hit show "The Five", our friend Geraldo Rivera.\par \par \uc2 All right. Geraldo, I know you really -- why does this family -- this is what really bothered me.\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, CO-HOST OF "THE FIVE": Did you leave out Tammy?\par \par \uc2 TAMMY BRUCE, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: No, he said -- there was some other applause that was fabulous.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I was clapping over you.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Before I get to the political issues, explain to me why does \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  not recognize his own granddaughter?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: It's terrible. It's really low. I think that there's some -- there's a special place in hell for people who ignore children --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So you think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going to hell? Is that what you're saying?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Because I think that he will do the decent righteous thing eventually and I think that you have to remember that it's, first of all --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He's 80 and the kids four years old.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I'm a happy grandfather of five kids. I love my grandchildren. The Biden family will ultimately I hope come around because this child did nothing wrong.\par \par \uc2 It's a dirt bag. \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is a dirt bag. \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is a junkie. Here's all of those things, at least he was.\par \par \uc2 But the one thing I will say and this will get you make you mad at me --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's not hard.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: That's a unique thing. It's four and a half years and no one has proven international money laundering yet. No one has proven foreign influence peddling yet. Those are the big things. He's a bad person.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Geraldo, don't you want to know -- doesn't everybody in America deserve to know how much money in business that the Bidens did with the communist Chinese, with the Russians, with Ukraine? How does \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  with no experience --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: The Delaware U.S. attorney has been investigating him since they've come up with what?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They've come up with a corrupt system that doesn't indict Democrats, that's what they come up with.\par \par \uc2 Kayleigh, let me go to you, because we already know Hunter went on GMA, said he had no experience in Ukraine, oil, gas, energy. Why are you getting paid all this money? He said, I don't know. Maybe because your father is the vice president? Probably.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEIGH MCENANY\uc2 , "OUTNUMBERED" CO-HOST: Right. Exactly, I mean, that's what we call common sense and short supply in the Democrat Party. That's common sense.\par \par \uc2 We know the U.S. attorney's Delaware investigation, they don't come out and publicize what they're finding. They don't publicize what happens in the grand jury. But we know that a very specific -- question was asked in the grand jury, who is the big guy? The big guy was getting 10 percent.\par \par \uc2 And I asked a Democrat on "Outnumbered" if not \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , then who is the big guy? It directly implicates \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and I failed -- maybe Geraldo knows. I don't know who else could be the big guy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Do you know what else was in there? He complained to his own daughter about having to give half his income to pops. He complained -- Hunter complained bitterly about having to pay for Joe's home repairs. That sounds like he's implicating his own father, Tammy.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: It does and while it sounds like all this is about Hunter, he is simply a representation of a level of corruption in an entire family, because all these things we discuss. We also know there is Jill -- Jill Biden who I for a while thought she was like the decent person in which she would stop her husband from being abused in the system and he wouldn't even really run the first time, boy, was I wrong. I was wrong about her.\par \par \uc2 So you've got this entire system that where they're all invested in this kind of corruption because if there's anyone who's going to say, pay for the kid's upbringing, it should be Jill Biden, and clearly, there doesn't seem to be that kind of impression being made.\par \par \uc2 So, Americans, we look at this and this is about the system in general. He's been in office, Biden has, for 50 years. This is kind of a system -- a family system but it's also a political system that has been benefiting with corruption for far too long and explains why you can go into public service and have three homes, beach homes and millions of dollars and because how does that work?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Where's the illegality, Tammy? That's the point.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: