 not your heart be troubled, Laura Ingraham and I will do an audience show together, I'm not sure when. We'll invite Tucker, too.\par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020230309ej3800001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Dodges Question On Re-Election Announcement\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Tom Lahren, Joe Concha, Charlie Hurt, Sean Duffy \par \uc2 7,963 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 March 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Wow. What a great audience. Happy Friday, everybody, right? We made it.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for being here. We love having you.\par \par \uc2 We are back with our live studio audience. By the way, coming up tonight right here in studio, Congressman Jim Jordan of Ohio will be here.\par \par \uc2 Also, we have our -- right? You're doing a great job.\par \par \uc2 Along with our great, great American panel. Later, more explosive whistleblower testimony about how our DOJ has been weaponized.\par \par \uc2 Also, AOC is having a little bit of trouble. She might be in legal trouble. We'll explain straight ahead. And I may even shock you and defend her.\par \par \uc2 Hold on. You don't know what I'm going to do yet. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 All right. But first \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , well, he is continuing to keep us all in suspense and waiting. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Beg your pardon?\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: When will you announce your reelection, sir?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: When I announce it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANINTY: I don't think he knows it's Friday.\par \par \uc2 Now, the 80-year-old sitting president just won't say whether he plans to run for a second term, although his wife Jill said it for him. That does not exactly inspire any confidence in me. But if he ultimately does decide to run, it looks like it'll be back to the basement bunker for Joey who is reportedly now enlisting prominent Democrats to travel and speak on his behalf, because he's likely not capable.\par \par \uc2 Look at this number. Already 68 percent of you, the American people, think that Joe is way too old to run for reelection and in a poll released only last month, 16, that's it, only 16 percent said that they were better off financially under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, remember, with or without Biden, the 2024 election is well underway. Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO CLIP PLAYS)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just released that ad. Now, he did announce his bid last November. We also have Nikki Haley. We have \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  who's running. A few others are officially in the race.\par \par \uc2 Look for Senator Tim Scott, former VP \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former Secretary of State \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 , possibly Virginia Governor Glenn Youngkin, \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , New Hampshire Governor Sununu, all possible contenders and we will know by this time next year who's likely to get the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, both DeSantis and Trump are poised to visit Iowa this month. That is the site of the first Republican caucus. In multiple polls now, the duo are leading one and two, the Republican field with Trump as latest FOX News poll in first place. And while Republicans are moving full steam ahead, Democrats, they are in complete disarray.\par \par \uc2 Now with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's approval rating underwater, he is in deep trouble, and by the way, seeking a second term is not exciting pretty much anybody.\par \par \uc2 But as they say, you can't teach an old dog. You're dying -- what was it, a lying dog face pony show something? I forgot. Yeah, exactly.\par \par \uc2 You can't teach an old dog new tricks. But despite his tanking poll numbers, Biden is doubling and tripling down on his awful policies. New, today and accidentally leaked internal memo from the administration showing that Biden is prioritizing once again climate considerations over quote greater energy security. Wow, that compromises our national security.\par \par \uc2 Remember, oil, gas, coal is the lifeblood of our economy, period, end of sentence. And also new today, he announced another aid package to Ukraine, this time another $400 million of your dollars. Now, Biden refuses to allow Ukraine to have sophisticated warplanes that has been offered by other European countries. That would put them on in parity with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and could possibly hopefully end the war quickly.\par \par \uc2 Instead, he's funding what is now becoming a deadly quagmire all at your expense, even saying this war may go on three more years from today. Now, clearly, we have not learned from Iraq or Afghanistan, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is clearly not fighting or allowing the Ukrainians to fight and win. He's not allowing Ukraine to fight and win and Europe is now paying next to nothing compared to the American taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 Now, if you're not going to fight a war to win the war stop wasting the American taxpayers' dollars now, right? If you're going to fight, fight to win.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  beat the caliphate because he fought to win and he bombed the living hell out of them, and he did win the war. But the -- right? It worked.\par \par \uc2 But the reckless spending doesn't stop there. Joe continues to push his very unconstitutional plan to pay off student loans with your hard-earned tax dollars. Don't you love this idea, you empower your government to take other people's money to pay for a loan that you signed your name on that you said you would pay back. Why should someone else have to pay back your loan? Anyway, it's so bad that even "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ", they were forced to question the plan's legality.\par \par \uc2 And meanwhile, his own party is now turning against them. House Democrats feel betrayed by his apparent flip-flop on the D.C. crime bill which would significantly reduce penalties for violent criminals.\par \par \uc2 AOC publicly criticized Biden over his change of heart, to her millions of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers and privately, it's even worse because according to one House Democrat, quote, hundreds of his colleagues are panicking over the prospect of a weak, frail, cognitive mess who will be 82 years old if he runs again.\par \par \uc2 But even as the crisis pile up, well, Joe is once again off to Delaware for the weekend, of course, he is, for much needed R&R. But we don't know and won't know who he's going to be meeting. We never know that question, an answer to that question.\par \par \uc2 Anyway and that brings us to the Biden blunders of the week. You're going to love it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: By the way, there's an awful lot of really good Republicans but the MAGA Republicans are a different breed of cat. No, they're not bad or good. They're very different.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, you know I'm not -- I may be a white boy but I'm not stupid. But I'm not joking.\par \par \uc2 If they have to pay out $159 billion dollars let -- less.\par \par \uc2 You think I'm joking.\par \par \uc2 I want to make it clear, I'm going to raise some taxes. I'm going to raise some taxes.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: When will you announce your reelection, sir?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: When I announce it.\par \par \uc2 If you think I'm joking, I'm not.\par \par \uc2 And I met a nurse named Pearl Nelson, military. She'd come in and do things that I don't think can learn the medical school -- nursing school. She'd whisper in my ear, I didn't -- couldn't understand, she whispered and she leaned down, and actually breathed on me.\par \par \uc2 Look, folks -- anyway I don't want to get started.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's your president. Now, when Biden wasn't mumbling, bumbling, stumbling around this week, he was laughing about children dying from fentanyl. Take a look at this shocking and frankly disgusting video. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: A little bit of more \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and a few more, you're going to have a lot of Republicans running our way. I was the reason she was -- she was very specific. I shouldn't aggress probably.\par \par \uc2 I've read she -- she was very specific recently, saying that a mom, a poor mother who lost two kids to fentanyl, that that I killed her sons. Well, the interesting thing is that fentanyl they took came during the last administration. Look, folks -- anyway, I don't want to get started.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Can't help himself.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's give a warm Friday welcome to our great, great American panel. Outkick host Tomi Lahren, FOX News contributors Charlie Hurt and Joe Concha.\par \par \uc2 Thanks, guys. Good to see you. Thanks for coming, Joe. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 So, 68 percent of Americans don't want them to run, only 16 percent of them of Americans give him a decent grade on the economy. the question is will he run and is he qualified to do another term? I don't believe he is.\par \par \uc2 TOMI LAHREN, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: I don't think any of us believe he is, including the Democrats but they're in a really tricky position because if not Joe, they have pigeonholed themselves with this diversity index into having to choose \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and she doesn't have the excuse of dementia and her age. She has no excuse other than she just does a really poor job at her job.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Can you explain why she giggles at all the inappropriate moments?\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: Well, as you saw, Joe just did that too. Apparently, there's something in the water that they've both been drinking, though they haven't had the time to go to East Palestine, by the way, people are actually drinking toxic water or maybe in breathing toxic fumes.\par \par \uc2 But this is what the Democrats don't want. They don't want to have to elevate Kamala, so they will go with their Trojan horse, hope that he can make it through a debate, hope he can make it through an election, hide him as much as possible. They're in a bad spot.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, Joe, I was going to wait to begin our 2024 coverage, but every single person I talk to, that's all they want to talk about right now, and Republicans and conservatives around the country, they feel we are deteriorating very quickly, yeah, and they want to get the country back on track and it's not going to happen with these you know climate alarmists in charge.\par \par \uc2 JOE CONCHA, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, the election is right around the corner. It's about 700 days away. So we're going to be talking about that a lot.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: This time next year, we'll be right in the middle of Super Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: That's exactly right. So that'll go by pretty quickly.\par \par \uc2 Look, I think this president does run again. And by the way, this is a commander-in-chief that works 24/7. All right? That's -- I'm serious. That's 24 hours a week, seven months a year.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think you'd be a little generous on the seven months a year. All right. that was well done, well said.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Thank you. But \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2  gave the game away recently. He said as I did in 1988, 2008, and 2020, I look forward to being on your side, Mr. President, when you run in 2024. That's why Klain left. He's out to run his campaign.\par \par \uc2 So, but to your point, if not the cackler in chief in terms of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , then you have \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  whose bumper sticker will be, I'll do to America what I did to California which probably isn't the bumper sticker you want.\par \par \uc2 And then Spartacus, my senator from New Jersey, \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , you know? He might surprise you. And then --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But oh, wait, I can outdo him? Guess who my congressman is? George Santos.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Oh, wow. He says he's ready for re-election.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, yeah.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Yeah, hubris on that guy. But the only person to declare so far in the Democratic side, \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2 , all right? So keep an eye on her.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I would.\par \par \uc2 All right. So as this is now developing before our eyes, Charlie, where do you -- where do you think we're going to be one year from now?\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Oh, I think -- well, first of all, I think the Republican -- on the Republican side, it's going to be a magnificent fight. I think it's going to be a great fight. I think you're going to -- it's going to demonstrate yet again that all of the ideas, all the honest debate that's going on in politics is all on the Republican side. There is no honest debate going on in the Democrat side.\par \par \uc2 I do think that -- I do I agree with you, I think that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  winds up running, and I think that -- you know, it's kind of interesting, he has -- he has given the store away to the left-wing lunatics of his party and that's how he keeps -- he's kind of kept a serious challenge from a Bernie Sanders or some other kook like that from coming to his left.\par \par \uc2 The problem is that, of course, these policies are horrifically unpopular and they're actually punishing Americans and actually hurting them. So, so, I think he lit -- you know, a year from now, he's going to be limping along, and we're going to be watching over on the Republican side, a really great, marvelous, adult debate about ideas that Americans people care.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: One of the reasons I love ice hockey and I played ice hockey as a kid is they still allow fighting.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So I love fighting. I like debates. I would rather though for the Republicans that they unite a little bit more and not make it a war, but ultimately, we know where it's headed, it's going to be war.\par \par \uc2 HURT: But if you care about the ideas and I know you do --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I do.\par \par \uc2 HURT: -- then at the end of the day, I think a fight, you know, it's like a fight between brothers. At the end of the day, you get the fight, you get all your testosterone out and then you come together.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And that's why I train mixed martial arts for that reason.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How bad will it get, Tommy?\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: I fear for how bad it's going to get. I hope that it can be -- I'll tell you this.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: I've been a Trump supporter for a long time, 2016, 2020. If he's our nominee, I'll go harder for him than I ever have before.\par \par \uc2 I will say this though, what Trump needs to convince his supporters of is that he can win an election. He needs to do that. Instead of just taking cheap shots at \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , he needs to say, I can win more so than \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But I think we all know no matter who jumps into this race, it is Ron versus Don. That is it. Everybody else is in there to raise their name ID. None of them are going to be serious contenders.\par \par \uc2 We're waiting for that battle royale and we hope that the best man with the best policies wins, and then the other one joined together and let's take back the White House.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Well done.\par \par \uc2 The challenge and I've seen it on your show, the challenge for those running against Trump right now, you asked Nikki Haley, where do you differ from the former president on policy, and she really couldn't answer the question. And how will \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2  say he -- if he runs, he probably will - - say he differs from Trump? How will DeSantis when you look at Florida, it's hard to see DeSantis doing anything really different from whatever \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did when he was president?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: The agenda is set. It's a matter of the personality, or the person.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Correct, that's what's going to come down.\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: Winnability is what it's going to come down.\par \par \uc2 HURT: It's still the Trump party because of the issues that Trump brought to the table and Trump alone brought to the table the politicians in both parties had ignored for so long. And it does come down to who people think is going to be the better, smarter fighter.\par \par \uc2 And like you say, Tomi, who's going to win and then be that fighter.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So you think -- you think it's about electability? You all three agree it's about electability.\par \par \uc2 HURT: I think it's about electability and but more important than that is the willingness, the steel spine to stand up to these people. And we saw what these people did in the media and in Washington to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in his first term, and who has the guts to stand up to these people and get rid of all of them.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. So let me ask this question. I've never witnessed in my lifetime any one politician be smeared, slandered, besmirched, attacked like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been. I've never seen this witness this in my life. Whoever the nominee is, it will happen to that nominee, if it is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How much will the American people factor in the unfairness of the never- ending attacks against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in terms of why he's combative, why he sends out those tweets, why he fights as hard as he does, because he's attacked more than anybody. How much will that factor in people's minds?\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: I think it also helps him because the Trump loyalists are going to be loyal to Trump because they want to avenge 2020. So as much as we know the media lies on Trump more than anybody else and he's had to fight battle after battle, unfair hurdle after unfair hurdle, I think that that is also galvanized a lot of support behind him, people that want to see him get that revenge.\par \par \uc2 But is that best for our country? We're going to have to decide.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, let me then follow up and ask you this, what would you advise him in terms of that electability question you brought up?\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: You know, a leopard can't change its spots. Trump is going to have to stay Trump. We just hope that he fights the left and he fights the drug cartels and he fights China. Don't fight \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , because \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  at the end of the day is a Trump supporter, so you don't need to fight him. We need him, no matter which one is the nominee, we need them both.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is still going to be the future of our party, whether he runs in as our nominee or not. He is still someone that we need. So I would tell Trump, don't cut him off at the knees, even if you want to be the nominee because we still need \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . You are stronger.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: As much as you we could talk about they should all be united and all be friendly, when it comes to South Carolina, it is going to be World War III politically. It just always is. Look at McCain and \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 , that's true.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: DeSantis at this point, I don't know if you can keep this up, he's following the Reagan rule. Which is thou shalt not speak ill of another Republican. He says I'm not here to smear Republicans.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Is that a smart strategy?\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Yes, it is because he could run on his record and he has a record to run on.\par \par \uc2 But if DeSantis is the nominee, you said Trump had it bad, DeSantis will get it just as bad. We're already seeing it with the coverage of "don't say gay", for example, which it's not called --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's one example and I saw twice this week, people trying to label him a racist, just outright lying about him.\par \par \uc2 HURT: Which oddly is sort of an argument in favor of Trump again because it, you know, this idea that, oh, no, we're going to play nice if it's just not Trump, just don't go with Trump. No, you're not. You're going to smear anybody Republicans put forward. So why not go with Trump? Just put the lever down.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So if peace -- if peace and prosperity generally win out in terms of election issues, who do you think will -- if we look at world leaders like President Xi or President Putin, they're both dictators, who would they fear the most in the Republican -- of the Republican candidates?\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: They already feared \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I think they would also fear \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  because \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has a backbone like Trump. Whether they have the same amount of backbone, that's going to be seen when we see an announcement from \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , when we see how he battles Trump.\par \par \uc2 But I think that \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is so strong. It has been so strong in Florida, in the face of \uc2 Disney\uc2 , in the face of the culture wars, in the face of COVID lockdown policy. He has been that strong leader. I think he's going to be that leader.\par \par \uc2 But none of this matters unless Republicans figure out how to ballot a harvest and play the game.\par \par \uc2 HANN