s, or protests, or criticism because you happen to share the last name of the former president?\par \par \uc2 CHERISE TRUMP: Laura, I've been doing this for two years now, and actually it is the first time that I've actually been ever asked to get liability insurance or that there has ever been elevated risk to any event. Most people just ask me, and I say no, and then we move on, and that's the end of the conversation. So it is a bit ridiculous that they went to these extra measures. And again, it just shows how afraid they are of the woke mob and how little effort they plan to put in place to actually deter the mob from taking over the school.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Maybe it's actually time for a little lesson in common sense, pragmatism, clear thinking, objectivity, common sense. This would be a good moment to try to teach young people that it's OK, free speech won't hurt you, it's speech, and names don't bite, OK? Names don't bite. Cheris, this was wild. I didn't believe it when I heard it. Thank you so much, and good luck to you.\par \par \uc2 Now, speaking of campus insanity, the state of Florida is fighting back. The board of trustees at the New College of Florida voted Tuesday to abolish the school's DEI office. Joining me now is board member Chris Rufo. He's also a senior fellow at the Manhattan Institute, contributing editor for "City Journal."\par \par \uc2 Chris, you tweeted last night that mothers of college students, they are actually showing up at these board meetings and dressing up in "Handmaid's Tale" outfits? What the heck? What is going on?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUFO, MANHATTAN INSTITUTE SENIOR FELLOW: Yes. Well, it was quite a dramatic night. We became the first University in America to abolish its DEI program which was trafficking in race-based discrimination, categorizing people and demonizing on the basis of skin color, and in some Florida public universities they're actually offering racially segregated scholarships.\par \par \uc2 So we said not New College. We are abolishing the department. We are prohibiting that kind of programming. And I thought maybe students would be protesting on their own behalf as they did in the 1960s, but now actually it's the students' mothers. They are coming in, they're dressed up in costumes. They're totally hysterical, screaming into the microphone. And I think it really shows this kind of bizarre change in our society where we have helicopter parenting, we have extreme coddling to the point where, look, I would be mortified if my mom had come to my college to protest.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Mommie.\par \par \uc2 RUFO: And for these folks, this is now the status quo. It's quite something to see.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, the kids are already spoiled and indulged by their parents, and now their parents even have to protest for them. At least you could be self-respecting and do your own protest, Chris.\par \par \uc2 There is another college in Florida that isn't taking the same road that New College is. You've got documents from something called \uc2 Florida International University\uc2  -- I've never heard of it -- exposing its social justice badge program? Sounds like a social credit system. What is this?\par \par \uc2 RUFO: Yes, well, \uc2 Florida International University\uc2  has actually 40,000 students, it's a huge public university. I found documents according to their sunshine laws that show that they are dividing students along racial lines. They're actually holding racially segregated training programs telling white students they're oppressors, telling minority students that they are oppressed, and then actually encouraging and training students to become social justice warriors, teaching them how to participate in violent leftwing protests like BLM marches, even teaching them how to prevent teargas from affecting them, how to use encrypted communication. It's all out in the open. They're explicitly turning universities into factories for training leftwing activists. And luckily Governor DeSantis is putting forth legislation with the legislature to stop this kind of programming dead in his tracks.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We are learning from America First Legal tonight that we actually may be seeing because of the way they are fudging the equity mission they have, we may be seeing a time where our \uc2 IRS\uc2  targets people for audits disproportionately who are Asian and white to make things more even, because I guess they believe Asians and whites, they have an unfair advantage, so they are going to get audited more. Could that be what we are facing? Could that be where we're going here?\par \par \uc2 RUFO: That's absolutely plausible. And it's not just where we're going. It's actually where we are today. Universities punish whites and Asians for admissions, for scholarships, for other opportunities. You have DEI committees that advance hiring through these diversity statement filters that, again, punish white men, Asian men in particular. This is what equity means. Equity means treating people differently on the basis of their group identity. So nobody should be surprised that Biden administration is taking these policies of open determination and embedding them everywhere.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, using DEI to target, not just reward, targeting people. Chris, thank you for your work.\par \par \uc2 Now, breaking just moments ago, we are getting some horrific reports out of Chicago about an officer just shot. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I will try to get through this. It's a very difficult time for the \uc2 Chicago Police Department\uc2  . We are heartbroken. Unfortunately, we are delivering the very tragic news that one of our on-duty Chicago police officers has been fatally shot this evening.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The deceased officer was responding reports of a person with a firearm, and the 911 caller said that a man was chasing a woman down the street with a gun. When approached, the suspect ran and shot the officer multiple times, turned around. The officer was on a force for five years, reportedly comes from a family of public servants. We are praying for this officer, his family, and the entire city of Chicago.\par \par \uc2 "GUTFELD!" next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020230302ej3100001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Chuckles When Talking About A Woman Who Lost Two Children To Fentanyl\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Jeanine Pirro, Kellyanne Conway, Gianno Caldwell,  Dagen McDowell, Sean Duffy, Tom Shillue \par \uc2 7,822 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 March 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Tucker, thank you. How are you? Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST, "TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT": So great.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Say hi to Tucker, everybody.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Wow, wow, we got a great crowd.\par \par \uc2 All right. Welcome to HANNITY. Yes, we are back with a live studio audience.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, wow, look at this crowd.\par \par \uc2 Did you all have caffeine before the show because you're all wired? I love that. That's great.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, Judge Jeanine Pirro, Kellyanne Conway, former Congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , all in studio tonight, and our great, great American panel.\par \par \uc2 Later, we have a shocking, really despicable disgusting video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  actually laughing at Americans killed by fentanyl. We'll play -- yeah, yeah, I know. We'll play that tape.\par \par \uc2 Plus, we'll hear from two former \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents, whistleblowers, that left America's once premier law enforcement agency because of the bureau's political rot. That's coming up.\par \par \uc2 Also make no mistake, justice in this country is no longer blind. This is very sad for this country. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  has, in fact, been politicized and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the DOJ have both been weaponized. It is sad, but this is very, very real and needs to be dealt with. In fact, they actively now and knowingly are putting their thumb on the scale. They've done it now in every major election since 2016, including 2016.\par \par \uc2 But that's news apparently to \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  who's on Capitol Hill today. Take a look at this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHRISTOPHER WRAY\uc2 , FBI DIRECTOR: You know, I hear these claims of politicization but I can tell you that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is and it's going to stay independent, and that means following the facts wherever they lead no matter who likes it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And I can tell you that is not true, unless of course the facts could negatively impact a prominent Democrat, with the last name Clinton or Biden. Wray is either lying or living on another planet.\par \par \uc2 Now, remember, according to \uc2 Jim Comey\uc2 , no reasonable prosecutor would ever bring charges against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . She had all that top secret classified information on her servers after she was caught mishandling a ton of top secret material. And then, of course, she destroyed evidence, the 33,000 emails. We had never heard of Bleach Bit before. Everybody now knows what Bleach Bit is.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, then there were Blackberries and iPhones that were smashed with hammers and, of course, they also removed SIM cards so you could never recover any information on those Blackberries and iPhones.\par \par \uc2 Now, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  never bothered to raid \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 's Chappaqua mansion. I wonder why. Hannity, they didn't want to see me, that's why. Why didn't they raid that?\par \par \uc2 More recently, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  never bothered to conduct a search warrant at any of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's properties after top secret documents turned up here, there and pretty much everywhere \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was.\par \par \uc2 Now, apparently, early morning raids with SWAT teams, they are specifically reserved for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or his friends and associates like \uc2 Paul Manafort\uc2  or Roger Stone or other conservatives, other Republicans because we are now living in a country with a two-tiered system of justice.\par \par \uc2 Now, Director Wray had a chance to restore the integrity of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to once again make it the single premier law enforcement agency in the entire world after the disastrous tenure of \uc2 James Comey\uc2  and company. But instead, the bureaus pulled critical bias and abuse of power, it is now worse than ever.\par \par \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  is an abject failure. No America -- American should have confidence in his leadership. You decide.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: The documents investigation for former President Trump and the raid that happens in Mar-a-Lago, that show of force in that way as opposed to the documents investigation for President Biden and how that went down, you find out about those documents before the November election. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  then does the search of the house after that, but does not say anything prior to the midterm election.\par \par \uc2 WRAY: So we have a long history of handling investigations into the mishandling of classified information. And our standard for approaching those investigations is the same, no matter who it is. Our basic approach is the same.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That too is not true. That -- do you believe that true?\par \par \uc2 Equal treatment regardless of politics, he's saying, really? How do you explain then the curious case of Hunter Biden? Remember, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  got possession of the laptop from hell in December of 2019.\par \par \uc2 Now, instead of authenticating the laptop and investigating the variety of potential crimes documented on the laptop -- well, what did \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 's \uc2 FBI\uc2  do? Well, prior to the 2020 election, the bureau, they were warnings, every big tech social media company in the country, they were doing it on a weekly basis to be on high alert for foreign disinformation and it may be about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and it may even be about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So, when the very true New York post report came out about Hunter's laptop and that was released, big tech, they had already been primed week after week after week after week by \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents, people that work for \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , eagerly assuming what they were told was coming. That was some type of disinformation campaign from a foreign entity.\par \par \uc2 Well, it worked successfully because all the big tech companies, they censored the story weeks before the presidential election, which I would argue and polls have shown likely contributed to tipping the election to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Mission accomplished, right, \uc2 Chris Wray\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Now, how dirty can this get? You decide.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WRAY: The \uc2 FBI\uc2  does not and it's not in the business of functioning as the truth police.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Understood.\par \par \uc2 WRAY: We don't tell social media companies to censor anything.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, he you just told them on a weekly basis to be on the lookout, they may have misinformation about Joe and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . What do you think they were going to do as a result of that? Your \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents did it on a weekly basis. They don't tell social media companies to censor. They just feed them false information to create a false narrative, all in the hopes to shape the results of an election and the company's policies.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was doing this every single solitary week leading up to the 2020 presidential election. Not only did the \uc2 FBI\uc2  plant the seeded disinformation in big tech, but they also sat idly by and said nothing. Remember when 50 former intel officials with no proof at all whatsoever, they signed off on a letter claiming that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop has all the classic earmarks of Russian disinformation or a Russian information operation.\par \par \uc2 They had -- the \uc2 FBI\uc2  had the laptop 11 months prior to the presidential election in 2020. This is disgusting. It is corrupt. It is a national disgrace.\par \par \uc2 They knew it wasn't Russian disinformation, but they had an election to win. They had a favored candidate. His name was -- well, he can't remember it, but we remember, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And by the way, \uc2 Chris Wray\uc2  doesn't want to answer any questions about that matter either. He ducked, he dodged, he obfuscated left and right in this interview with Bret Baier.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WRAY: I can't speak to what former officials of the intelligence community may or may not have said. I can only speak to what we do. And unfortunately, as you would expect, if we're going to do this investigation in the right way, that means I can't talk about the specifics of that investigation, other than to assure everyone that I expect our people to tackle this investigation the way that I expect them to tackle every investigation which is to follow the facts wherever they lead no matter who likes it. There's always somebody who doesn't like it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You've had the laptop for three plus years. You had the laptop months before the presidential election. You could have verified that probably in a matter of 72 hours max.\par \par \uc2 Now, during a very revealing interview with Bret Baier, as I said, he ducked, he dodged every single solitary question. He obfuscated. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  director seems to think that he is accountable to nobody.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, this is -- you know, this isn't just about Trump and Biden and the presidential election. It's about political bias in our justice system, at the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the DOJ. That becomes a threat to anybody that maybe they don't like whatever group it happens to be.\par \par \uc2 For example, angry parents at school board meetings, remember, they were recently labeled and being investigated as potential domestic terrorists. Oh, they don't want CRT or they don't want transgender education for kids in kindergarten. Traditional Catholics, remember, they were targeted at their place of worship. Dozens of Americans had their bank records turned over to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , all because they took a bus to Washington, D.C. to hear a rally on January 6 2021. They didn't break any laws.\par \par \uc2 But if you try to light a federal courthouse on fire in Portland or participated in 574 violent riots in the summer of 2020, you likely never faced any real investigation. That is a two-tier justice system. That's what we're talking about.\par \par \uc2 That is apparently also true if you're firebombed an emergency pregnancy center or vandalize the church. Out of 250 recent attacks, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 's \uc2 FBI\uc2  only brought charges against two of these violent criminals. That's it. But they did manage to send a SWAT team, guns drawn, to the home of a pro-life activist who shoved a man allegedly harassing his son near an abortion clinic but don't expect an explanation from \uc2 Chris Wray\uc2 . Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Here's what I'm talking about is the dual system. You know, there's that for a pro-life activist, but not that for a Black Lives Matter protester who maybe torches a federal building over the summer. So that disparity, that dichotomy is what sticks in people's mind.\par \par \uc2 WRAY: I understand that people have their opinions. All I can tell you is that we have one standard, one standard, which is irrespective of ideology, of politics.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That is a croc of Adam Schiff, I don't believe any of that.\par \par \uc2 Their one standard -- thank you -- their one standard, conservatives, Republicans, they get targeted, while violent criminals on the left, they get a free pass. I think it's obvious. It is clear. It is transparent.\par \par \uc2 So, Director Wray needs to resign or he needs to be fired and frankly the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the DOJ may need to be dismantled to bring back the honor and integrity that it once had, but that likely won't happen under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , because \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  is dutifully serving the Biden administration. They're part of the executive branch of government.\par \par \uc2 And today, Biden's attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , well, he echoed his colleagues at the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . What a shocker. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOSH HAWLEY\uc2  (R-MO): A Catholic pro-life demonstrator, father, is accused of disorderly conduct in front of an abortion center, the local prosecutor, the Philadelphia district attorney who is a Democrat, a liberal, very progressive, declined to prosecute. There was a private suit that got dismissed.\par \par \uc2 And then after all of that, your Justice Department sent between 20 and 30 armed agents and the early morning hours to the house private residence to arrest this guy after he had offered to turn himself in voluntarily.\par \par \uc2 MERRICK GARLAND\uc2 , ATTORNEY GENERAL: Determinations of how to make arrest under arrest warrant are made based by the tactical operators in the district.\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: But you certainly looked into it at this point, right? You know the answer.\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: All I know is what the \uc2 FBI\uc2  had said, which is that they made the decision on the ground, as to what was safest and easiest.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So get this: the DOJ is perfectly fine with sending a SWAT team in that scenario but they won't even bring charges against anybody that was doxxing or harassing or threatening \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  justices at their homes. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. TED CRUZ (R-TX): Have you brought a single case against any of these protesters threatening the justices under 18 USC Section 1507? You brought even one.\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: Senator, you asked me whether I sat on my hands and quite of the opposite I sent 70 United States Marshals --\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Try again, has the Department of Justice brought even a single case under the statute? It's a yes/no question. It's not a give a speech on the other things you did.\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: The job of the United States Marshals is to defend the lives --\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: So the answer is no?\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: -- is to defend the lives of the justices and that's their number one priority. They have full --\par \par \uc2 CRUZ: Are you unwilling to say no? The answer is no, you know it's no, I know it's no. Everyone in this in this hearing room knows it's no. You're not willing to answer a question.\par \par \uc2 Have you brought a case under this statute? Yes or no?\par \par \uc2 GARLAND: As far as I know, we haven't.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Checkmate, Ted Cruz. That was slam dunk.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's be clear, a politicized and weaponized justice system will not stand the test of time. But in the meantime, Wray and Garland don't seem to care.\par \par \uc2 All right. Joining us now, two former \uc2 FBI\uc2  special agents Nicole Parker and Steve Friend are with us.\par \par \uc2 Thank you both for joining us. Thank you for your service.\par \par \uc2 Nicole, I'll start with you. You had a very high paying job on Wall Street with a hedge fund and you were there on 9/11 when those towers were hit and you made a decision you wanted to serve your country and join the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Forty-five I think or 50,000 people applied for the job. You were one of a few hundred that got hired. Is that correct?\par \par \uc2 NICOLE PARKER, FORMER FBI SPECIAL AGENT: Yes, Sean, that's correct. I witnessed the terrorist attacks on the World Trade Center on September 11th of 2001 in New York City, and it impacted my life in a way that I knew one day I needed to and wanted to serve this country.\par \par \uc2 And I looked long and hard and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was the vehicle that I was going to use to give back and to serve my nation.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay and you went and you served, and after about 12 or 13 years, you left before your retirement. Why did you leave?\par \par \uc2 PARKER: I left because of everything that you've just shown your audience. I mean, one thing after another after another after another. You know, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  says that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is fair, that they follow the evidence. If that was the case, I wouldn't have left the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the employees that are extremely frustrated probably wouldn't be frustrated either.\par \par \uc2 It just -- you feel like you don't have a voice, that you're so low on the totem pole. How are they even going to know my concerns as a rank and file agent? I was working violent crime, I worked shoulder to shoulder with incredible heroes. You know, the individuals in my violent crime squad, we were out there saving individuals and putting bad people behind bars and that is why I came to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But I was getting drowned out by this constant noise. It started in 2016 with, you know, \uc2 Jim Comey\uc2  coming out on July 5th, 2016 and making a statement that seemed in my opinion to be somewhat of a prosecutorial decision when in reality the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is supposed to present evidence to the Department of Justice and they're supposed to make the prosecutorial decision. Then, there was Operation Crossfire Hurricane, and then it just kept coming and coming and coming.\par \par \uc2 And then you've discussed all the disparities between how investigations were conducted at the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . I wasn't involved in any of those. The fine men and women of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  doing the heavy lifting were not involved in those either. But unfortunately, it has a trickle-down effect for those that are involved and it brings down the entire organization and quite frankly, I felt like I could probably make a stronger impact outside of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  than inside of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , and that is why I chose to leave.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And you risked your life and you even lost fellow agents that were killed in the line of duty.\par \par \uc2 Let me bring in if I can hear Steve Friend.\par \par \uc2 You're an \uc2 FBI\uc2  hero as well. We are going to hear Steve from dozens of \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents whistleblowers in the days and weeks and months to come. Tell us about your experience with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and your reaction to what \uc2 Chris Wray\uc2  and \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said today.\par \par \uc2 STEVE FRIEND, FORMER FBI SPECIAL AGENT: Well, I think we have to start with the first question that was asked to him in in that interview and that was how he felt about the public perception of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . And his response to that was we have to remember who the \uc2 FBI\uc2  serves and who they work with. And he immediately pivoted to the hiring of new applicants in the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And that to me is very revelatory because clearly, the Christopher Wray FBI does not consider the American population their customers. It's very obviously --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, you talk about the Washington -- I'm sorry, I didn't mean to step on you. Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND: I said it's very obviously the Biden administration and in the political left and he's ready willing and able to provide a well-staffed and well-compensated workforce that's going to do their bidding.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So you have stated before and I know you're on with John Solomon, a friend of this program, that the Washington, D.C. field office is manipulating \uc2 FBI\uc2  case management protocol. You talk about the \uc2 FBI\uc2  domestic terrorism case that are being opened on innocent Americans, how the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has post facto designated, you know, a grassy area outside the Capital as a restricted zone.\par \par \uc2 What other offenses did you witness?\par \par \uc2 FRIEND: Well, I -- from my own personal perspective, I was assigned to work violent crimes against children, essentially child pornography investigations. And in the fall of 2021 was told that I was going to be reassigned to work domestic terrorism, January 6th, and that any of the work that I was doing on those would be considered a local matter no longer resourced by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I don't think you have to be a non-partisan if you are a partisan to come to the conclusion that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is clearly prioritized this January 6 investigation and is willing to put the public safety at risk if you use these overly aggressive SWAT team arrest tactics and large-scale arrest operations, and when it's just not necessary when you have individuals who have been cooperative and pledged like Mark Hawk did to be cooperative and surrender himself should charges come. It's not necessary to send a tactical team in a bearcat or 30 agents in body armor with slung M4s.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, like look at what -- they look at the way they treated Roger Stone or \uc2 Paul Manafort\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, Nicole and Steve, thank you. You are leading the pack and we will be hearing from dozens of your fellow agents talking about how the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has been politicized, the DOJ weaponize. Thank you for your courage. Thank you for your service.\par \par \uc2 And for all the rank and file \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents that do a great job and protect and serve this country, I can't thank them enough. We're not talking about them. Thank you for being with us. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right. Here with more reaction, she is the co-host of the hit show "The Five" -- look who's here. No introduction needed, Judge Jeanine Pirro.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, CO-HOST OF "THE FIVE": Thank you.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: People may not know -- we've been friends along -- we've been friends forever.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Too long.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Really?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We've been friends a long time. People don't know that you were a prosecutor. We're going to hear from dozens of agents like this and stories one after another.\par \par \uc2 I don't think we can fix it with people like Director Wray and \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  in these positions.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Well, there's no question we can't fix it. I mean never has