tary Presence In Region; \uc2 EPA\uc2  Vows To Hold Railroad Accountable For Cleanup; New Hampshire Governor Mulls 2024 Run; Gov.\par \par \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  (R-NH) Mulls 024 Run; Son Of Defendant Testifies In Double Slaying Trial Of The Murdaugh Murders\par \par \uc2 JOHNNY JOEY JONES, FOX NEWS MEDIA CONTRIBUTOR: I got hounded by bomb dog. A DOD (PH) dog. Its name is Guinness. It's so famous. It's got its own little stuffed animal.\par \par \uc2 That's with his handler, that's another deputy that's a big fan, and brought the stuffed animal home. And there is Margo with Guinness.\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Oh, so cute. So cute.\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Oh, so sweet.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Joey, that was hilarious.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: All right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: You win. You win "ONE MORE THING".\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes. Joey Suede.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: SPECIAL REPORT is up next. Hey, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR (on camera): Hi, Greg. Joey wins "ONE MORE THING."\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Good evening. Welcome to Washington. I'm Bret Baier. "BREAKING TONIGHT", as the world marks the first anniversary of the Ukraine war, a war of words between the leaders of the U.S. and Russia.\par \par \uc2 President Biden today in Poland, saying there will be hard and bitter days ahead as Ukraine battles Russians across that country. But the president saying having just visited there, the U.S. will support Ukraine for "as long as it takes."\par \par \uc2 Meantime, in dueling speeches, Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  says he is suspending Russia's participation in the last remaining nuclear arms control pact with the U.S., insisting the west is dead set on destroying Russia.\par \par \uc2 White House correspondent Peter Doocy is traveling with President Biden, reports tonight from Warsaw, Poland. Good evening, Peter.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT (on camera): Good evening, Bret.\par \par \uc2 Here in Warsaw, President Biden did not publicly pressure China's President Xi to stay out of Ukraine. Instead, he kept almost his entire focus where it has been for most of the last year on \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Autocrats only understand one word. No, no, no.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): White House officials are putting out the word, it would not be good if China starts arming Russia.\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY, COORDINATOR FOR STRATEGIC COMMUNICATIONS, NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL: Obviously, a burgeoning and deepening defense relationship between these two countries, while Mr. Putin is prosecuting a brutal war in Ukraine. Clearly, that would have very, very bad ramifications.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Ramifications and consequences from Biden have not deterred Putin, the war continues. And now, Russia is suspending its participation in the New START nuclear arms control treaty.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR PUTIN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF RUSSIA (through translator): They can't be stupid people. They want to deliver us a strategic defeat, while sneaking into our strategic nuclear objects.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: U.S. inspections of Russian nuclear facilities now seize.\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2 , UNITED STATES SECRETARY OF STATE: The announcement by Russia that it's suspending participation in New START is deeply unfortunate and irresponsible.\par \par \uc2 In Warsaw, President Biden's remarks touted the West's response to Russia as a success so far.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: One year ago, the world was bracing for the fall of Kyiv. Well, I just come from a visit to Kyiv, and I can report Kyiv stand strong.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: But Putin has no plans to pull back.\par \par \uc2 PUTIN: I want to repeat, it is they who have started the war. We have used and are