That was intonation.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: It seemed to be. Look, he is absolutely right. And look, I think everybody who wants to try it out should go in. It's a free country. If you want to run for president, go ahead and throw your hat in the ring and see if you can gather some enthusiasm. But the problem is in 2016 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the nomination with a third the electorate, right. And you even saw that playing out in some of the primaries where he endorsed candidates who won with 32 percent when 68 percent of the state was against his chosen candidates.\par \par \uc2 So if these people get in the race -- he didn't get above 50 percent until the New York primary in answer April 19th. So he won the nomination with a third the vote. He could do that again if we don't have the discipline. So, candidates should go in, test the waters. And if you don't catch a wave, get out of the race.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So the former president, very active this weekend on Truth Social, called this network the RINO network. He also said about Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , "Florida was doing great long before Ron DeSanctus got there." "DeSanctimonious" is the word he uses. "People are fleeing from New York to Florida and other places because of high taxes and out of control crime, not because of Governor (thank you President Trump!) DeSanctimonious. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  did great. Even \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  had very good numbers. Sunshine and ocean, very alluring." \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , of course, the Democrat that he ran against, DeSantis did, and defeated soundly.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: President Trump never shies away from nicknaming his opponents. DeSantis has not declared even though it's clear he may be getting in given his countrywide crime tour. Interesting how he has treated Nikki Haley, not a whole lot of nicknames on that.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yet.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: But he has 40 percent -- yet. But he has 40 percent of the voters in the Republican Party as of now. And if there are a number of candidates who stay in for far too long and their goal as candidates is to beat him, the math doesn't add up.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: But quickly, Josh, the Republican Party probably has a little angst with these see these posts.\par \par \uc2 KRAUSHAAR: They do. But going back to Sununu, likability matters. Haley had a very optimistic message, she is likeable. Sununu put on a good face here on the show tonight. Trump and DeSantis, that's their biggest vulnerability.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, thank you all.\par \par \uc2 It's Tuesday. It's time for "Tuesday Tweets." First up, Dan asks, "Bret, does Biden visit to Ukraine put pressure on GOP presidential candidates to take a stand on support for Ukraine?" One-hundred percent. It's a question out there, if the president is out visiting and talking like he is talking, it will be a major issue as you head into this race.\par \par \uc2 Next up, Dr. Strangelove tweets, "Do you think the Biden administration will include F-16 fighter jets in a future Ukrainian aid package?" Hard to see right now. They have said no. But we have seen this evolution of all of this stuff.\par \par \uc2 Last, Cindy wants to know, "Who is your favorite "FIVE" host that transitions from their show to yours?" It's kind of like a box of chocolates. You never know what's going to be in there. Greg usually has the biggest surprises on the handover.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced, and still unafraid. "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME" starts right now. Jesse is pretty good on the handover.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written perm