ame and reputation sullied by his father's political enemies, for absolutely, positively no reason at all whatsoever, Hunter is now fighting back with a team around him or at least that's how the media mob is trying to spin it. It looks like it might be true, and letters are popping here and there and everywhere, to the DOJ, the \uc2 IRS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Anyway, Hunter's lawyers now are asking pops, Joey, to put an end to the disinformation of materials on \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop from hell. This is where it gets interesting. At the very same time, Hunter's camp is actively refusing to admit that the information on the laptop actually belongs to Hunter even though one of the lawyers seem to indicate it was his laptop and that was his information. So, is it or not according to his lawyers? We can't tell you what message his team is trying to convey.\par \par \uc2 In other words, they're asking the government to stop the spread of Hunter's materials without admitting that it is Hunter's materials.\par \par \uc2 Now, I would normally say that's pretty dumb and stupid and really not smart. But -- the fact that I've done this so many years, I actually suspect there is a legal strategy behind all of this and I think time will prove me right.\par \par \uc2 Now, this gives us a really good opportunity, we have been reaching out -- to everybody out there watching the show. We have been reaching out to Hunter's legal team for quite some time through dozens and dozens of requests. My team on the show have asked about numerous reports and sadly, Hunter's team, they never want once -- not one time bother to get back to us. They have neither confirmed or denied anything.\par \par \uc2 So, now, that they decided to start talking, we have a few questions. Actually, I can think over 100 just for tonight's show, that would probably be a week's worth of shows.\par \par \uc2 So, we're going to start tonight with five questions, and we'll do five tomorrow night. And we'll do five probably in perpetuity.\par \par \uc2 But number one, here is the question that I would like to answer right now that they are finally talking. Why was Hunter even on the board of \uc2 Burisma\uc2 ? That's the Ukrainian oil and gas giant.\par \par \uc2 And according to the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  finance report, despite having no experience in oil or gas or Ukraine, Hunter collected a huge monthly, you know, fee from \uc2 Burisma\uc2  while his father was the vice president in charge of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Now, on "\uc2 GMA\uc2 ," "Good Morning America", Hunter himself admitted that he probably would not have been invited to join that board because he admitted he had no experience if he wasn't vice president or then-Vice President Biden's son. He admitted on that show he had no experience in energy and zero experience in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 So my question is, why was Hunter paid a little small fortune to sit on the board of \uc2 Burisma\uc2 ? What benefit did they get or did they expect to get?\par \par \uc2 Now I'm sure you recall around the same time, according to "The Hill", then-Vice President Biden, remember and we saw the tape of this and I played it a lot during the Trump-Ukraine impeachment idiocy of the left. Anyway, Vice President Biden was bragging he leveraged US$1 billion to get a Ukrainian prosecutor fired in six hours, I said, six hours, I said, oh you're not getting the money.\par \par \uc2 Why would a vice president of the United States want a Ukrainian prosecutor fired?\par \par \uc2 Now, according to investigative reporter John Solomon, the prosecutor was allegedly investigating Hunter and \uc2 Burisma\uc2  for corruption, and Joe said and bragged in that tape, son of a B, to quote \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , he got him fired and Ukraine got your one billion dollars in other words \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  leveraged that money and he helped leverage it to fire the prosecutor, that has said in interviews, she was looking at investigating his son.\par \par \uc2 Now, here's a question. Was this \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's quid pro quo moment on Ukraine? You may recall what the country went through. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the phone with the then new president of Ukraine, Zelenskyy, and asking him if he's not going to be like his predecessors and squander his taxpayers' money. Now, did \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  -- did he -- what did he do to stop this investigation into his son? Why would he ever do that? Why, so his son could still be paid a small fortune with no experience from \uc2 Burisma\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Here's our next question. Why was Hunter Biden wired $3.5 million from a Russian oligarch known as the former first lady of Moscow as reported by the Senate's Homeland Security Committee? Why? What did he do for the money, what experience did he have?\par \par \uc2 Now, according to that same committee, in 2013, Hunter traveled with his father to China was a trip to Asia, but they went to China on Air Force II. Ten days later, the Senate committee, they claimed that he struck a lucrative deal with the Bank of China despite his terrible reputation, lackluster resume. Peter Schweizer writes that it was a billion dollars.\par \par \uc2 So what was the real figure? How did Hunter land that kind of deal? What was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's role? Why wouldn't China prefer, say, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 , \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 ? You know, can Hunter's team now explain to this country why they've benefited from that deal over those companies that have real experience?\par \par \uc2 And how much money did Hunter or maybe future money promised or any other Biden make from this big deal with China?\par \par \uc2 And look at this -- why did a Chinese businessman gift the Biden family a hundred thousand dollar shopping spree in 2017 as outlined in the U.S. Senate Committee on Homeland Security?\par \par \uc2 By the way, would anyone in the audience like a hundred thousand dollar shopping spree? Okay.\par \par \uc2 That very same year, an email from Hunter's laptop sourced by "The New York Post" revealed the structure of a business venture with a Chinese energy company, quote, 10 for Jim, that would be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's brother's name, 10 held by H for the big guy. The big guy -- is that a reference to President Biden?\par \par \uc2 Well, Tony Bobulinski thinks so. He said so in an interview. If so, why was he cut in on Hunter's deal with the Chinese energy firm?\par \par \uc2 Now, two years later, according to "The New York Post", Hunter texted his own daughter that he was forced to fork over half of his salary and give it to pops. Pops would be his father, that would be Joe. But he said he wouldn't do this to his own daughter.\par \par \uc2 So did Hunter in real truth actually split his earnings with his father? If so, how much money was involved? If so, did Joe declare all of this on his taxes?\par \par \uc2 Is it fair to say that Hunter implicated his own father and proving that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lied to the country when he said during the campaign again and again and again that he never had a single conversation with his son Hunter about his foreign business dealings? Does all of this kind of reek of potential corruption? Does this not highlight the need for oversight from the new Republican Congress?\par \par \uc2 So if any or all of this is true, here's the question the country needs answered for the national security purposes. Now for this question, it's for Joe, Hunter's father, the big guy. Is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  -- Joe, are you compromised when it comes to Russia? They are our number two geopolitical foe.\par \par \uc2 Are you compromised with Ukraine? Are you compromised with the United States of America's number one geopolitical threat and that would be China? Did your family with your knowledge do lucrative deals with China -- yeah, our number one political foe, and Russia and Ukraine? Did you do those deals?\par \par \uc2 You might have noticed that Russia and China are more aggressive than they were during the Trump years by a long shot. Just one example, right now, there is a high altitude Chinese spy balloon reportedly flying over the northern United States. By the way, somebody have a pin that they can shoot up in the air and take that balloon out of the sky, if you're so convinced it's there, okay.\par \par \uc2 As far as we know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has taken no action to disable that balloon. Why?\par \par \uc2 Here now with reaction, the host of "Unfiltered", our friend Dan Bongino. By the way, there's no such thing as a filtered Dan Bongino. I can tell you that part.\par \par \uc2 We welcome you, Dan Bongino, to the show.\par \par \uc2 DAN BONGINO, HOST OF "UNFILTERED": Good to be here.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's get your overall thoughts, because we have all of these sources and all of these unanswered questions all of our calls were not returned. That doesn't surprise me, but we tried hard. I mean, we have a stack of emails that we sent.\par \par \uc2 And my question is, Dan, I'd like to know what you think of all of this.\par \par \uc2 BONGINO: Well, let me answer a couple of questions here. At first, it's pretty cool you got a studio audience. I may have to do that for my show. So get names and numbers and you can send them all --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: HANNITY comes up with a good idea and it gets copied, that's never happened before.\par \par \uc2 BONGINO: Right, of course, yeah. Well, why not? You've been on the air for 40 years or something like that. Of course, I'm going to steal your stuff.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And by the way, he's a friend.\par \par \uc2 BONGINO: Don't worry about it. I am a friend, at least I'm honest about it, you know?\par \par \uc2 So, listen, here's the deal -- let's answer your first question you asked. Why was \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  on the board of \uc2 Burisma\uc2 ? Well, yes, of course, it was because the Ukrainians were looking to leverage the point man \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to get money from the United States, but that's not it. That's not the only reason.\par \par \uc2 If you listen to the dirt cash tapes that were leaked, it was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's on the phone with Poroshenko, the Ukrainian president before Zelenskyy follows. Isn't that difficult? I don't want anyone to get lost in the names here.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's on a recording actually threatening them or appearing to threaten an \uc2 IMF\uc2  loan if they don't close the bank in Ukraine called PrivatBank. The \uc2 IMF\uc2  loan, Sean, was worth tens of billions of dollars and what he -- what the bank he wants closed on the tape is called PrivatBank.\par \par \uc2 Here's the real kick in the teeth here, right? The bank is run by a guy by the name of \uc2 Igor Kolomoisky\uc2 , right, who has a business tie to \uc2 Burisma\uc2 . The number three guy in \uc2 Burisma\uc2  is known as Kolomoisky's fixer. The PrivatBank was under investigation by the same prosecutor \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wanted fired.\par \par \uc2 This is -- and the bank, by the way, has been tied, according to multiple reports, to payments to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . So just follow me for a second here.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Some of this is new information for me that I've not heard. Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 BONGINO: It's tough to tie together, but it's all there. It's all in -- and you can see it, it's all laid out and reporting that's already out there. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in a recording demanding this bank be closed of the prior Ukrainian president and he says in the recording, by the way, hey, Kolomoisky's a real, quote, pain in the ass.\par \par \uc2 Kolomoisky, his guy is the fixer at \uc2 Burisma\uc2  that hired Hunter, and the bank is under investigation in Ukraine for sending money to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . And that's the prosecutor investigating the bank that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's on tape he wants fired.\par \par \uc2 Wait, here's another kick in the teeth. The guy on stage at that Council of Foreign Relations speech where \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's demanding the prosecutor to get fired, his name is Michael Carpenter. You'll never believe who Michael Carpenter is. He's the senior director at the Penn Biden Center where they found the classified documents, according to reports about, what, about Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 And Biden actually gives him a shout out after he says he demanded the guy to be fired, he goes, oh, Michael knows. This is his territory. They all know it.\par \par \uc2 Here's the dirty little secret of this whole thing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 BONGINO: Ukraine was a big international piggy bank and Joe and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  had their hands in the cookie jar, too. They wanted to get paid and get paid big.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have less than a minute. This is the question I most often asked -- all right, we went through the entire Trump-Russia collusion hoax and lie, and we got it right on this program, unpeeling every layer of the onion for nearly three years.\par \par \uc2 "The Columbia Journalism Review" excoriated "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ". By the way, they got a Pulitzer Prize, I didn't get anything, and also "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ". But they said they were wrong and they excoriated them on the issue of the Steele dossier.\par \par \uc2 The question I get asked the most, Dan Bongino, is will there be justice? Will they be held accountable? If there was a quid pro quo with a billion taxpayer dollars to protect his son and that's proven out, wouldn't that warrant the impeachment that they gave \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 BONGINO: Yeah. Will they be held accountable? Not with \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  in charge, and I encourage everyone to go read this article "Politico" by the way from 2017. I'll read the headline for you. Ukrainian efforts to sabotage \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  backfire, "Politico", Kenneth Vogel, January 11, 2017.\par \par \uc2 You want to see how the impeachment hoax, the Russia hoax, Ukraine, the classified documents and Biden getting the fire the -- but the prosecutor fired and his son's gig in Ukraine are all tied together? Read this piece. They run from it now, but I promise you, it's still up online.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainians played a key role in the Russia hoax, if not the key role in the Russia hoax. Trump knew about it, and that's why they wanted to impeach him and he knew about Biden's grift in Ukraine, too.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Dan Bongino, great to -- great to have you. Thank you as always for being with us. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 All right. Now to Capitol Hill where Congresswoman Omar has been booted from the House Foreign Affairs Committee but not before some theatrics from Omar's far left colleagues. By the way, where were these theatrics when Jim Jordan and Jim Banks weren't allowed on the Jan 6 Committee? Where was this when \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and other Republicans were denied any committee assignments?\par \par \uc2 Take a look and remember that as you watched.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): Don't tell me this is about consistency. Don't tell me that this is a condemnation of antisemitic remarks. This is about targeting women of color in the United States of America. Don't tell me because I didn't get a single apology --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Time has expired.\par \par \uc2 OCASIO-CORTEZ: -- when my life was threatened. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 REP. RASHIDA TLAIB (D-MI): The GOP is now doing what it is best at, weaponizing hate against a Black, beautiful Muslim woman --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The gentlewoman's time has expired.\par \par \uc2 TLAIB: -- not be silenced. To Congresswoman Omar, I'm sorry --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The gentlewoman's time has expired.\par \par \uc2 TLAIB: -- that our country is failing you today, to this chamber --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The gentlewoman is no longer recognized.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Forget the hysteria, here are the facts: Congresswoman Omar was removed from the Foreign Affairs Committee because of her own terrible behavior, a reckless rhetoric, irresponsible rhetoric, antisemitic rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 For example, here's what she tweeted out about our top ally Israel: Israel has hypnotized the world and may Allah awaken the people and help them see the evil doings of Israel.\par \par \uc2 Omar also used Jewish tropes about money pushed conspiracy theories about Jewish influence over the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 , and according to Omar, it's all about the Benjamins, baby.\par \par \uc2 And then she also palled around with the notorious, well, bigot of Israel, that's \uc2 Linda Sarsour\uc2 . That's pictured right there, and Omar even compared the U.S. to al Qaeda, and suggested that many terror groups really aren't that bad and no different from the \uc2 U.S. Army\uc2 . And by the way, he or she is laughing and smirking while one of her colleagues spoke about American troops being killed in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 And who can ever forget when she described 9/11 as a time, well, some people did something. Two thousand nine hundred seventy-seven people died that day, our fellow Americans, worst attack on American soil and people still died from its aftermath.\par \par \uc2 Omar's conduct is so reprehensible that our own Democratic colleagues once introduced the resolution, they condemned her remarks. She was also banned from the country of Israel, rightly so.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: people who openly detest America, our allies, they have no place representing us on the world stage, in the Foreign Affairs Committee.\par \par \uc2 All right. Brings us now to the HANNITY hot seat. By the way, let's give a warm HANNITY audience welcome our friend, Geraldo Rivera.\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, CO-HOST OF THE FIVE: Hi, everybody. Hello.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Our other friend, Tammy Bruce.\par \par \uc2 TAMMY BRUCE, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Hi you guys.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Geraldo, you're raising my blood pressure the last three appearances. You're driving me nuts and we've been friends forever.\par \par \uc2 Please tell me a woman that is spewing that hatred, that anti-Semitism, that she does not want -- she's allowed on committees -- now \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  wouldn't let Republicans on commit.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I disagree with your characterization, my dear brother. I think that you have to be careful that criticism of Israel is not necessarily anti-Semitism and vice versa. She can criticize a state that she has meaningful disagreements with. I mean, she is a Muslim woman. She's the first naturalized --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: My question, we're going to have a poll. How many people think she's antisemitic? Let's show it.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: How many people agree with Geraldo?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: It doesn't hurt my feelings. I believe that you cannot remove people from committees because of their personal views, otherwise what are you going to have in Congress? A bunch of yes man? The vote to eject her was purely partisan, Sean, and 118 --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: When was the voice when \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  was not allowed on a single committee? Hang on.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Terrible.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Democrats -- where are all those Democrats standing up for her?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I agree with you on that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And Jim Jordan and Jim Banks were kicked off the J6 committee.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I absolutely agree with that.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay, they set the president. At least Kevin McCarthy's allowing her committee assignments, just not that one.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: This has shocked Congress so profoundly that they --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, stop it.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- the Republicans are now -- under Congresswoman Nancy Mace today introducing a new rule that no member of any committee can be ejected again without due process. That's as of today.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: The big difference here with this committee, she's on other committees, is that the Foreign Relations Committee is viewed by the world as speaking effectively for Congress, all right? That the people on it have a certain -- why do you think they were reacting so strongly because of the influence it gives you. It mattered to them.\par \par \uc2 So this is why the -- her other committee assignments are not affected but if this is about what America stands for. Is America antisemitic? Do we hate the Jews?\par \par \uc2 Also, hoping that Israel is, you know, destroyed. I've been comparing us and Israel to terrorist groups. So when you're sitting on the Foreign Relations Committee and you have that attitude, look, there are some people in America who are anti-Semitic, who hate the Jews. They do.\par \par \uc2 But we need to take a stand and that's what happened today is she was checked, and helping also others -- let me put -- I'm just -- you know, this is also important for other Democrats who have harmed.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Do we hate the Muslims?\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: No just a minute, you had -- you've had your space and I love him, too. I've known him for a long, long time.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh geez, you're ruining the show, stop.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: But no, but we can disagree in this regard in that, you know, you've got to have a framework where the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  and Americans have wanted Congress to represent us again and this kind of rhetoric, Jew-hating rhetoric, it's not just being critical of Israel, it's everything else combined and that is where she also cannot be objective when dealing with these issues.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's get an answer from Geraldo.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Every single Democrat voted to keep her on the committee, every single Republican voted to eject her. This was a pure partisan act.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What was the last Congress --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: We can't couch this in nobility. This is not about nobility.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: She's allowed on committees.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: This is about retribution. This is about you did it to Gosar and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: They weren't allowed on any committees, Geraldo. That's not the case.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: The reason we have diversity, you want different views, Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Tammy?\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: If this was about retribution and partisanship, she would be off all committees. Democrats would be off committees. There would be this -- you know, you have to hand it to \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . She was a bull in a china shop. She did whatever she wanted to do, and the Republicans kind of let it happen.\par \par \uc2 This is the proper thing to do. It was based in the nature of her comments, and what people have argued --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I have a question -- I have a question for you.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- myself, I reject that characterization.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Was it the right decision to take -- thank -- I can't even believe, he couldn't write this in a novel. Was it the right decision to take Fang Fang's BFF Swalwell off the Intel Committee?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I believe that when you --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Answer.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: No, no, my answer is no.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, a Chinese spy?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: You cannot make judgments based on politics. However, you characterize it.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: It's all politics.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Are you accusing the congressman to being a spy from China?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Fang Fang was identified everywhere as a spy from China.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: So you think that he'd be so -- what?\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Kevin McCarthy all but said they got briefed on it.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- and not infect our foreign relations.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're hanging out with a spy from China but you can be on the intel committee.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Oh, believe me, you look at the people in Washington, D.C., who they have --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Oh, really, you've got stories?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: After the show, you and I --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. We got to roll.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: All right.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I love these guys both. They're great friends of the show. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 All right. Coming up, the left is still coming for your gas stoves, they haven't stopped. You're not going to believe what one internal Biden memo said. We're going to tell you and we'll check in with Charles Payne and the one and only Jimmy Failla. They react as we continue. Thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. It appears that the Biden administration's effort to control every aspect of your life is back in full force. Why don't they believe in freedom? Simple concept.\par \par \uc2 Now as the Energy Department now published a proposal yesterday to target your gas stoves, I like to cook. I was actually a chef at a restaurant when I was 13. I like cooking and I don't like electric stoves. They suck.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, they're claiming that it's about reducing energy consumption. The proposal is rightly igniting even more backlash, and it appears to be yet another crazy bizarre effort to appease the climate alarmist, religious cultists. And despite the fact that gas stoves are an efficient natural gas product, we have an abundance of natural gas, hundreds of years of our own supply. We don't need any from any other country and we can get it cheaply.\par \par \uc2 And get this -- an internal memo from the \uc2 Consumer Product Safety Commission\uc2 , it reveals team Biden was totally on board with the idea of banning gas stoves back when it was first floated, but then back down amid the public uproar. Joey really standing on principle.\par \par \uc2 But what's -- what's this really all about? Why are these far left bureaucrats so hell-bent on telling you what kind of stove you can have?\par \par \uc2 And there's even pictures of Jill Biden cooking on a gas stove. Lead by example. Davos, Switzerland, private jets, to tell us we can't eat meat, really?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, here to answer that much more, he is the host of "Making Money", Charles Payne is here, along with "FOX Across America" host Jimmy Failla is back here.\par \par \uc2 Oh, come on in.\par \par \uc2 By the way, Jimmy, did you wear the -- did you wear the tuxedo for me or for Charles?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Charles, why? You know, we have an economy -- you saw the story this week, two-thirds of Americans, even Americans making a hundred thousand dollars a year and, by the way, it's not their fault. They budgeted. They didn't budget for Biden's ten thousand dollar household inflation tax.\par \par \uc2 Why is the government getting involved in what we cook on leave us the hell alone.\par \par \uc2 CHARLES PAYNE, FBN HOST: I heard you mention the Davos n in that crowd and the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2 . I mean, it's all part and parcel of the ultimate control of not just the of America but you know, of the Western world by this group -- of this group of elitists who by the way have a get out of jail card, right? They can fly in private jets. They can cook on the gas stoves, but --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I've been in them -- they're the greatest convention in all of mankind, you know? If you can afford it, but that --\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Oh, sure, sure. Of course.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But I'm not going to tell anybody else they can't drive a caravan or an Escalade or they can't eat meat.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Right, right and they're making it legal, right? Illegal, it