derbilt? Is he Harriman? Is he Carnegie? Is he JP freakin' Morgan? No. No, he's not.\par \par \uc2 Actually, he is an accused felon who just this week was photographed shuffling along in handcuffs on his way to his cell. It's just so awesome.\par \par \uc2 These people are ridiculous and that's the real lesson of \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2  and we're going to enjoy every second of it.\par \par \uc2 Now, it's a little harder to enjoy what's happening to the rest of the economy -- inflation, especially. Inflation is one of those economic phenomena you don't need to be an MIT Professor to identify. Has the price of things you buy every week gone up a lot? Oh, it has. Okay, you've got inflation. Inflation is demonstrable.\par \par \uc2 Anyone who claims otherwise is lying and everybody knows that and that's why even most politicians, people who lie about anything, don't bother to lie about inflation. It's just too easy to catch them, but some still persist in lying about it. They just enjoy the experience of lying. It makes them feel alive.\par \par \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  is one of those. Watch her here to tell you that the inflation you're experiencing every day is not real. It's a mirage. It's "transitory."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANET YELLEN\uc2 , US TREASURY SECRETARY JUNE 2021: We've had several months of high inflation that most economists including me believe will be transitory.\par \par \uc2 YELLEN, JUNE 2021: I personally believe that this represents transitory factors.\par \par \uc2 NORA O'DONNELL, \uc2 CBS\uc2  NEWS, OCTOBER 2021: Are higher prices here to stay?\par \par \uc2 YELLEN: I believe it's transitory but I don't mean to suggest that these pressures will disappear in the next month or two.\par \par \uc2 YELLEN, JULY 2021, CNBC: It is important that we monitor it carefully, but I believe fundamentally that this is something that will all settle down.\par \par \uc2 SARA EISEN, CNBC NEWS ANCHOR: Transitory?\par \par \uc2 YELLEN: Transitory.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Did you hear that? She's an economist. She's not a scam artist who got rich from bribes disguised as speaking fees from the big banks after she had been running the Fed. No, no, no, no. She's an economist and because she's an economist and you're not, she knows that there are many kinds of inflation.\par \par \uc2 There is conventional inflation and there's something called transitory inflation and that's the kind of inflation you're not allowed to complain about, especially before a Midterm Election.\par \par \uc2 You are commanded to ignore that kind of inflation and if it still bothers you, then you have to do your patriotic duty and get an abortion. That's the word from \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , who as of tonight is literally our Treasury Secretary.\par \par \uc2 So, Merry Christmas much-lied-to American people. At least you know who we're dealing with now. The good news is we can still be happy. Happiness is a gift from God, and even the Biden administration can't take it away.\par \par \uc2 Jason Whitlock is a happy man. He is host of "Fearless." He joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Jason, thanks so much for coming on. I mean, you've got to admit, the upside to their lying is there's no question about what it is. They don't even try.\par \par \uc2 JASON WHITLOCK, HOST, "FEARLESS": They don't. Tucker, I loved your list, but you left a few things off it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, I know. A lot.\par \par \uc2 WHITLOCK: Well, listen, Ukraine, they released this blockbuster movie, "Top Gun: Maverick," the ghost of Kyiv. That fighter pilot that shot down Boris Yeltsin, Nikita Khrushchev, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and then when they crashed his plane, he hopped out of it and beat up Ivan Drago. You've got to remember that lie, of course.\par \par \uc2 The other one that I was big on, you mentioned it briefly. But I still think there is meat on the bones with Paul Pelosi, this guy remakes, MC Hammer's "U Can't Touch This" into "You Can Touch This" Hammer Time that's one of the biggest lies.\par \par \uc2 What about on the border, with the people with the whip? They were whipping -- oh, it reminded people gave everybody slavery flashbacks of the immigrants and this was -- and then on a more serious note, just for me because we're so close to Christmas, the January 6 Committee, that to me is the biggest lie we've got going on in America. And we are so close to Christmas and I think about those people that are locked up and being treated like they were George Floyd rioters and looters when they were really just going to confront the politicians that they were frustrated with. So that would have been my list, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You know, you're so right and I was going to include that, but honestly, it made me so mad, I couldn't write anything funny about it, honestly.\par \par \uc2 But we can be happy anyway and Jason Whitlock, we're so -- we are grateful for you and your appearances so often on the show. They really make a difference. Thank you. Merry Christmas.\par \par \uc2 WHITLOCK: Thank you. Merry Christmas.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Winter storms are disrupting a lot of things in the country, especially air travel, something called the bomb cyclone, they're telling us is now in progress.\par \par \uc2 FOX's \uc2 Mike Tobin\uc2  is at Chicago's O'Hare Airport with the very latest.\par \par \uc2 Mike Tobin\uc2 , thanks for joining us. What's going on there?\par \par \uc2 MIKE TOBIN\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Well, you know in terms of bodies piling up to the airport, Tucker, it never really got that bad and I've got to give a tip of the hat to the airlines because they communicated with the travelers when the flights were being canceled, when they were being delayed. It is a little different on the other side of security because you've got a lot of people who couldn't get on their connecting flights.\par \par \uc2 But what is a bomb cyclone? It is a weather phenomenon when you have a low pressure system colliding with a high pressure system, it drives down a bunch of cold air, creates a bunch of wind and usually precipitation.\par \par \uc2 It is marked by a drop in the barometer of 24 millibars over a 24-hour period. Now, I've been tracking it, I've tracked 14 millibars. So unfortunately for all the suffering I think we're going to fall a little short of earning your bomb cyclone merit badge. We will leave the final call to the meteorologists. I'm just a hack at these things.\par \par \uc2 What you did get a lot of flight cancellations. Seattle-Tacoma airport in particular, they got dumped on with freezing rain and that ice over the runways and the ice is actually harder to get off the runways than the snow. So they had to shut down the whole airport, and that meant \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2  canceled all of their flights out of Seattle and Portland as well.\par \par \uc2 By noon today, you had just about 4,000 flights that were canceled. So the ripple effect impacted pretty much all the major air carriers in every airport. If you're one of the people who made it home on time, you're one of the lucky ones.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Unfortunately, last night, we were scheduled to leave out about 7:50 this morning. We got a text last night saying they rescheduled us to Austin at 12 o'clock today with a layover.\par \par \uc2 We're just trying to figure out what's going on. We're trying to avoid this line. And we're just trying to get home.\par \par \uc2 This is a mess.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We were originally meant to fly to Toronto from London, England last night and our flight was canceled. Then we re-booked to Detroit today, but that was canceled as well.\par \par \uc2 So we just tried to get another flight to Toronto or Detroit and there is nothing left for us.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TOBIN: So the system didn't create too much snow, it did create a lot of cold, create a lot of wind. It drove the snow around last night, made it really treacherous to see if you were trying to drive. Today, the roads aren't that bad, but it is cold, cold, cold. I'm talking to you right now, negative five in Chicago with a windchill of negative 30 -- Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, bad, but not as bad as it might have been, which makes it good. And we appreciate that good news from you, \uc2 Mike Tobin\uc2 , thank you.\par \par \uc2 TOBIN: There you go. Merry Christmas.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So one comedian just explained why exactly the lifestyle left is so angry at the Christmas songs he grew up with. "Baby it's Cold Outside." That's hate speech. He join us in a minute to explain.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: The good news about the collapse of the traditional legacy media is that new media is moving to fill the void they left behind, and Libs of TikTok is honestly, well, it's a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account, but it has become one of the most important sites of reporting in the new media. And essentially what Libs with TikTok does is find videos that people have posted online about themselves publicly and hold them up for a bigger audience.\par \par \uc2 Libs of TikTok is one of the reasons we know what is happening in classrooms around the country right now. Here is a sample.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I have had multiple students come out to me not just with their sexuality, but also with their gender identity. It's one of the reasons I think it's so important to be out and loud and proud.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I teach my elementary school students about gender identity. Some people are girls, some are boys, some are both, some are neither.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I might tell this kid, we do have a flag in the class that you can pledge your allegiance to and he like looks around he goes, oh, that one.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So there's something really wrong in the country and in our classrooms. Kids are being exposed to it without the knowledge of their parents and we wouldn't even know that were it not in a lot of cases for the reporting of Libs of TikTok, who, by the way, doesn't editorialize much, just holds up what people have said about themselves.\par \par \uc2 For doing this, the left has really tried to hurt the person who runs Libs of TikTok. Taylor Lorenz of "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ," wrote a whole piece trying to find out who this person is so other people could harass her.\par \par \uc2 Well, the person who runs Libs of TikTok just sat down with us and for the first time revealed her identity for a new episode of "\uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  Today." Here is part of it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LIBS OF TIKTOK CREATOR: People ask me all the time, this is one of the most common questions is if you could say one thing to Taylor, what would it be? Or if you can ask her one question. And I thought about this so much and I always -- I wasn't -- I was never sure how to answer the question and I thought about it a lot and then I realized the answer is I don't want to talk to her.\par \par \uc2 She is a bad person and she is toxic. And I don't want to -- we agree -- we disagree. Sorry, we disagree on everything. There is -- we have nothing in common. She is not a person I ever want to be in the same room with. I never want to be in her presence. So there's my answer. I don't want to talk to her.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So on Tuesday, we're going to take that off her face and you will see for the first time who runs Libs of TikTok. She will be public and we think a force in American media. That's going to happen Tuesday right here on this show. The whole interview drops that day on FOX Nation. We hope you watch.\par \par \uc2 So remember the fake outrage over the Christmas song "Baby it's Cold Outside," you are supposed to be very mad about that song. Part of a broader effort to destroy everything you grew up with that was good. Your history, your culture, but they told us at the time, it was #MeToo.\par \par \uc2 Well, comedian Tom Cotter remembers that very well and he noted that that song generated a lot more outrage among lifestyle liberals than a pop song about women's genitals. So Tom Cotter's bit on this is all over the internet, you may have seen it. If you haven't, here's part of it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TOM COTTER, COMEDIAN: And the one that really killed me was last Christmas, we canceled a song that was written in the 1940s called "Baby it's Cold Outside," which is fine if you feel that way, but the exact same time the number one song in this nation for over two months was "Wet [bleep]." I'm not making that up. You can look it up. Truthfully.\par \par \uc2 So I want to wrap up my show by comparing and contrasting the lyrics of these two songs, that's it, if indeed this country has lost its [bleep] mind, shall we?\par \par \uc2 Let's start with the hardly offensive Christmas song written just after World War Two.\par \par \uc2 "I really can't stay, baby, it's cold outside. I've got to go away, baby it's cold outside. This evening has been so very nice." Yes, you [bleep] with some wet [bleep] bucket and a mop for this wet [bleep]. Beat it up and work extra, large extra hard. Put this [bleep] right in your face, swipe your nose like a credit card.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So when you destroy people's culture, you replace it with something new, a new culture and he pointed it out what the new culture is and it is not just "Baby it's Cold Outside" because it's not just one song. It's everything you grew up with, everything that you thought made this country decent, all the happy memories from childhood are now banned.\par \par \uc2 So that would include Christmas carols like "God Rest Ye Weary Gentlemen." We found this video from 2020 of people singing the new woke version of "God Rest Ye Weary Gentlemen." Here it is.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TEXT: God rest you all so women with the wind against your face. Who think and plan, create, design and finish yet displaced. God rest you queer and questioning your anxious hearts be still. Believe that you are deeply known and part of God's good will.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So again, the point is not to make it any more inclusive, it is to destroy the things that you love.\par \par \uc2 Tom Cotter, of course knows that. Comedians are really insightful. That's why they are comedian.\par \par \uc2 Tom Cotter who just saw joins us now.\par \par \uc2 Tom, thanks so much for coming on. So what inspired you to compare yesterday's deeply offensive song with today's totally okay song?\par \par \uc2 COTTER: Yes, I'm not trying to bash anyone over the head with my politics, but I just think you've got to draw a line in the sand somewhere. Like, I consider Christmas a birthday party. It's a birthday party for the Baby Jesus and these people want to destroy a kid's birthday party, which I think is outrageous.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Right.\par \par \uc2 COTTER: They wake up in the morning waiting to be outraged. What can I be triggered by today so I can become a Christmas Karen and ruin it for everybody else? And how long before White Christmas is deemed racist or ho- ho-ho is offensive to people in the entertainment industry or candy canes are offensive to handicapped people?\par \par \uc2 You've got to draw a line somewhere or it is just going to get further and further out of control. And I'm just done with the woke people destroying it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, I completely agree. And ho-ho-ho is offensive to sex workers, as you know, but we say it anyway. So what's the response when you point this out in the hilarious way you do?\par \par \uc2 COTTER: Well, I've been eviscerated by some. You know, what kills me is it's young millennial men that are really coming after me. I thought it would be they maybe I'm sexist, but I thought it would be millennial women, but it is really the men that are coming after me and really taking shots at me on my posts and stuff.\par \par \uc2 But most people, the vast majority are positive because I think the vast majority believe as I do that, these are traditions that we hold dear that we've hold on to for our whole lives.\par \par \uc2 My kids have never asked what Santa's pronouns are. They don't care. You know what I mean? And what about the systematic oppression of the elves? When do we give them reparations? And how come the reindeer aren't more inclusive? They're all cisgender males. Aren't they -- well, Prancer, maybe but, you know, at some point, you just have to say no, there shouldn't be an elk or a caribou, they are reindeer. They went after "The Santa Clause" the movie by Tim Allen. They said it was fat shaming.\par \par \uc2 It's Santa. He's fat. Can we get over it? Can we just move on with our lives and not ruin it for kids?\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Tom Cotter, thank you.\par \par \uc2 COTTER: Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So the thing they hate most, of course, is actual Christianity because it suggests there is a power over, bigger than, more powerful than the people currently in charge and so Christianity is now effectively illegal in parts of Europe including in Christian Great Britain.\par \par \uc2 A woman there was just arrested for praying silently in front of an abortion clinic, not making that up. It's on video. She joins us next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MARIANNE RAFFERTY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Welcome to "FOX News Live," I am Marianne Rafferty in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Tens of millions of Americans facing bone-chilling temperatures as a winter storm sweeps the nation. More than 200 million Americans are under an advisory or warning tonight. That's according to the National Weather Service and more than a million people are without power.\par \par \uc2 The system has been mayhem for holiday travelers as nearly 5,000 flights have been canceled, while those who are hitting the roads to get to their destinations aren't faring any better. The massive storm is being dubbed by some meteorologists as a "once in a decade" weather event.\par \par \uc2 And lawmakers are now home for the Holidays, but not before the House passed a whopping $1.7 trillion spending bill. This Bill will prevent the government from running out of money at midnight. It will also send an additional $45 billion in aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 I'm Marianne Rafferty, now back to Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Here is an amazing story.\par \par \uc2 Isabel Vaughan-Spruce is the leader of 40 Days For Life Campaign in Birmingham, England. She is not a terrorist, she is the opposite. She is someone who prays a lot.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, she was praying silently outside an abortion clinic in Birmingham. She wasn't yelling or carrying a sign or blocking the doorway or doing anything disruptive. She was just praying, praying, not to the government, to God -- and that's not allowed anymore, so police approached her and arrested her and charged with violating a public space protection order and committing, "antisocial behavior," and we're not making this up. It was caught on video. Here it is.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 OFFICER: What are you here for today?\par \par \uc2 ISABEL VAUGHAN-SPRUCE, LEADER OF 40 DAYS FOR LIFE CAMPAIGN: Physically, I am just standing here.\par \par \uc2 OFFICER: Well, why here, of all places? I know you don't live nearby.\par \par \uc2 VAUGHAN-SPRUCE: This is an abortion center.\par \par \uc2 OFFICER: Are you praying?\par \par \uc2 VAUGHAN-SPRUCE: I might be praying in my head, not out loud.\par \par \uc2 OFFICER; So, I'll ask you once more, will you voluntarily come with us now to the police station? We need to ask you some questions about today and for the days where there are allegations that you've broken Public Places Protection Order?\par \par \uc2 VAUGHAN-SPRUCE: If I have got a choice, then no.\par \par \uc2 OFFICER: Okay, well, then, you're under arrest on suspicion of failing to comply with Public Spaces Protection Order.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Public Spaces Protection Order. Isabel Vaughan-Spruce joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Isabel, thank you so much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 VAUGHAN-SPRUCE: Thanks for having me.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So this order is designed -- the law is designed to protect public spaces from praying?\par \par \uc2 VAUGHAN-SPRUCE: Well, maybe -- maybe if I can give a bit of a background to this.\par \par \uc2 So for 20 years or around that, I've been going outside abortion centers, and praying there and offering help to women. I know well over a hundred women who have accepted our help and continued their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 But September this year, the local Council in Birmingham brought in this censorship zone, this PSPO. Formerly, these were used for dog or fouling and drunken behavior and things like that. But they're now popping up around the country, surrounding abortion centers and they ban behavior, like protesting. But it also names prayer and counseling as forms of protesting.\par \par \uc2 And so four times I went and stood near the closed abortion center, and silently prayed there. And as you can see, the police came and asked me if I was protesting, which I wasn't. They asked me if I was praying, I said, I might be silently praying.\par \par \uc2 I was arrested. I was searched. I was locked in a cell.\par \par \uc2 I was then interviewed or interrogated, however you'd like to see it, during which I was quizzed about what I was praying about. I was then released on bail, and then subsequently charged on four counts of protesting and engaging in an act intimidating of service users.\par \par \uc2 So I now stand on trial on February 2nd supported by ADF UK, really for freedom of thought. And the concern is here in England, the national buffer zones are now being discussed. So there is a possibility of every abortion center in this country having a similar zone around it and obviously, the implications of that are really concerning.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: If you're arresting people for praying, you are committing an act of evil. It's not a close call at all. There is sort of no debate about that. And I would think that even secular people would recognize that. Did anybody -- any prominent person step forward to defend you?\par \par \uc2 VAUGHAN-SPRUCE: I have had a lot of people who say they are pro-choice or that they support abortion, but they've also got concerns about this and that in itself is very encouraging to hear, that it's not necessarily about people who support abortion or don't support abortion. This is more to do with freedom of thought here. It is even going further than freedom of prayer.\par \par \uc2 I mean, we all talk about that the cancel culture and the concerns we have about people being canceled, you know, speaking in public, maybe public speaking engagements, but to be arresting somebody for what they are thinking, it's just going even a step further. It's just -- it's actually quite surreal, that's the word I'd use to describe it, and then the amount of people who have used the word Orwellian to me to describe this, likening it to the 1984 novel, and it really seemed like that to me from start to finish. And obviously, it's not over yet, but it's just quite a surreal experience.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, it's evil. It's an act of evil: Arresting someone for praying is an act of evil. Period. And it just breaks your heart to think of all the people in charge, your Prime Minister on down who are standing by and allowing this to happen and I'm just so glad that you did this. I hope you'll continue to do it. That's a human right. They can't take it away from you and I appreciate your telling us about it on this show.\par \par \uc2 Isabel Vaughan-Spruce, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Well, \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 , of course, is a scam artists. It looks like he pulled off the biggest financial fraud in history. He is already out of jail, though, on $250 million bond, which actually turned out to be fake. He didn't have to pay a cent.\par \par \uc2 His parents put up their relatively modest $4 million house as collateral and that somehow covered the quarter billion in bail. The remaining collateral apparently came from an unnamed relative and a friend. Another scam right in front of our faces.\par \par \uc2 How long before this guy flees to somewhere else?\par \par \uc2 Charlie Gasparino is a senior correspondent with FOX Business and followed this story from the beginning. He joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Charlie, what -- this seems like another kind of fraud perpetrated by a Court.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GASPARINO, FOX BUSINESS NETWORK SENIOR CORRESPONDENT: Listen, I laugh. This isn't a funny story. If you're out the money that was stolen from your FTX crypto account and used to gamble away in their side hustle, which was some sort of a hedge fund.\par \par \uc2 Listen, this is so bizarre. They should really release the names of the people who put up their houses or whoever they are, because we should know -- as you know, both \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 's mom and dad, Mrs. Fried and Mr. Bankman have very close ties to major people in the Democratic Party that the mom was a huge Democratic Party fundraiser.\par \par \uc2 I mean, for all I know, this is \uc2 George Soros\uc2 . I'm not saying it is \uc2 George Soros\uc2 . But if you can -- if I found out tomorrow that \uc2 George Soros\uc2  put up part of his bond, you know, by some house that he has, or someone like that, I would not be surprised because that is in the wheelhouse of this very lefty politically connected with rich people family.\par \par \uc2 So I mean, they shouldn't really release who these people are just so we get the full notice of how this guy is getting out of jail.\par \par \uc2 You know, here's the other thing, Tucker. They don't need him as a witness. There is no reason why they have to be nice to this guy and here is why. Caroline Ellison, his girlfriend or ex-girlfriend was part of the whole mess of FTX and the side hustle hedge fund. She has turned evidence and she said point blank in her charging documents that she cut a deal with the Feds, that me -- I conspired with \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 , I'm paraphrasing, to basically not disclose what we were doing on the hedge fund and prevent that from being aired.\par \par \uc2 That means he is toast, stick and fork in him, done. They don't need him.\par \par \uc2 I mean, you usually cut these deals with these guys like \uc2 Bernie Madoff\uc2 . Remember, Madoff admitted to everything. He cut a deal with the Feds to keep them out of jail. He gave them $10 million, which was nothing, but he was helping people find where those funds are.\par \par \uc2 They don't need this guy to help them find the funds.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: No, they don't.\par \par \uc2 GASPARINO: First of all, they are probably gone, just gambled away. So this is a big story. It's a weird side story to this whole thing. Why everybody -- why people in power are still being nice to this guy. It is bizarre.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: A million people defrauded by \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GASPARINO: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: And we can't know who put up the bond?\par \par \uc2 GASPARINO: The next \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  -- those names were hysterical by the way.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Carnegie, Harriman. No prison inmate.\par \par \uc2 Charlie Gasparino, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You, too, pal.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 So in order for your healthcare system to 