l calling himself Father and continue to celebrate mass since the Vatican's excommunication, or communication about this.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Father Frank Pavone, national director of Priests for Life. Father Pavone, it's good to see you, tonight. I know it's a very difficult time for you. You said you learned this from a news agency. Have you been formally notified by the Vatican?\par \par \uc2 REV. FRANK PAVONE, PRIESTS FOR LIFE NATIONAL DIRECTION: That's right. Laura, this is actually the culmination of 21 years of abuse by church authorities to me and to my ministry despite the fact that we help the Vatican. We help run some of the operations out of the Pope's mission to the United Nations. We help the secretary of state with international pro- life issues. We run the largest ministry for healing after abortion for which \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has personally encouraged me to keep going on it.\par \par \uc2 We do all kinds of other pro-life work with which many of our viewers are familiar. Why are they doing this? A lot of it obviously is connected with the cancel culture that comes against supporters of President Trump and critics of the Democrat Party. And we are only going to get louder about that. We are not going to be silenced. This is an effort -- this is not just an effort to silence me but to so many of us. People are losing their jobs, as you know, because they stand for their conservative values. They stand up for their conscience. And so they are trying to do the same within the church to priests like me. It's not going to work. The social media post is just an excuse. They've given me 21 years of excuses. It's always shifting sands. It's always changing goalposts, as you can well appreciate.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Let me ask one question, Father Pavone. I know your work, and you've done such amazing work over the years. But were you asked at one point to become a parish priest and you declined, did that actually occur?\par \par \uc2 PAVONE: Absolutely. That's how this started. The reason I say 21 years is that in 2001, Cardinal Egan, after I lead Priests for Life for eight years and also served at the Vatican for two of those years in the pro-life office under \uc2 John Paul II\uc2 , he said I want you to go do parish work. There was an uproar from the people. There wasn't only an objection from me. His office got inundated. And Priests for Life at that time was only a fraction of the size that we are now. And people said why can't a priest devote himself full-time to defending the unborn and ending abortion? I'm convinced that's part of my vocation. My vocation is to be a priest and to be a full-time pro-life leader, and I don't intend to walk away.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But as a priest, yes, but as a priest, Father Pavone, you have to go where the church tells you to go, correct? I know a lot of priests who didn't want to change parishes, but they were told they had to go to inner-city parish. We don't want to get into all the minutia because it's confusing. I've got to ask one other question, though, because you say that you want to appeal this. But they say there is no appeal process for what just happened. So what do you do?\par \par \uc2 PAVONE: If the Pope signs off on something, what they mean is there's nobody in the church above the Pope. We all understand that. But that doesn't mean there's no way to change this. The Pope himself can reverse it, the next Pope can reverse it. And the people, and I am appealing to the people of God to continue working with us and show their support for this work of saving lives and healing hearts. If the Pope closes the door on me, Laura, I'm going to be right there on the other side of that door waiting for it to open again. I'm not going to a different church. I'm a loyal Catholic. I'm a loyal priest. And this is not going to last because this is against all of us. And it's a cancel culture in the church. It's got to be exposed, and it's got to be resisted.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And meanwhile, Father James Martin, he gets meetings with the Pope, and he obviously is a fairly radical guy, and no problem there. Father, we really appreciate you and we're going to be following this story very closely. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Now, you may have heard a few rumors or seen some pictures. So I'm going to clear it all up for you nosey nellies. Up next, the man I spent my Saturday night with. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, so which bespectacled man did I spend my Saturday night with? Some of you guessed Roger Stone. Elton John? \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 ? Wrong. Wrong. Wrong.\par \par \uc2 Tucker and I and his amazing insistent Emily, we had a ball Saturday night. We flew from Turning Point's big Phoenix convention back to the east coast, got there in the wee hours of the morning back home. We ate junk food, a lot of junk food, swapped stories for five hours or so, unbelievable. Trivia question, though, whose glasses is Tucker wearing? Look at the reflection in the glass. We'll answer that incredibly important question on tomorrow night's show.\par \par \uc2 If you want to check out my Turning Point speech, go to FOXNation.com where you can stream right now.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us tonight.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020221220eicj00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Anti-Humanism At The Heart Of Modern Leftist Thought; Increasing Acceptance Of Euthanasia Isn't Normal; Assisted Suicide Has Become Encouraged Suicide; New York Times Promotes End Of Humanity; Biden's 'Europe First' Agenda; Bankman-Fried's Shameless Resurrection Campaign; Investment Firm \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  's Attempt To Steer Investment Towards Environmental, Social, And Governance Funds Examined; Analysts Debate The Current State Of American Economy Of Possibility Of Recession And Continued High Inflation; Republican Lieutenant Governor Of George Geoff Duncan Claims He Could Not Vote For Either Candidate In Senate Runoff Election\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, New Gingrich \par \uc2 7,409 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 December 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2  , FOX NEWS HOST: Please set your DVR so you never, ever, ever, ever miss an episode of "HANNITY". For news anytime, all the time, every time, go to foxnews.com, Hannity.com. And, in the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Laura Ingraham and THE INGRAHAM ANGLE is next. You're going to make fun of me tonight. The South (ph) American flag tie. You're going to make fun of that.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: I know. I was just going to say you're looking very Yankee Doodle Dandy, right, the tie. It's very good. I like it a lot.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Even a compliment from you has a little dig behind it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A little bit. You can't be too nice to Hannity, always have to like just a needle on a little bit. Like, what else do we do? Hey, I have a question for you, a serious question.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. What's the question?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do you think Republicans are doing enough for \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  in Georgia? Do you think there--\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Some are. And, look, it's really up to the people of Georgia right now. All the arguments have been made. Everybody in Georgia either going to get a radical Warnock that supports \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  100 percent of the times, or that's it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. All right. Well, we know--\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: (inaudible) probably could do more.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Well, I think are the early voting deficit for Republicans has got to be addressed. If that's not fixed, then we're never going to win an election. So, I certainly hope that is fixed. But, I enjoyed that interview with Herschel. That was excellent.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, I hope he wins. He would be a great Senator.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You bet. Hannity, it's great to see you, and I will pick it up where you left off. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is THE INGRAHAM ANGLE from Washington tonight. The anti-humans, that's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Now, there are so many causes trying to get your attention during the year, like, advocating for animal rights, maybe for the Second Amendment, abortion, for veterans. But, you probably didn't know that there is a movement that's actively lobbying for the end of the human race.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DR. PHIL MCGRAW, HOST, "DR. PHIL": You're involved with an extinction movement.\par \par \uc2 LES KNIGHT, FOUNDER, THE VOLUNTARY HUMAN EXTINCTION MOVEMENT: Correct.\par \par \uc2 MCGRAW: You basically say we just need to live long and die out. We just need to feed, not breed. Is that what you are saying?\par \par \uc2 KNIGHT: Don't breed them. Yes, that's right. My plan is for everyone to think before they procreate, and if we all stop procreating, we will go extinct slowly. We can clean up our messes as we go. And, the biosphere, what's left of it will have a chance to recover.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, Gramps. Well, the "Voluntary Human Extinction Movement" is essentially a Wacko Consortium, kind of an environmental group, that believes man is killing the planet, and therefore that man has to die off in order to save the planet. Les Knight, who you just saw there, founded the organization, and feels very altruistic for having gotten a vasectomy at the ripe old age of 25. Now, he claims that childlessness would give the last humans the opportunity to live in a world comparable to the Garden of Eden. And, he claims that procreation today is de facto child abuse. And, of course, being a hippie from the 70s, he thinks people like him are victims.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KNIGHT: Hundreds of millions of couples are denied their right to not procreate. They do not have the contraceptive services, reproductive health services that they need. Those are not provided. Try to get a sterilization here in America when you haven't had kids and you're only 22.\par \par \uc2 MCGRAW: That's true.\par \par \uc2 KNIGHT: We're not allowing people to not breed.\par \par \uc2 MCGRAW: Do you see people--\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, Les. Maybe only the stupid people should die out. Now, he may seem extreme and he is, but this ideology is actually growing. The Atlantic recently noted that from Silicon Valley boardrooms to rural communities to academic philosophy departments, a seemingly inconceivable idea is being seriously discussed, that the end of humanity's reign on earth is imminent, and that we should welcome it. Anti-humanism is inspired by revulsion at humanity's destruction of the natural environment. And, some anti-humanist thinkers look forward to the extinction of our species, while others predict that even if some people survive the coming environmental apocalypse, civilization, as a whole, is doomed.\par \par \uc2 Then, there is another gem called transhumanism. It propounds that the only way forward for humanity is to create new forms of intelligent life that will no longer be Homo sapiens, I guess, think robots and things happening in the metaverse. Now, crusaders for climate change, abortion, euthanasia, gender fluidity, they all lead eventually, they're thinking, to the devaluing of human life. So, at its core of being anti-human, it means being anti-truth, because it involves the questioning or denying of objective facts, including those at the very heart of our existence.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MATT WALSH, HOST, "THE MATT WALSH SHOW: You stood up here and said transwomen are women.\par \par \uc2 ADDISON (PH): Yes.\par \par \uc2 WALSH\uc2  : Tell me what you mean. What is a -\par \par \uc2 WALSH\uc2  : Tell me what you mean. What is a woman?\par \par \uc2 ADDISON: Womanhood is something that, just as you explained, I cannot define because I am not myself.\par \par \uc2 WALSH\uc2  : But, you used the word. So, what did you mean when you said trans women are women, if you don't know what it means?\par \par \uc2 ADDISON: So, here is the thing. So, I do not define what a woman is because I do not identity as a woman. Womanhood is something that is an umbrella term. It includes people who--\par \par \uc2 WALSH\uc2  : That describes what?\par \par \uc2 ADDISON: People who identify as a woman.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, when asked simple questions, the cult of gender deviancy collapses into meaningless slogans and blather. None of it makes any sense, but it's deeply anti-human. Now, it's same with so much of what we hear from the Church of Global Warming. William Happer, Professor of Physics at Princeton refers to it as the Carbon Cult. And, remember, carbon is essential in both the production of food and overall nutrition for us. It's impossible without carbon dioxide, and a lot of carbon dioxide is necessary to feed the planet. But, remember, a lot of powerful people secretly agree with Mr. Knight that there are too many humans around anyway, and they're the problem.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): Our planet is going to hit disaster if we don't turn this ship around. And so, it's basically like there is a scientific consensus that the lives of children are going to be very difficult. And, it does lead, I think, young people to have a legitimate question, should - is it OK to still have children?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, the battle to kill off oil and gas is actually a battle against life itself, because cheap abundant energy makes more life possible. But, these forces, the ones we're discussing, they don't want more life, at least not human life. Now, look at the story we brought you earlier this week, the sick obsession in Canada with not just euthanasia but in streamlining access to it. Now, in Canada, one in 30 deaths are due to assisted suicide, and it's even promoted by corporations in weird sleek promotional campaigns.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, this isn't assisted suicide. It is encouraged suicide, sold ironically as a human right. For years now, choosing when life should end, essentially playing God, is marketed as the godly thing to do.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JEREMY MAKE, HEALTHCARE CONSULTANT: Just as I choose a ship to sailing or house to live in, so I choose a death for my passage from life. Nowhere should we indulge the soul more than in dying. Let it go as it lists. If it craves the sword or the news (ph) or some portion that constricts its veins on with it, let it break the chain of slavery.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Slavery, life is slavery. Here in America, 10 states in Washington, D.C. already permit assisted suicide. And, in Oregon, the death lobby is so