\par \uc2 WESLEY J. SMITH, CONTRIBUTOR, NATIONAL REVIEW: Yes, and I was really glad you made such a broad - so many broad examples of what we're talking about, because these are all connected into a belief of human unexceptionalism, and it's extremely unhealthy. I mean, we wonder why our children are having a suicide crisis. Why there is so much depression, drug addiction, and so forth, when you have so many people over so many different kinds of issues, pushing the idea that human beings are wrong, that we shouldn't be here, that there is something wrong with us, that paradise - a paradise without Adam and Eve would be better, but paradise without Adam and Eve, nobody would know it was paradise. It's just really sad, and it's really nihilistic.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, more about this Les Knight character that \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  profiled. They described him as, "Tall and gentle", he comes across as a clear-eyed and thoughtful, like a mash-up of Bill Nye and Fred Rogers. While Mr. Knight may be against the creation of more humans, he shows great compassion for the ones that already exist. A high school substitute teacher, Knight is fondly regarded by students." Wesley, this is the - I mean, you can't pay for a press like that from \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  . That's a - that's pretty good.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: You see this across issue after issue where the mainstream media really does push things like suicide parties, euthanasia, dying on your own terms. But, they haven't thought about the dogs, Laura. If we're all dead, who is going to take care of the dogs? The dogs need us and love us. So, they're being very cruel to animals.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Right now, how do you, as a political party, which of course the Democrats embrace so many of these ideals, how do you push this idea that you want life better on Earth when so much of your adherence actually believe that life is the problem on Earth?\par \par \uc2 SMITH: That's a very interesting question, and why so many people seem to be attracted to this. I think that there is a sense of despair and a sense of hopelessness that's abounding in society. And, what the transhumanists are doing, for example, is a worship of technology. That is, we are all going to die. Oh, no, my Gosh, we are going to die. So, we're going to have technology save us, and we're going to live forever by being uploaded into a computer.\par \par \uc2 But, if you're uploaded into a computer, you're not in that computer. There is a computer program in that computer, you're dead. But, it just is a sense of - if all we are is carbon molecules, what's the point, and that's where transhumanism comes in. That's where radical environmentalism comes in, which is becoming an Earth worship. And, the rejection of human exceptionalism is something that drives people crazy, and we start eating our own tails.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Wesley, it is shocking, but this is the logical conclusion. This is where it all ends up, fewer people, fewer consumption - less consumption and less life. Wesley, thank you.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And, switching gears, the big story in Washington tonight is the Biden White House's state dinner, hosting French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  . But, the news happened earlier today after Macron kicked and screamed over Biden's "Made in America" pledge, and the president responded with a big French kiss.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: There is tweaks that we can make that can fundamentally make it easier for European countries to participate and/or be on their own. But, that is something that is a matter to be worked out. I never intended to exclude folks who were cooperating with us. We're back in business. Europe is back in business. And, we are going to continue to create manufacturing jobs in America, but not at the expense of Europe.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, the climate change bill, which was erroneously named the Inflation Reduction Act, was sold to America in large part because of all of its "Made in America" provisions. But, you can see, the moment Emanuel complained, Biden backed away from that.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Newt Gingrich, former Speaker of the House, Fox News Contributor. Newt, Europe says jump, and Biden says how high. Your reaction tonight.\par \par \uc2 NEWT GINGRICH\uc2  , FORMER SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE, & FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Why should we be surprised? As long as it weakens America, Biden is for it, whether it's selling oil to - buying oil from Venezuela or it's appeasing the Chinese or it's any one of 100 other things. So, why wouldn't he also try to appease the French? "Made in America" to Biden, is a slogan, not a policy, and he is happy to give that slogan up if it makes his many friends around the world happy.\par \par \uc2 I think people need to recognize that there is the Biden at the press conference, and there is the Biden in the real policies. And, the real policies are virtually always designed to undermine and weaken America. And, I think his meeting with Macron is just one more example of that. When in doubt, sell out America, embrace the Europeans. When in doubt, sell in America and brace the Chinese. Just go down the list.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Newt, it's pretty obvious that the Europe is pretty happy that Biden is president, because when Trump went over there, he was very demanding. He demanded that Europe actually live up to its obligations under the NATO Treaty to give two percent of its GDP to defense, military spending. And, I believe none of the countries - maybe one of the countries has met its obligation. But, now, that's all out the window.\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Look, I think you have to recognize, if you were like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , actually committed to fighting for America, then a lot of countries, who had been ripping us off, were going to be really unhappy, whether they were Mexico or China, or the entire \uc2 European Union\uc2  . And, the fact is that when the American economy is rolling, when we're encouraging entrepreneurs, when we're creating new jobs and new products and new capabilities, nobody else in the world can compete with us.\par \par \uc2 And so, all of them decide that they're unhappy, because in order for Europe to compete with us, they would have to change their welfare state. They'd have to change their bureaucracies. They'd have to go through so much change that it's better for them just to hate America. And, along comes \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  . And, Biden basically says, let me do everything I can to make sure that you're happy, and if that means I have to sell out American workers and American values and American interest, well, what the heck? After all, we're the elite, and these are just everyday people, and why would we pay attention to them? And, I think that's the heart of what you're seeing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Newt, great to see you tonight. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 And, the media and Wall Street are looking to provide a soft landing for the crypto fraudster \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2  . Why is that? Plus, another big loss for the investing scam known as ESG. The details on that, happily next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANDREW ROSS SORKIN\uc2  , COLUMNIST, THE NEW YORK TIMES: What are your lawyers telling you right now? Are they suggesting this is a good idea for you to be speaking?\par \par \uc2 SAM BANKMAN-FRIED, FOUNDER & FORMER CEO, FTX: No. They're very much not. And, I mean, you know the classic advice, right? Don't say anything.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The most remarkable aspect of the \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2  saga, aside from the massive theft and fraud, has been the resurrection campaign for the liberal wunderkind. Now, what all those elites revealed by kind of laughing off the immense pain caused by SBF is something about themselves. They're in on the game. And, it didn't end at the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  ' Dealbook Summit. George Stephanopoulos didn't just fly down to the Bahamas for a sit down. ABC's GMA saw fit to produce a slip promo that any celeb who got busted with a hooker would get.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Why did they always do the voices like that? But, it isn't just the media. Some of the biggest Wall Street and investing honchos are getting in on the sympathy game as well. Billionaire investor and hedge fund manager \uc2 Bill Ackman\uc2  tweeted, "Call me crazy, but I think SPF is telling the truth". Shark Tank's \uc2 Kevin O'Leary\uc2  agreed, saying "I lost millions as an investor in FTX, and got sandblasted as a paid spokesperson for the firm. But, I'm in the Aquaman camp about the kid."\par \par \uc2 So, it's here that you have to start asking yourself, why are all these people working overtime to provide this kid with a soft PR landing? Well, I have an easy answer. He is part of their brand. He is their investment. Think about it. Now, he is the son of liberal professors who gave generously to the Democrats. He goes down in a blaze of glory, so too do they.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now, Chris Bedford, Executive Editor of the Common Sense Society. Chris, seeing all this, you almost start to get the feeling that the Sam Bankman-Friend freak is going to get away with it. Do you?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS BEDFORD, EXECUTIVE EDITOR, COMMON SENSE SOCIETY: And, certainly, he started to wonder that if he is going to get away with that, he has got so many defenders, so many people from the media which is - by the way, he was basically the first cryptocurrency to be covered positively at all by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  because of exactly what you said, the club he belongs to, from people in business who are trying to save face, everyone is just wishing this should go away.\par \par \uc2 But, this is a different kind of scheme that we're looking at here. This is not just simply some another criminal, \uc2 Bernie Madoff\uc2  . Those guys have always existed. The conman, Madoff, of course, got a lot more money than most conmen get. But, those guys have always existed, just playing off of people's greed and using their trust. What makes Sam different, we have a piece coming out in our \uc2 Substack\uc2  of the Common Sense Society tomorrow about this.\par \par \uc2 What makes him different is he is - he was trafficking in something that's new in American circles, trafficking in virtue signaling. If you want to give to - if you want to be an investor in his company, you're part of the Effective Altruism group. You're making the world a better place. You're not just getting rich. You're not just buying a massive mansion, like he did, and some kind of tax haven and throwing sex parties there. You're actually a good person. It makes you feel good. All these people buy into that. And, right now, you can rise in American society or post says, just by that kind of virtue signaling. It's a new kind of status symbol you can attain, and that's what he was selling, and that's what people are so desperate to defend.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And, in one of those interviews, he was kind of blowing off the ESG model saying that, essentially, people are just checking boxes, and it doesn't really have any positive effect on the world. So, that was an interesting moment when he kind of like - well, that - that that doesn't really mean anything.\par \par \uc2 BEDFORD: He is in on this game. He has admitted in some private chats that have since been leaked, that a lot of this was just part of a really effective marketing strategy. He put himself up to the government as an expert on how to regulate cryptocurrency. He put himself out to the press as not only someone who had paid for lavish trips with them, but someone who could talk to them, who could be cool like them, be part of their club. That was all part of it. And, ESG is another kind of scam, exactly, something that just basically employs people to be good virtue checkers inside of your company, allows left- politics in your company and puts business interests in common sense in second place.\par \par \uc2 It's another scam. He recognizes that. But, as long as his virtue signaling is still a way to gain status, as long as the CEO of \uc2 Disney\uc2  can ignore their customers, or Tim Cook can ignore the American conservatives and Christians while doing business with China, as long as those sort of things to continue, this virtue - fake virtue signaling will continue as well.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Bankman-Fried also gave generously not just to Democrats but to liberal publications like Vox and \uc2 Ben Smith\uc2  startup Semafor. So, he was asked about this. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BANKMAN-FRIED: I think media matters a lot, and I want to support good media ventures. That was the whole thesis there. And, I don't have, like, governance over any of these. I was looking to support journalists doing great work, because I think what they do is really important.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Really important work, like, giving him more glossy profiles or helping him out on the PR side.\par \par \uc2 BEDFORD: It's so open. It's so flagrant. It's kind of wild. It's impressive how flagrant he is to hand over all these, all this money to journalists in exchange for good coverage. I mean, that's part of the game and a large part of the journalism industry. They pretend that they're martyrs that they're out there. They're risking their lives. They're risking their tails. In reality, they're taking money from Corporate America to whisper things back to Corporate America that it wants to hear.\par \par \uc2 And, Corporate America has got a problem here, because Sam is not the only person absolutely skirting the rules here. Sam is not the only person who wasn't being supervised. This is a problem throughout finance. This is a problem with \uc2 Google\uc2  ads. This is a problem in a lot of Corporate America, and they definitely don't want to see too much - too many people poking around it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Chris, great to see you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Now, one fraud to another, the scourge of, as I just mentioned, the environmental, social and governance standards or so-called standards, ESG investing will lead to America's economic ruin eventually. Yet, their Pied Piper of the scam, \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  's \uc2 Larry Fink\uc2  was still out this week defending the practice.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LARRY FINK\uc2  , CEO, BLACKROCK: There is a lot of noise, and it really does fill the airwaves. And so, it fills up the time on the airwaves about the attacks from some states, to me specifically, and to the firm. The reality is the majority, the unheard unspoken majority, really like what we're doing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He is such a blowhard. Just hours after those comments, Florida pulled $2 billion worth of assets from \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  , the largest divestment of its kind. Now, to date, Republican-led states have pulled nearly $4 billion from multiple states from the asset managing giant.\par \par \uc2 Now, joining us now is one of the first to draw attention to this tactic, West Virginia State Treasurer Riley Moore. Now, Riley, \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  , I think manages about $8 trillion in assets. So, a couple of billion here or there is not going to break the bank, obviously. But, doesn't this foreshadow problems for the politicization of Corporate America given what this is going to do to shareholders; interests.\par \par \uc2 RILEY MOORE, WEST VIRGINIA STATE TREASURER: Laura, absolutely. And thanks for having me on again. Look, we've had now six states, Florida has now joined. West Virginia was the first state to divest from \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  . This is a growing movement in pushback along ESG and woke capitalism. We know ESG is a scam. It does not work. I think as we saw here just recently, you had \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  actually close one of their ESG ETF because that was a lack of interest in it. The people are speaking on this and they are going to pay the price. And you said $8 trillion assets under management. I want to be clear, just earlier this year that was $10 trillion. They have lost $2 trillion because of this faulty and phony ESG investing scheme.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  CEO Fink isn't just popping up on the ESG issue but political movements as well. Check it out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LARRY FINK\uc2  , \uc2 BLACKROCK\uc2  CEO: Unfortunately, the long-term is not something that is a topical today. And let's be clear, populism is not about long- termism. Populism is about the moment. And let me be clear, one of the greatest reasons we have inflation is because of populism. We are doing things for the short term.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, they are really threatened by the America First movement, by economic populism. They are all about one global governance system of which ESG is just part of the equation. Does this make sense to you?\par \par \uc2 MOORE: Absolutely not. It is very clear that \uc2 Larry Fink\uc2  and the other elite globalists out there have a God complex, obviously. They feel like they're the masters of the universe, but people like me, an America First conservative, I only have one master of the universe, and that's God. And we're not going to let these folks continue to destroy the free capitalist system here in America, which has made us the greatest nation on the face of the planet. They think we're thinking in the short term. We are thinking about the future of our children. We actually like children, unlike some of these folks, obviously.\par \par \uc2 So we're