: Oh, why? Why should we hold anyone to anything? Why rush? That's not important about this. And you know, the defenders of democracy, you really have to worry about them, because they're working very long hours.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: To those people who are demanding that we work that we move - move faster with count, they are already working 14 hours to 18 hours a day. We can't go any further than that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We can't go any faster. Now, if democracy is really on the line, like Biden said before they thought they outperform why didn't they have the infrastructure in place to handle this? And they were getting very snippy today. I noticed at their press conference.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Why is it taking the amount of time this taking I'm here to tell you the goalposts have changed? All right. And the reason that the goalposts have change is because wonderful news that we had 290,000 mail in ballots dropped off at our vote centers on Election Day that broke the previous record by 70 percent.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Why didn't you have the staff in place and you think Republican Governor Ducey would have fixed this mess? Same day, mail in, drop off voting, sounds nifty, but not if you can't count the votes, again, not rocket science. Now I realize that they have to follow these idiotic rules that Arizona has in place. But this screwed up system is so corrosive, it just it chips away at the public's confidence in inaccurate outcomes, right. They want accurate outcomes, but don't think they're getting them.\par \par \uc2 But of course, pretty much everyone in the press will brand any objection raised by any Republican about almost any aspect of voting as wacky, election denier conspiracy theory stuff? Well, I say too bad. There are legitimate reasons for Americans of both parties to be concerned about ho