e'll have you on soon. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Now could Kevin McCarthy is path to the speakership be tougher than he realizes. Up next we speak to Freedom Caucus Member of Bob Good, who says he still hasn't earned the vote. Plus, why does the destruction of the nuclear family plays such an outsized role in the future success of the Democrats party? Some new data has the answers. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Republican voters are putting out an All-Points Bulletin, Wanted, leaders who actually like the base voters they purportedly represent. OK, but too often, we've had leaders who not only ignore their own voters, but basically despise them.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STEELE, FORMER RNC CHAIRMAN: You have Republicans who want to turn back the clock on civil rights, women's rights, human rights. And I think that should be the focus.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Michael Steele was the Former Chairman of the \uc2 RNC\uc2  during Obama, but he's not alone.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. LIZ CHENEY (R-WY): I think that you saw in really important races around the country, people coming together to say we believe in democracy and a real rejection of the toxicity and the hate and the vitriol and of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Until May of last year, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  was the number three Republican in the House. Republicans now have to fill every position and leadership from the House to the Senate, with people who have a proven track record of accomplishment and whose views are aligned with a Republican base.\par \par \uc2 Now, Republicans always say they believe in merit, and that people should earn what they get. So let's apply these principles here. You want to be in leadership, then get on TV and convince Americans to vote for the Republican Party. Don't be afraid to stand up to the President or your colleagues, don't cower on any bills of Americans are getting the shaft, but you're getting some ridiculous promise from Democrats that they never intend to keep.\par \par \uc2 And know that if you agree with someone like \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  on policy, then you probably shouldn't be in leadership. And you'll get voted out the next time around. So it's incredibly important that the right leader someone who is America first who believes in the conservative movement is picked when Republicans officially take the house. Now, Kevin McCarthy is already trying to get the speaker's gavel. But he's running into the same challenges that derailed him back in 2015, The House Freedom Caucus.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. KEVIN MCCARTHY (R-CA): I'm not concerned think about this. Since I've been leader for the last four years, we've only gained seats. It's the goal of winning the majority, we won the majority. I think I accomplished the goal that we wanted to, people could have input, we want to have a very open input process. We're going to have a smaller majority. So we're going to find that we work together.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: House Freedom Caucus Member and Virginia Congressman, Bob Good joins me now. Congressman, should Kevin McCarthy be concerned tonight? Is there rumblings afoot in the Freedom Caucus that you need to go in another direction?\par \par \uc2 REP. BOB GOOD (R-VA): He absolutely should be concerned. His only priority the last two years has seemed to be able to get the majority and become speaker just for the sake of having the majority becoming speaker. He's essentially had a two year audition where he had the exclusive opportunity to earn the vote of the conference to demonstrate that he was willing to fight against the Biden, Pelosi, Schumer agenda, and he failed to do that. In all across the country, Republican voters continue to tell me and other members of Congress and candidates that they don't support Kevin McCarthy because he's not a true conservative and they want someone that will fight. There's many examples in the past two years where he's failed to do that.\par \par \uc2 When I came in as a new freshman two years ago, he told our freshman class, hey, we're going to control the floor, that the majority number is so small with only five or six majority for the Democrats, that we're going to control the floor, because we're going to lead the fight. We're going to be united in our fight. And over and over he's failed to respond to our efforts to fight as a minority when there's no real pressure like there will be in the majority.\par \par \uc2 He didn't support our efforts to vacate the chair when \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  was at her weakest moments. He didn't support our efforts to request recorded votes. He didn't support our efforts to fight suspension bills. He has not supported our efforts to fight against the NDAA when we had the leverage to block it as Republicans because Democrats couldn't pass it, a bad NDAA bill without Republican votes. On issue after issue and time after time, he has failed to support our efforts to fight, truly fight against an oppressive Democrat majority.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, you caucus is pushing McCarthy to restore the motion to vacate, that's the House rule recently ditched by the Democrats. It allows a single member to force a vote on the speakership at any given time. How big of a sticking point is that for your caucus?\par \par \uc2 GOOD: Yes, we gave him a rules package. We asked him two months ago to change the rules of Congress, when we get the majority, to change the Republican rules, the rules of our conference, and to change the rules of Congress to empower regular members. One of those being able to vacate the chair. A secure, confident leader understands that he or she has the trust of the support of those they purport to lead and they're not threatened by that.\par \par \uc2 But that was a rule that was in place in the 115th Congress until \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  changed it. But we want other changes. Amendments from the floor if 10 percent Republicans support it, a majority of the majority rule where he can't pass legislation that a majority of Republicans don't support, that we get to elect our own chairman of our respective committees, that we have the Holman rule that would allow to us defund certain agencies or departments or even salaries of individuals that are violating the oath of their office. There's rules that we want to change to empower regular members instead of having the control with a few elites at the top like we currently have in the Democrat majority. We shouldn't have that under a Republican majority either.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, is there anyone else's whose name is floating out there that would want to be speaker?\par \par \uc2 GOOD: I can tell you that there absolutely will be a challenge to Kevin McCarthy's leadership bid when we have our organizational meetings next week, and the intent on November 15 when that is scheduled to be will be to demonstrate that he doesn't have near 218 votes, and then that opens it up for anyone to be considered on January 3rd. And I think there's a lot of members of Congress who will be interested in being speaker once it's clear that Kevin McCarthy does not have the required 218 votes\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, we're going to invite Kevin McCarthy on to respond to some of your criticism. I look forward to hearing what he has to say. But Congressman, thank you. We're up to date on that now.\par \par \uc2 Up next, I reveal why the Democrats are pushing so hard for the destruction of the American family, plus a shocking revelation about the role the \uc2 FBI\uc2  played in January 6th. Details in moments.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: One of the most extraordinary thing about the Dobbs decision is what was about to challenge American women when the justice said they have it in their power, basically saying let's see what they're going to do. Guess what? You all showed up and beat the hell out of them.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How lovely. If you ever wondered why the Democrat Party works so hard to push abortion and bring about the deterioration of the nuclear family, look no further than these election results from Tuesday. Married men broke for Republicans by 20 points. Married women broke for Republicans by 14 points. And while unmarried men still broke for Republicans, it was only by seven points. But unmarried women, they went Democrat by a mind blowing 37 points.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Kira Davis, editor-at-large of RedState, host of the "Just Listen to Yourself" podcast. Kira, by 2010 for the first time in our country's history, most households did not include a married couple and marriage only continued to decline since then. So is this the democrats' new, I don't know, soccer moms? What is this?\par \par \uc2 KIRA DAVIS, REDSTATE, WRITER AND EDITOR-AT-LARGE: It's always been this way, hasn't it, right? We've seen this in the black community. This was the Democrats' strategy in the black community that has effectively destroyed the American black community. And there were many people warning about those issues bubbling up and spreading out into general America and they have.\par \par \uc2 But we've seen the what the destruction of the nuclear family does in black America. And we also -- it's also not coincidental that black America does vote very heavily towards Democrats. You need a strong nuclear family to have strong principles, to have a strong character. And if you don't have a family that's providing for you, then you're going to go seek out someone to provide for you. And in the case of a lot of single women, that's the government.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And former \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  adviser Symone Sanders had something to say today about the abortion issue.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SYMONE SANDERS, MSNBC CONTRIBUTOR: We heard for weeks post Kansas how Democrats overcalculated on roe, abortion is not a kitchen table issue. And if you are a woman, a person with a daughter, a man in this country, it is a kitchen table issue for you. Abortion is an economic issue, and we are seeing that borne out in the data and the votes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Kira, what do you make of this push to make abortion just an economic issue, like a child is just a number?\par \par \uc2 DAVIS: It's morbid. It really is. It's very, it's very disturbing. And as a black woman, to hear a black woman saying that basically she's advocating for fewer black women in the world, yes, I have a problem with that. And since the dawn of humanity, families have been the key to economic success. At one time, you needed a big family to help work and support the family. But now families are the keys to making us mature, making us in to the type of people who want to care for our communities, who want to care for our schools and our government entities.\par \par \uc2 So the family isn't just about a mom, a dad, kids, and people holding hands and maybe trying to do their best imitation of leave it to beaver. The family is literally the basis of a stable and thriving society. So it's no wonder that America is in a lot of chaos right now, because you look around, and the nuclear family is in a ton of chaos.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And no wonder it's a threat to the Democrat Party. Kira, thank you. Great to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 Now, there's evidence that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  tonight knew about January 6th months before it happened and did nothing. While everyone was focused on the midterms Tuesday, "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " conveniently dropped this piece saying an "Informant likely to testify as defense witness in Oath Keeper's sedition trial. A man who served as the group's number two is said to have secretly reported to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in the months leading up to January 6th."\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Julie Kelly, senior writer for "American Greatness" and author of "January 6, How Democrats Used the Capitol Protest to Launch a War on Terror against the Political Right." Julie, this certainly is a stunning little detail, lending credence to a lot of the work in your book.\par \par \uc2 JULIE KELLY, "AMERICAN GREATNESS" SENIOR WRITER: It certainly is quite a bombshell. The idea that the number two, who they called the vice president of the Oath Keepers, this alleged militia group that participated in the events of January 6th, the idea that he was working with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  as an informant for months before January 6th is pretty explosive.\par \par \uc2 And Laura, as you know because you and I have talked about this, this mirrors the \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  fed-napping hoax where the top \uc2 FBI\uc2  informant who was paid roughly $60,000 for his work also was the number two, the commanding officer of an alleged militia group involved in that case. And he used his position to lure people into this entrapment scheme. So once again, we have a comparison between the Whitmer fed-napping hoax, which involved dozens of \uc2 FBI\uc2  supervising agents, informants, and undercover agents, another comparison between that and the events of January 6th.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Julie, we're going to continue to follow this. And I know there's a pretrial detention finally lifted for 20 months when a former marine was in pretrial detention for 20 months after January 6th. That also happened this week. Julie, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is confident Tuesday put him in the driver's seat for 2024. But some of his media cheerleaders not so certain.\par \par \uc2 Plus, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just levelled a bizarre attack on \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , setting up more 2024 drama. Charlie Kirk, \uc2 Hogan Gidley\uc2  react in moments.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: While Biden thinks Tuesday night helps cement his status as the Dems 2024 frontrunner, some of his fiercest allies in the media are floating potential replacements.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This is a guy, you know who he is, you know what you're getting, and that ultimately matters in politics.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Fetterman as a nominee at some point for president.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , a top Democrat suggested to me, watch for \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  in years in the future to run for president.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What is \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  going to do with her war chest? She has a lot of money left over. And she's already signaled she's not going to go quietly and intends to fight for democracy in this country.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And she might be a presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, please, we beg you, any of you, run for president, please. You can even throw Beto or Mayor Pete into the race.\par \par \uc2 Now, they're also talking about Democrat governors who are total disasters for their states, but of course they got reelected, like Newsom, Whitmer, and a new one, Illinois Governor \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2 . Some in party circles have viewed him as a viable national candidate due to his strong stances on progressive issues and his essentially bottomless financial well of resources. Bottomless also could describe his favorite type of buffet. Wait a second, who wrote that?\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Charlie Kirk, founder and president of Turning Point USA, and author of "The College Scam," and \uc2 Hogan Gidley\uc2 , former White House deputy press secretary. Charlie, many of these people are the embodiment of big government, OK, speaking of Pritzker. But it doesn't same like Biden's pals are so sure of his status as the frontrunner.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE KIRK, TURNING POINT USA FOUNDER: You know, Laura, when you said Pritzker, I said he's never run for anything in his life. I'm being mean. I'll stop. When it comes to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , I think he's going to misread the results earlier this week. First of all, it's great the Republicans are going to take the House. That's great news. But \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , I think, is going to say, look, it could have gone a lot worse and therefore I'm going to run. His approval ratings are very, very low. And I say this as someone who wants to take the White House back in 2024, I hope he runs again. He has no enthusiasm, no energy.\par \par \uc2 And not to mention, Republicans are leading in the national congressional House popular vote. This is the buried lead from Tuesday. It's not manifesting itself in as many seats as we would have thought, but Republicans in the national popular vote actually did very, very well. And because of weird maps and gerrymandering rules and a lot of other things happening in states, it just didn't play out the way that some people thought in the projections. But \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  running in 2024 I think would be a gift for Republicans whoever is on the top of the ticket.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Hogan?\par \par \uc2 HOGAN GIDLEY, FORMER WHITE HOUSE DEPUTY PRESS SECRETARY: Yes, he's absolutely right. Look, all these candidates you just mentioned are exactly the same. They all want big government, top down control over you. They all want to raise taxes. They all want to defund the police. They put the American people and the American priorities last. Talk about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . She's less popular now as vice president than she was as a candidate, and she ranked eighth among African American voters behind the fake Indian Elizabeth Warren and \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 . She once called \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a sex criminal and a segregationist on a debate stage. And who is