governor's race there to obviously. There's more work that needs to be done. But from Oregon to New York, and of course in Florida, we made big progress. Since we know Democrat policies are only going to drive crime and the cost of living higher in all of these States in the next few years, Republican prospects and recruiting should just continue to improve in all the States.\par \par \uc2 Third, there is no reason to believe that a more establishment approach would have done better and most of the Senate races. Now while many Trump back candidates did lose, McConnell's favorite candidate in Colorado, Joe O'Dea got annihilated.\par \par \uc2 And then think about this \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  he fought off Romney's preferred candidate in Utah, Trump hater Evan McMullin. Murkowski she's behind in Alaska, but J.D. Vance he won in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Fourth, the runoff in Georgia could very well decide who controls the Senate and whether Biden gets another Supreme Court nominee. So anyone who thinks of himself or herself as a major player in the GOP should be planning to go down there and win this election. It's far more important than pointing fingers about who won and who won last night. The Democrats line on this today in Georgia was pathetic.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALICIA MENENDEZ, AMERICAN VOICES: I keep looking at Georgia right now. And it is shocking to me that \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  who can barely put two sentences together sometimes says things that don't make any kind of sense or search them with a lot of bravado, tells lies is rude to people is doing so well.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, well, she's talking about \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  can't put two sentences together. This is the party of Biden and apparently now \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . I think we can drop that line. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Now, we blew Georgia that run-off last time by splitting the party there. We can never let that happen again. \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  needs to win this. Now while the late vote really does appear to have broken toward Republicans. You can see this in the exit polls and the vote count for Election Day. The Democrats appear to have done very well at getting a lot of votes before Election Day.\par \par \uc2 So look if everyone had voted yesterday, we might have seen the Red Wave that was being picked up in some of the polls, but we don't have Election Day anymore. It's more like election month. And that means that going forward, the GOP cannot count from on this coming from behind strategy in States like New York, or Virginia or Michigan or even Pennsylvania. The Democrats are going to be ready to start turning out their voters on the first day of early voting. OK and Republicans going forward are going to have to do the same.\par \par \uc2 Now, look, they did this in Miami-Dade County. And that was fantastic. We got a lot of Republicans voting early in Miami-Dade. But the old turnout models just don't work anymore. They just don't. Also you need to be in the lead, frankly, on Labor Day going forward. The GOP should act as if laid basically Election Day comes five weeks early, they should just pretend that it does. Because if they're five points behind in late September, the Democrats are just going to bank a huge amount of votes against them. And even if some of those folks change their mind later, it's going to be too late.\par \par \uc2 So going into 2024, the Republicans are going to be looking for candidates who are focused on winning, not just making a point, or settling a score. So to really change the country, we're going to have to win. And we have to win over voters outside our traditional base that means young people to, that's got to be the goal for the next presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The populist movement is about ideas. It is not about any one person. If the voters conclude that you're putting your own ego or your own grudges ahead of what's 