os family and former President Trump has been there. If she wins this race it will be a bright spot for Democrats, not only the fact that she won but the way she won, I'm talking about economic issues, and she could catapult herself into the conversation if, indeed, President Biden does not run in 24, even in 28 when we know he won't run.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Your governor's race was Georgia? We got a sneak peak of that.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Governor's race is Georgia. We're going to watch --\par \par \uc2 FORD: I'm sorry. Did I go?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Kemp is up by about five points right now in the latest polling that we are seeing on this race. And \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  is making the argument that black men in Georgia have been fed misinformation in this race. So when you boil down what information is out there, you look at crime is up about four percent. They've got a higher inflation rate in Georgia than the rest of the country, it's at nine percent. So those are the numbers.\par \par \uc2 It's been fascinating to watch Governor Kemp kind of thread the needle in his own way and separate himself from former President Trump and still manage to be strong in this race. So perhaps if he does win by the kinds of numbers we are seeing, maybe he potentially pulls \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  up above 50, because the runoff it becomes a whole other question. But if he has got a big enough lead tomorrow night, that's something we will be watching, can he pull Walker.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: There are a number of races around the country that that could happen, where the governors could take the Senate candidate over.\par \par \uc2 Last thing, come Wednesday, depending on the runoff in December if that happens or not, we will likely stop talking about polls for a while. There have been so many polls.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: I mean, you start to hate polls.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: They can't all be right.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: No.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And so if it is a wave, we are looking at Republicans being undercounted in polls anywhere from two to five points. And that has happened in previous elections. If that happens, you are talking about races that tick down, to your point, Ben, across the country.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: It's a systemic problem, it's a huge problem, and it's one that we are going to continue to deal with. And I think there is going to be egg on a lot of the pollster's faces come Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, we're almost there. We're almost there. Tomorrow, we will have complete election coverage from here in New York. Martha and I will be tomorrow starting at 6:00 p.m. eastern time. We follow "THE FIVE," and it will be fun. Who knows what's going to happen? A lot could happen.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced, and still unafraid. "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME" starts right now. Hey, Jesse.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020221108eib700001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Razor Thin Margins in Key Senate Races\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Kellyanne Conway, Mike Huckabee, Ari Fleischer \par \uc2 10,779 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: All right. Election eve, Tucker. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 It's going to be an interesting day tomorrow. Welcome.\par \par \uc2 All right. It is officially here. The moment is upon us. Tomorrow is Election Day in America. And you will decide the balance of power in the Washington swamp.\par \par \uc2 At this hour, we are monitoring tonight's massive Trump rally and it's massive. It's in Ohio with J.D. Vance. There's expectations of a big announcement. We'll dip in live straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 Also, Dr. Oz will join us with his final thoughts from Pennsylvania. We'll bring you the latest polls from across the country.\par \par \uc2 Right now, five Senate races, more than two dozen House contests, three gubernatorial elections are all within two points. That is called a statistical tie. Now, as a reminder, three key swing states if you go back to 2016 propelled \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to victory in 2016. The combined vote of those three swing states, 70,000 votes, 2020, 43,000 votes in three states. That would be Georgia, Wisconsin and Arizona decided the election.\par \par \uc2 If you stay home, Democrats, well, they likely to win, and you'll get the government that you deserve. We are warning you. We warned you.\par \par \uc2 And this brings us to the most important question every American this election eve needs to be asking themselves. Are you better off -- are you better off than you were 21 months ago? Are you happy?\par \par \uc2 We have a 40-year record high of inflation. We have back breaking gas prices. Diesel prices and a diesel shortage. Are you happy about that? Is that -- is that the best we're capable of?\par \par \uc2 Are you happy that our borders are wide open? Four-point-five million illegal immigrants its estimated aided and abetted by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his policies, human trafficking, drug smuggling, record deaths of fentanyl and heroin. Are you happy with your children getting indoctrinated with critical race theory, radical gender theory, other woke ideologies while parents, by the way, you're told to sit down, shut up or you'll risk being investigated as a domestic terrorist?\par \par \uc2 Are you happy with zero bail laws in this country? In other words, violent criminal, bank robber, they get caught, let them out. No bail. Get caught again, let them out with to bail. Are you happy with lax prosecutions? Even from violent crimes. Are you happy with the spiking crime all over this country, in small towns and big cities?\par \par \uc2 If so, my advice you vote Democrat or state home. But if you're furious, if you think we're better as a country that we can be better as a country, if you're unhappy with the direction of this country, you have a chance tomorrow to let your voice be heard at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 So much is at stake. This is an inflection point, tipping point election. Any cliche you want to use, they're all appropriate. The current crop of Democratic candidates, I've been doing this since 1987 starting on radio. They're the most radical beyond radical that I've witnessed in my lifetime.\par \par \uc2 You have, for example, in Pennsylvania, that trust fund brat, this guy thinks it's Halloween all year around, in a hoodie, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . He dresses up like a working guy except he's never had a job in his life, a lifelong opponent of fracking. That's an $83 billion industry in Pennsylvania, the commonwealth. He's against all domestic energy production.\par \par \uc2 He's obsessed with letting first degree convicted murderers out of prison. Additionally, he wants to open up the prisons in Pennsylvania, led 1/3 to 1/2 of the prisoners walk out free. By the way, he's in favor of safe heroin injections sites. You live in the commonwealth of Pennsylvania, you get to pay for that.\par \par \uc2 He's for sanctuary states and cities. No limits at all on abortion, an hour before you're about to give birth, you can have an abortion.\par \par \uc2 During his reign as mayor of the tiny town of Braddock, population declined by 40 percent to only 1,700 people. That's his one job in life. In the meantime, crime and poverty skyrocketed.\par \par \uc2 Next up, look at Georgia. OK, you have \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 . Democrats there, you want to vote for Warnock? Let's see, he loves not God bless America, GD America, Jeremiah Wright. Loves \uc2 Louis Farrakhan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senator Warnock, a big fan of critical race theory, thinks the school should be teaching it, a proponent of defund, dismantle, no bail laws, all around the country. The guy that even calls the police gangsters and thugs.\par \par \uc2 Warnock praised \uc2 Fidel Castro\uc2 , a thug murderer, demanded that America repent for America's whiteness. He was previously accused of running over his wife -- his estranged wife's foot with a car after a domestic dispute.\par \par \uc2 He was also arrested after he was leading a church camp. Child abuse took place. And apparently, they found five varying cases that were in fact true. And he was arrested for obstructing justice. He now also collects a large paycheck as a pastor who supports no limits on abortion until the moment of birth.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in the great state of Wisconsin, there you have radical Mandela Barnes. He wants to cut the prison population fully in half, open up the prisons. Let everyone go free.\par \par \uc2 He wants all cash bail ended. He wants to defund the police and he once even praised the 2020 riots. Dozens of Americans died, thousands of cops injured.\par \par \uc2 In New Hampshire, you have \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 . She support as abolishing the legislative filibuster. She also voted against the Keystone XL pipeline, voted against new natural gas exploration and during her time as governor, she signed a 23 percent gas tax hike.\par \par \uc2 They're expecting in all of New England, including New Hampshire, that the possibility that the grid itself won't have enough natural gas to be powered and they'll have blackouts in New England this winter with a minimum 30 percent anticipated price increase to heat your home, whether you heat it by gas or oil, doesn't matter.\par \par \uc2 Out in Arizona, you have Democrat Mark Kelly. He's no moderate. He votes with Chucky and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  98 percent of the time. For example, he voted to hire 83,000 new \uc2 IRS\uc2  agents, voted against hiring 18,000 new Border Patrol agents. I wonder whose side he's on?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, he also voted to defund border wall construction three separate times, voted against deporting illegal immigrants during the pandemic. And then to top it off, he has big dreams of using Obamacare as a back door into a single-payer socialized healthcare system in America.\par \par \uc2 Arizona, you're a border state. Are you happy with Mr. Kelly?\par \par \uc2 Now, none of these far left candidates should be in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 . But tonight, in the spirit of fairness, I want to highlight the Democrats closing arguments to you, the American people, featuring a big new plan to combat inflation, Chef Boyardee, not kidding. Here's the Democratic congressional campaign chief, the guy that's in charge of helping elect Democrats, \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 . He's running himself. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGINVIDEO LCIP0\par \par \uc2 INTERVIEWER: Hudson Valley residents are feeling pain at the pump and at grocery stores. What have you done, and what do you plan to do to help solve our inflation problem?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 SEAN PATRICK MALONEY\uc2  (D-NY): Yeah. Well, I grew up in a family if the gas price went up, the