any new drilling.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: If you think energy costs are bad now, just wait until that plan takes effect. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  must be held in check. That's what tomorrow is about.\par \par \uc2 The good news for you tonight is the momentum important Republicans is palpable. Take a look at your screen. Look at that screen, massive outdoor Trump rally. That was the one in Pennsylvania with Dr. Oz. Absolutely packed. Compare that to the \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  rally, same day, same night. \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oh, half the place is empty. They had to hide the empty seats. While this is a great sign, it is the only thing that is going to matter is what happens tomorrow. Election Day in America.\par \par \uc2 So get to the polls or you'll get the government you deserve. It's that simple.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, FOX News contributor Kellyanne Conway, former governor of Arkansas, \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , and FOX News contributor \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne, we start with you. You're really good with numbers. So, when we go back to 2016, if we take the three swing states that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won, combined total votes, 70,000. That's not a lot. If you look at 2020 and you look at Arizona, Georgia, Wisconsin, you're talking about 43,000 votes, Kellyanne.\par \par \uc2 So when I look at the polls in Georgia and I look at the polls in New Hampshire, and Pennsylvania, and Nevada, Arizona, although a poll has Blake Masters up by three today, and I look at those polls, am I wrong in believing that probably every one of those races the power in the Senate will be determined by tens of thousands of votes and not hundreds of thousands?\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes, Sean. You're right. That's the way the elections have been going and that's why these are called swing states. They literally sit on the razor's edge. It depends on turnout a