ood to see you, Governor.\par \par \uc2 I know you've been all over the country campaigning especially for -- especially for gubernatorial candidates. What do you feel on the ground? Often you get a feeling on the ground. I've been out on the campaign trail when I felt no energy and when I felt a lot of energy. There's a discernible difference.\par \par \uc2 GOV. GLENN YOUNGKIN (R), VIRGINIA: Yeah, Sean. The momentum is huge. Everywhere that I have had the great privilege of campaigning, the momentum has been giant.\par \par \uc2 And listen, this red wave that found its head waters in the Commonwealth of Virginia last year has grown in momentum. Tonight, we had an amazing rally for Jen Kiggans in the second district.\par \par \uc2 We had the future Speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy with us. We had 50th speaker \uc2 Newt Gingrich\uc2  with us. The crowd was huge.\par \par \uc2 Folks can feel this happening. And it's time. It's time for change. Americans have been hurting, Virginians have been hurting. They've seen the damage that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has done to our nation, and they're going to show up and make a statement.\par \par \uc2 I hope that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  answers this wake-up call because there's going to be a loud one. But, Sean, we've got to do the work. Tomorrow is the day to get out and vote. Get ten friends, get to the polls and do the work. Let's win this.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Governor, stay right there. We're going to come back.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance has taken the stage in Ohio with President Trump -- former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 JD VANCE (R), OHIO U.S. SENATE CANDIDATE: -- people who are going to fight for the issues and actually get something done for the people of Ohio. That's what I'm going to do. Let's get out to the polls tomorrow. Thank you all.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you, JD. You're going to win big. We have to send a signal to these people that are ruining our country. They're destroying our country.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, you also need to get out and vote and re-elect Governor \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2  and your lieutenant governor, John Husted. You've got to do that. He's done a good job. He's done a good job.\par \par \uc2 Mike and John have been an outstanding team who have fought tirelessly to bring jobs and factories back to Ohio. I worked with them on doing that, including $20 billion Intel plant that will create more than 20,000 Ohio jobs and they cut taxes, slash regulations and they delivered historic funding for support and for the police officers. And they have really done a job.\par \par \uc2 Mike and John are running against a radical left lunatic who was a disaster as a major of Dayton. I've got to know her when we had a terrible shooting here. Remember, I went to the hospital. I got to know her. And I said --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. President Trump with J.D. Vance in Ohio. Massive crowd. Final rally of the midterms this year.\par \par \uc2 We go back to Governor Glenn Youngkin.\par \par \uc2 You know, Governor, you ran in a state that many argued for years that was purple but was really a blue state. You didn't just win, you won by a significant margin.\par \par \uc2 The issues that were very prevalent in your race, everything from education to law and order and safety and security and not defunding the police or no bail laws, the issues of the economy and inflation and record gas prices, they seem to be resonating all around the country.\par \par \uc2 You know, with that said, as you look at these very close races, as we look at Pennsylvania and Georgia and New Hampshire and Arizona and Nevada, what do you see happening?\par \par \uc2 YOUNGKIN: Sean, Americans are hurting. And when they sit around their kitchen tables at that night, that's what they're talking about. The silent peeve of inflation stealing their hard-earned money, the undermining of their schools, the demeaning of law enforcement. And, oh, by the way, a crisis at the border that has made every state a border state.\par \par \uc2 So Republicans have answers. They've seen Republican governors lead. They have seen our congressmen and senators want to make change and be held back. And tomorrow is going to be a loud wake-up call.\par \par \uc2 We've got to do the work. Boy, Americans are ready to lock arms. And, Sean, the amazing thing is it's not just Republicans against Democrats. But it's Americans that will stand up and make a statement about our future.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, the reality is, I don't think -- the Democratic Party in the past that I knew, governor, they used to hide their real opinions. It was interesting when you were running against \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2 , he was part of the Clinton administration. Very close to the Clintons.\par \par \uc2 Yet he made these outrageous comments about parents need to stay out of the classroom. You were saying excuse me. Parents have every right to know what's going on in the classroom.\par \par \uc2 And what's fascinating, things that Democrats would never say years ago, they are now openly advocating. Defund the police. Dismantle the police. No bail laws.\par \par \uc2 They're proud of wide open borders. They have no problem speaking out and saying, no, we don't need to be energy independent at all. Oh, and you need to go buy an electric car, which is only $22,000 more than a gas powered car and by the way, it's powered by an electric grid that is 90 percent fossil fuels.\par \par \uc2 All of these issues now seem to be resonating around the country. Do you see the Democratic Party, if in fact this is a bad day for them today, do you see any hope of any change? \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  once said the era of big government is over, the end of welfare as we know. I don't see that in this party. I don't see moderate voices out there.\par \par \uc2 YOUNGKIN: Well, I -- I hope that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hears this loud wake-up call that is coming tomorrow. Listen, we have not seen any Democrat candidates profess anything close to common sense. You hit it right on the nose.\par \par \uc2 We've got inflation, stealing everybody's hard earned money. They've undermined our schools. They've demeaned law enforcements. We have a wide open border.\par \par \uc2 These are straightforward to go at and fix. They have done nothing. That's why there's going to be a sea change tomorrow. And you know what, Sean, in Virginia, we've got three amazing congressional candidates, Jen Kiggans, Yesli Vega, Hung Cao.\par \par \uc2 We're going to make a big statement that Virginia is going to continue the red wave that we started last year. This reflects the needs of Virginians and Americans. It's going to make a big statement today.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We'll get the early races of Virginia. They could be indicative of what's going to happen the rest of the night.\par \par \uc2 Governor Youngkin, thank you.\par \par \uc2 We had back to the great state of Ohio. President Trump with his rally for JD Vance, it's expected the president will make a big announcement tonight.\par \par \uc2 My sources are telling me that he has come to a decision. Will he give that decision tonight? There's conflicting reports. We'll see.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : The best in the whole country. Best wrestler.\par \par \uc2 But I look at it and I looked at those years. I shouldn't say this. I said they guy had some things going on with the fighting stuff. But he is such a warrior. Is he here? Is he here?\par \par \uc2 Come here. I love this guy.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 Come here. Say something.\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN (R-OH): They've heard from me, Mr. President. But they want you back here. I'll just say this. My favorite scripture verse is second Timothy 4:7.\par \par \uc2 It says: Fight the good fight, finish the course, keep the faith.\par \par \uc2 And I tell folks, I tell folks, that's a verse for our country -- fight, finish, keep. Words of action. Not timid works, not sissy words. Words that we associate with America and words that we associate with the best president we've ever had, President Trump.\par \par \uc2 God bless you all.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : Thank you, Jim, very much. A friend of Jim's, a friend of all of us, Warren, Davidson Warren. Good job you're doing.\par \par \uc2 Mike Kerry and a person who -- where is Mike? Good job, mike. Warrior.\par \par \uc2 Another warrior, a person who is very shy, very timid, we're trying to get her tougher. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 . She's terrific.\par \par \uc2 She did a commercial. Yes, yes, something can break into my house. We'll treat her nicely. But, first, she's got to go through this. I said that's a hell of a commercial. But she's great. She's done a tremendous job.\par \par \uc2 She's highly respected, highly respected. She just won with almost like everybody voted for her. She's great. Thanks very much, Marjorie.\par \par \uc2 Congressional candidates, oh, I love this guy. Max Miller. Where is Max? Where is Max?\par \par \uc2 I'll tell you, the job he's done, right? He was with me for four years. I know him maybe almost as well as this guy right there, Jim.\par \par \uc2 But Max is going to be a great congressman. Turn out to be an incredible campaigner. Had a hard time with the district. It kept getting worse and worse. They got to a Trump plus 20, a Trump plus 10, then it was a Trump plus 2. They kept playing.\par \par \uc2 And kept saying, said don't worry about it, sir. I'm going to win anyway. Doesn't matter. And it went to other way. He said don't worry about it.\par \par \uc2 In the end, it became like a Trump plus 18. I don't know how the hell you pulled that off. But you know what? You did a great job for me, Max. And I'm here for you and you're going to have a great career. Young man and a great man. Grew up right here. Thank you very much, Max.\par \par \uc2 And, J.R. Majewski, he suffered a lot of false -- false statements. And I just want to tell you, everyone knows -- all of the people I just named. But they have my complete and total endorsement. You know that. They treated J.R. very unfairly.\par \par \uc2 They made up a lot of stories. He is a tremendous warrior and a great gentleman and I think he's going to do very well tomorrow. I think you got treated very unfairly. I don't know what's going to happen.\par \par \uc2 The fake news went after him and we don't know what will happen. I think you're doing to have a good result. The people know that you are a legitimate hero. You know who told me that? Jim Jordan. That's all I have to hear. When Jim says it.\par \par \uc2 So good luck tomorrow, fellows. Good luck tomorrow. Ohio Republican Party chairman, Bob --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. That is president Trump. He's stumps his last campaign rally in this midterm election cycle. Obviously it's election night in America. Tomorrow, election day.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, our friends, our pollsters, Matt Towery, Insider Advantage, and Robert Cahaly, Trafalgar. They have been polling every race.\par \par \uc2 All right, guys. This is your final opportunity. We're going to be go through especially the Senate races. A lot of these gubernatorial races. Let's start in the great state of Georgia. Both of you have \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  in the lead.\par \par \uc2 Robert Cahaly, what's going to happen tomorrow?\par \par \uc2 ROBERT CAHALY, TRAFALGAR: I think Herschel is going to come in first and I think he's going to get it barely and avoid a run-off.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. So, you think it's a run-off on December 6. And in that --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What's that? Oh, you think without a runoff.\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: I think he avoids it.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wow, that would a change for -- that would be a big night for Republicans if that happens.\par \par \uc2 Matt Towery, do you agree?\par \par \uc2 MATT TOWERY, INSIDER ADVANTAGE: Well, I have to tell you, I'm increasingly convinced that Robert is the best pollster on this. I think \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  will make it across the 50 percent plus one, partly because African American men will vote for Walker at an even higher level than they have told us in the polls.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What about -- you can't deny \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  has run a great campaign for governor.\par \par \uc2 TOWERY: Oh, yeah. He's lifting all boats in Georgia. He's going to absolutely -- he will have a big night. Let's puts it that way over \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 . Yes, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  will add to \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 's likelihood of making it without a run off.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Let's go to this great state of North Carolina and \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 . Where do you see that race, Matt Towery?\par \par \uc2 TOWERY: Budd. That's easy.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK, easy.\par \par \uc2 Robert, agreement?\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: Yes. Budd comfortably.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. Let's go to New Hampshire. A poll came out today had General Bolduc up by one. You have a governor in \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  that is leading anywhere from 12 to 18 points in some polls. Is that going to help General Bolduc who also had a good debate I thought against \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 ? Where is that state going, Matt Towery?\par \par \uc2 TOWERY: Well, it's very close. You know, they don't have that early voting. They don't have a lot of noise before the actual election. He's been rising the entire time.\par \par \uc2 The British betting houses say he's not going to win. I say he has a chance of winning. It will be close. Robert thinks I think that it's probably going to be closer.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What do you think Robert?\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: Yeah, I think just exactly what you said. He had a great debate. He has Governor Sununu behind him. That's a big move. The governor has done a bunch of town halls and \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  sat in the basement. So, I think in the end, he pulls it out. I said Bolduc wins this thing.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know what? You look at General Bolduc. He's not a polished politician. He's been a general. He did ten tours of duty, two Purple Hearts, five Bronze Stars. He's in it to serve the people of the Granite State, New Hampshire. He would be a great choice. I hope he pulls this out.\par \par \uc2 Let's go to the state of Pennsylvania. We paid a lot of attention to this race. You have I think in \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the most extreme candidate ever to run for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 . It's still relatively close.\par \par \uc2 Your take, Robert.\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: I think in the end, Oz is going to get the most votes. I think Mastriano outperforms all of his polling and makes that a little more competitive than anybody gives him credit for. But what happens after Pennsylvania drags it out a week is anybody's guess.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: He gets the most votes. That sounds like code words, but I'm not going there.\par \par \uc2 Matt?\par \par \uc2 TOWERY: OK. Well, I alluded a moment ago to the British odds makers that tend to be the very best at figuring out American politics. Go figure. And they have moved this race to favor Oz winning. So has \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2 , who's known to have a pretty good crystal ball. Our poll in Philadelphia had Oz up by several points.\par \par \uc2 I think Oz will win the race. It's going to be tight and I agree with Robert. He will get the most votes. We'll see what happens.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I will argue that \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , if you're in Pennsylvania, you can't let that happen in this country.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's look at JD Vance and let's also look at Ron Johnson. Any issues there for either of you?\par \par \uc2 TOWERY: None.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: None.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Let's go to the state of Arizona. Blake Masters. Robert, you had him up by three today.\par \par \uc2 CAHALY: Actually, our brand new poll has him up by one. That's the first poll that we've put out with Masters winning. What we've seen happen is what we expected. Once this libertarian got out, looks like Masters is --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: We're going to dip back in to the Ohio rally with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He's with JD Vance. Let's listen in.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : We will end visa lottery and end illegal immigration in our country once and for all. We want people to come in but they have to come in legally. Have to come in legally.\par \par \uc2 We will stop the crime wave in Democrat-run cities. We will give our police the power they need and the respect that they deserve. We will not take legal protection away from our police.\par \par \uc2 They want to take protection so that if somebody sues a police person for doing their job, they have to go out and hire their own lawyer. That's not a good idea.\par \par \uc2 We will restore law and order in America. We will hold China accountable for unleashing the virus upon the world, $65 trillion in damage. They can't pay that much. But something is going to happen.\par \par \uc2 We will abolish all COVID mandates and lockdowns and rehire every patriot that was fired from the military with an apology and fullback pay.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 And we will defend our Constitution, we will defend the Second Amendment that we will proudly uphold, the Judeo-Christian values and principles of our nation's founding.\par \par \uc2 We will restore patriotic education to our schools and we will teach our children to love their country, honor our history and to always respect our great American flag. Always respect our flag.\par \par \uc2 In conclusion, our MAGA movement, make America great again, is by far the greatest political movement in the history of our country. They never challenge that. They have never challenged that. It's an amazing thing.\par \par \uc2 They wouldn't challenge it. If I said anything slightly wrong they would challenge it. But they can't challenge that.\par \par \uc2 Together, we are standing up against some of the most menacing forces, entrenched interests and vicious opponents our people have ever seen. Despite great outside dangers, our biggest threat remains the sick, sinister and evil people from within our country. You know who I'm talking about. You see them all the time.\par \par \uc2 But no matter how big or powerful the corrupt radical left Democrats that we're fighting against may be, you must never get this nation does not belong to them. This nation belongs to you. That's who it belongs to.\par \par \uc2 This is your home. This is your heritage. And our American liberty is your God-given right.\par \par \uc2 From Akron to Toledo, from Cleveland to Columbus, from Youngstown to Dayton, you inherit the legacy of generations of Americans that risk their everything for the beloved country that they love so much. Ohio is the state that gave us American heroes, icons and legends with names like Neil Armstrong, Annie Oakley and the great general and President Ulysses S. Grant.\par \par \uc2 And this is the state that gave us legions of farmers, soldiers, steel workers and skilled craftsmen who built this country with the sweat of their brows and the strength of their spines and they suffered so greatly. But they also gave us something very, very special, the goodness of their souls. Your Ohio ancestors broke the barriers, they conquered the unknown dangers, they pushed into unchartered frontiers and they made America into the greatest nation in the history of the world.\par \par \uc2 But now, we are a nation in decline. We are a failing nation. We are a nation that has the highest inflation in 50 years, and where the stock market finished the worst first half of the year since 1872.\par \par \uc2 Likewise, we are a nation that has the highest energy costs in its history. We are no longer energy independent or