er 31st, there have been 281 officers shot this year. 55 of them were killed.\par \par \uc2 The organization's president issued a statement saying, in part, "We are experiencing a real crisis with the level of violence directed at law enforcement officers. Frankly, it is unlike anything I've seen in my 36 years of law enforcement. Many will often look at this data and just see numbers. We must remember that they represent heroes, fathers, mothers, sons, and daughters."\par \par \uc2 "BREAKING TONIGHT", it appears \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is about to get another shot at the prime minister job in Israel, despite being on trial for corruption there.\par \par \uc2 Preliminary indications suggest voters in Israel may elect their most right-leaning government yet. Correspondent Trey Yingst is in Jerusalem tonight.\par \par \uc2 TREY YINGST, FOX NEWS CHANNEL FOREIGN CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): After the fifth round of Israeli elections in less than four years, former Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is poised to take power once again after failing to form a government last year.\par \par \uc2 Exit polls show the opposition leader has at least the 61 seats needed to control the Israeli parliament in Jerusalem, known as the Knesset.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BENJAMIN NETANYAHU\uc2 , PRIME MINISTER, ISRAEL (THROUGH TRANSLATOR): If indeed the real election results reflect the exit polls, I will establish a nationalist government that can see all Israeli citizens without any exceptions to all.\par \par \uc2 YINGST: Once formal results are announced later this week, Netanyahu is expected to receive a mandate from Israeli President \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2 , who then have 28 days to form a coalition government that is expected to be one of the most conservative in the history of the Jewish state.\par \par \uc2 Current Prime Minister \uc2 Yair Lapid\uc2  spoke overnight, encouraging his supporters to wait for the final results, since they could be 