t I think we need to be paying attention to.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So you're a student, Ohio State, how much do you think, to mention social issues, the issue of abortion affects things for you and for this state?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: For me, personally, I think that it affects me greatly. I am a pro choice woman in the state of Ohio, and it is a right that I think I will probably never need to take advantage of but it's a right that all women should be able to have Ohio. And it is a right that I think I will probably never need to take advantage of, but it's a right that all women should be able to have the choice to be able to make.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So it's driving your vote or factor in your vote?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It certainly is. And there are several other factors, I think, but abortion is definitely one that'll drive it.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So right now, I believe in Ohio, abortion is legal, up to 22 weeks. So, does anyone think that that will change? Go ahead in the back, sir. Is it Joe? Joe, sorry.\par \par \uc2 BJORKMAN: I mean, you look at, you know, they passed the heartbeat bill a while ago, and it got struck down, or they weren't enforcing it or whatever. And then they put it into action. And then I think one of the judges in Cincinnati struck that down but it's only temporary.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Drew, did you want to -- you raise your hand?\par \par \uc2 DREW, OHIO VOTER: Oh. That it does affect us, that it's going to change. Yes, I think so. JD Vance has said that he does not believe in the reproductive rights for women. And -- I'm sorry --\par \par \uc2 BAIER: No, go ahead.\par \par \uc2 DREW: And \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  has I think he believes that women -- reproductive decision should be between a woman and their doctor. And I think Ohio is heading in a direction where they're going to ban abortion completely.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Jeff?\par \par \uc2 JEFF, OHIO VOTER: I don't think it's a factor in this race to 