asing half the prison population like your opponent would like to do.\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: And, Sean, Mandela Barnes says the founding of this nation awful. And of course, President \uc2 Obama\uc2  and President Biden, as Candace said, they wanted to fundamentally transform America. And I ask audience, do you even like or just love something you want to fundamentally transform? Of course not.\par \par \uc2 So you have the leaders of the Democrat Party don't particularly like America, Mandela Barnes compared racism down South to racism in Wisconsin and said, we even does (ph) -- we've institutionalized it. He says we concealed. He called it concealed carry racism.\par \par \uc2 Why does he want to represent a bunch of Wisconsinites he views are systemically racist? So, no, the leaders of Democrat Party don't particularly like this country. So I'm asking Democrats, independents in Wisconsin, if you love this country, I think most do, if you're concerned about our future, join us. Join us in healing and unifying and saving this country because that's what's at stake.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Three critical races. We got Georgia, we got Pennsylvania, we got Wisconsin. Senator, thanks for being with us.\par \par \uc2 All right. Straight ahead tonight, "The View" used children as political pawns on their Halloween show today. We're going to play you a pretty disturbing video. That's straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Earlier today on that hard-hitting news show on "The View" on ABC, the hosts decided to use there Halloween segments is a way to use kids in political ponds in to attack \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: (INADUIBLE) He flush them down the toilet so we have Trump as a toilet with our \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents.\par \par \uc2 Now, we don't want to endorse violence of any kind, but we couldn't help, but talk about one of the hottest hot topics this year. So, we have our interpretation. We have an Oscar statue. We call this the Oscar slap because of the red face paint on the statue.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Joining us now, \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2  with "The Epoch Times" and along with "Outnumbered" co-host \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I'm not going to act offended because I'm not offended. I don't really care what they do in "The View". I would assume the parents of these kids participated gave their full approval. \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 KAYLEIGH MCENANY\uc2 , OUTNUMBERED CO-HOST: Yeah, look, I'm with you. I don't really care either, but what I will say is this, imagine if your life obsession is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is the Republican Party. They also had a costume that mocked Dr. Oz.\par \par \uc2 I mean, I was on the streets with my daughter. She was a princess. I saw firefighters, I saw fairies, I saw all kinds of cute little kids. I didn't see agency one of them dressed as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . I didn't see one of them dressed as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . These were kids having fun.\par \par \uc2 These women on "The View", I mean, their life obsession is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and it must be very painful way to live when you got to even dress kids up as such.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, for years, Larry, I would do a bit on the radio where I would say Halloween is bad because you're teaching kids to be liberal because you're telling them to knock on people 's door and get something for free. It was a bit, it was a joke, I was kidding around.\par \par \uc2 And people would go nuts saying Hannity is calling Halloween liberal. It's like no, you're just too stupid to be in on the joke.\par \par \uc2 These things don't offend me, but they do often liberals, don't they? If you had a scary mask of \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  or any other Democrats, that's sexist, that's racist, that's homophobic. They would make up something.\par \par \uc2 LARRY ELDER\uc2 , RADIO TALK SHOW HOST: Well, Sean, first of all, you should get me stressed pay for making me want to see segments of "The View". Now, earlier, you had Ron Johnson on and talking about \uc2 Obama\uc2  and he said what is he so angry? Every time I watched watch "The View", I have the same reaction. Why are these ladies led by Whoopi Goldberg so angry?\par \par \uc2 At one time, you might remember years ago, Whoopi Goldberg was the highest- paid actress in Hollywood. She has a multimillion dollar job sitting their every day trashing conservatives and this is a woman who was briefly on welfare . She should be doing handstands about how great America is.\par \par \uc2 Instead she is incredibly angry. I felt the same way about \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . He claimed he and his mom were on welfare raised by a single mom, raised by his maternal grandparents, goes to Harvard, becomes the president -- the first Black president of the "Harvard Law Review", then runs for senator, gets elected.\par \par \uc2 He spent eight years basically telling White people you're oppressors and Black people you are a victim, while living right now in $12 million mansion in Martha's Vineyard. You can't make this up.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And yet, 30 acres and here we have 50 people who those 50 people and 15 of the 30 acres were there illegally and Martha's Vineyard.\par \par \uc2 Paul Pelosi, let me ask you, \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2 , as I look at this case, and look at the Democrats' reaction. Where is the same anger and outrage over everybody that is a victim of violence in every big city run by liberal Democrats for decades?\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: That is a great question. You know, I fielded so many questions about violence at the podium. Of course, we condemn violence whether it was Paul Pelosi or anybody else where there were never questions when it went the other way. There were questions about the dozens of people who lost their lives and the riots.\par \par \uc2 And there is a rush to try Paul Pelosi to a political angle, but when we see violence go the other way there are many such examples, where was the president of the United States when there was an assassination attempt on Justice Kavanaugh? Spokespeople spoke, but he did not speak. That would have been untenable position in a Trump White House.\par \par \uc2 But because we have a press that simply doesn't care, they get away with doing that and not condemning the violence.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. By the way, taking your daughter to go trick or treating , not a good idea. I'm kidding.\par \par \uc2 More HANNITY next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for joining us. Please set your DVR so you never miss an episode of HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, I've got great news. Let not your heart be troubled, Laura Ingraham, this is a spooky Halloween edition of "THE INGRAHAM ANGLE."\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020221101eiav00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Paul Pelosi Was Attacked By A Drugged Up Lunatic; Left Sees Attack As Opportunity To Stifle Political Opposition; Political Violence From The Left Is Always Minimized; A Berkeley Nudist Is Supposed To Represent The GOP?; Left's Historical Ignorance On Full Display; Dems Can't Process Their Impending Losses; Abortion And Jan 6TH Won't Do It For Dems; Michigan Republican Gubernatorial Candidate Tudor Dixon Interviewed On Closing Days Of Campaign Against Incumbent Democratic Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 ; "The View" Displays Children In Political Halloween Costumes; Former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  Campaigns For Democratic Candidates For Upcoming Midterm Elections\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Miranda Devine \par \uc2 7,063 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Please set your DVR, so you've never ever, ever miss an episode of Hannity. In the meantime, I've got great news. Let not your heart be troubled Laura Ingraham. This is a spooky Halloween edition of THE INGRAHAM ANGLE. Well.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: My kids wanted me to go in costume, and I said I am in costume. OK, I'm a conservative television host. OK. I think, do you like to see costumes? I have a question. Do you like the really scary costumes? Because at the end of my show, I'm going to show what my kids wore tonight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And I wasn't really in favor of it. But this is what they wanted to do. Boys want to you know they want to wear this scary things. I was terrifying.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know what; I am all in favor of letting kids be themselves. And even if it means they can be a little politically correct. Remember back in the day, they used to have the Nixon mask, and that was a big deal. And then a Reagan mask and every President since has had a mask. I guess you can't do that anymore.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well. No, I like being remembered. We were just bombs because we didn't have any money to get a costume. So we were just bum.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That was, every year I was a bum. I haven't changed.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now you can't even say bum anymore. That's how bad it is. Alright--\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: That's true. We probably gone through. So we're in trouble.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'll send you the photo, in case you're not up.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, I want to see it. Send it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, I see you tomorrow. I'm Laura Ingraham, this is THE INGRAHAM ANGLE from Washington tonight. 'Smears From The Thought Police', that is the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Now just as we expected, almost within minutes of the horrific and terrifying attack on Paul Pelosi, Democrats saw a political opportunity. Now this couldn't be seen as simply a reprehensible assault by a fringe lunatic on an elderly man, it had to be portrayed as a referendum on the entire Republican Party, and then as a justification to limit political speech. We address these in reverse order.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. RO KHANNA (D-CA): The reality is this was an individual who was radicalized; he was radicalized to commit an act of political violence. And we have to ask, why was he radicalized? Why are we in American democracy feeding these outlandish conspiracy theories? Why are they festering on social media? And we all need to take accountability, the social media companies, the role of some of the media and certainly elected officials and people in the Republican Party who've been fueling some of these conspiracies.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh Ro, these types of baseless defamatory statements, they were echoed all weekend long. Now notice the would be speech Police they never name names because they can. Now 