he knows the Democrats don't have a winning agenda, or even a single solution to help fight inflation or crime, which is what most voters actually care about. So he resorts to two messages. The first, just trust us because the establishment will take care of you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: The only way to save democracy is if we together nurture it and fight for it, and that starts with electing people who know you and see you and care about you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ," the CIA, the plutocrats on Wall Street, Silicon Valley billionaires who show up at Davos, these are the people that he thinks should make policy and who care about us? If you trust them, if you do what they tell you, if the make the sacrifices they demand that you make, yes, things won't be all that great, but at least you're going to have done the right thing according to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His second message when he descended from Mount Martha's Vineyard was mistrust everyone who criticizes the establishment.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: Just about every Republican politician is obsessed with just two things -- own the libs and getting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's approval.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He thinks if you're one of those people who criticizes the establishment, well, you're probably a racist, a sexist, and a homophobe. He's always punching down, all appealing to snobbery, always defending the establishment and the status quo. It has made him really rich, after all. He had eight years to reform the system, but he never wanted to do it. He likes it, and he thinks everyone should like it.\par \par \uc2 Aren't we tired of all this by now? We have real policies that are working all over America, and the real politicians who are willing to fight for the average person even if that means taking on "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ." We should be listening to them, not watching Obama's nostalgia tour from the days when Americans actually trusted that system.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Charles Hurt, "Washington Times" opinion editor and FOX News contributor. Charlie, I think they think that magic of Obama somehow can help them limp across the finish line next Tuesday. You're thoughts tonight?\par \par \uc2 CHARLES HURT, OPINION EDITOR, "THE WASHINGTON TIMES": I guess, you know, they think, and they're probably right about this, the magic of Obama is certainly better than the alternative, that being \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , which is a total disaster. But the other thing watching these clips that I'm reminded of is that Trump revolution has just begun, and this guy doesn't realize that.\par \par \uc2 Remember in 2008, this guy ran on a platform of changing government, changing politics. And as you point out, he slid into the hot tub in Washington, and he never did thing to change all of it. And he just became a useful idiot, and he served the government, he served the people that were in charge exactly as they wanted him to. And it was because of that service to those people that opened the way for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to come along and absolutely destroy the place and do what this guy was too scared, or possibly too dumb to figure out how to do himself.\par \par \uc2 And let's not forget, listening to him lecture people is a nice reminder, under the eight years he was president, Democrats lost over 1,000 seats across this country. Obama got himself reelected, but Democrats lost over 1,000 seats because the American people were tired of what he was peddling, and they no longer believed him. But he opened the way for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jay-Z and Beyonce came to the White House, I guess that was nice. And they had the cast of "Hamilton" come to the White House, that was kind of fun. But for the regular people, it was just kind of, OK, what about us.\par \par \uc2 Charlie, I have to play some of the blather from the fawning media about this. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: President Obama remains a star for many Democrats. It's always, of course, a danger to speak in a rally where President Obama is speaking if you're not as talented an orator as he is.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN MARTIN, CNN POLITICAL ANALYST: The fact is that Obama has gifts that most politicians don't.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Obama is a really gifted orator. And I think sometimes we forget how gifted he is.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Charlie, have you forgotten how gifted he is. Remember when he came out of the surf in Hawaii with the glistening pectoralis muscles. Remember that guy Eli Saslow wrote that in "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yes, it's amazing. I swear, these people, they just talk to themselves, they talk to one another. They don't talk to normal people. Under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , people suffered, and they suffered in really profound ways, which is what opened the way for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to pick off all of those Democrats, actual voters.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Charlie, Charlie, thank you.\par \par \uc2 And when we come back, a creepy reveal from the Ingraham house.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I hope you all had a happy Halloween, especially those with little kids. Here are my boys, Niko and Dima. I don't know what they are. What are they, Jason? I don't know what that is. Myers, I always get them confused. Michael Myers, Sam says. Here's our senior executive producer Tommy Firth's kids, Poppy (ph), Wonder Woman -- oh, my God, they're so cute, I can't stand it. Tierney (ph) Catwoman, little Tommy (ph) as Spiderman. Is he angry? Here in Sam Fox's son Teddy (ph) as Frankenstein. OK, that is great. But he decided that wasn't scary enough. He changed into this mask to go trick-or-treating with his cousin Julio (ph).\par \par \uc2 OK, that's it for us tonight. Isn't that great? Come on, you can't do that forever, but I'm still dressing up a little right now. Thanks for watching. "GUTFELD!" and the gang, they take it all from here. Happy Halloween.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020221101eiav00001\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd